hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"33067","(33067) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, saying: Saad bin Ibrahim narrated to us that he had been informed that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: People are followers of Quraysh. They are pious to pious ones, and the ungodly among them is for the ungodly among them."
"33068","(33068) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr informed us, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best women who rode camels were the women of Quraysh. They were kind to him when he was young. And he took care of him over Baal in the same hand. (Ahmed 502)"
"33069","(33069) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Rashid told us, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The best of the women who rode camels were the women of Quraysh. They were kind to him when he was young, and they took care of him when he was a husband. Oh my God, if I had known that Maryam, the daughter of Imran, rode a camel, I would not have preferred anyone over her. (Ibn Saad 152)"
"33070","(33070) Abd bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He was the best of the women who rode camels, and the best of the women of Quraysh. He took care of him with a husband of his own, and was kind to him with a son when he was young."
"33071","(33071) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do not curse my companions, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if one of you spent as much gold as anyone The mudd of one of them reaches you, and there is no half of it. (Muslim 1967. Ibn Hibban 6994)"
"33072","(33072) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said To his companions: You are to people like salt is to food. He said: Then Al-Hasan said: Food is not flavorful except with salt. Then Al-Hasan says: How about a people whose salt has gone? (Abu Ali 2754; Abd al-Razzaq 20377)"
"33073","(33073) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Mujma’ bin Yahya, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burda, on the authority of Abi Burda, On the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: His companions are safe for my nation, so if his companions go, he will come. My nation is not promised.\n(Muslim 1961; Ahmad 399)"
"33074","(33074) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The best of my nation is the generation who follow me, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose testimony precedes the right of one of them, and the testimony of his right precedes his right. (Bukhari 2452, Muslim 1962)"
"33075","(33075) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ja’ad bin Hubaira, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The best of people are my kin, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then the last. \n(Tabarani 2188, Hakim 191)"
"33076","(33076) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Bahi, on the authority of Aisha, she said: A man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Which of people is the best? He said: The century I am in, then the second, then the third. (Muslim) 1965)"
"33077","(33077) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, he said: Hilal bin Yasaf told us, he said: I heard Imran bin Husayn say : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then Those who color them. (Tirmidhi 2221 and Ibn Hibban 7229)"
"33078","(33078) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Jamra, he said: Zahudum bin Mudharib narrated to me, he said: I heard Imran bin Husayn narrates that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say: The best of you are my generation, then those after them. Then those who are similar to them. He said: I do not know. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said after his generation twice, or three times.\n(Muslim 1964. Tabarani 582)"
"33079","(33079) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Qubaisi bin Jabir, who said: Omar addressed us at the tax collector’s door and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us as he stood among you. Then he said: O people: fear God regarding my companions, then those who are like them, then those who are like them, then spread lies And false witness.\n(Ibn Majah 2362. Tabarani 245)"
"33080","(33080) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Khaythama, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The best people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then a people who will come. Their testimony precedes their faith, and their faith precedes their testimony. (Ahmad 2761 Bazzar 2767)"
"33081","(33081) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin His master, he said: I was walking with Buraida al-Aslami, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Good. This nation is the generation into which I was sent, then those who will follow them, then those who will follow them, then those Color them, then there will be among them a people whose testimony precedes their oaths and whose oaths precede their testimony. (احمد ۳۵۰)"
"33082","(33082) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nasir ibn Dhu’luq, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Do not curse your companions. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so an hour’s work for one of you is better than the work of one of you in a lifetime."
"33083","(33083) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then there will come a people They are given testimony before they are asked for it."
"33084","(33084) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Ala’ Abu Al-Zubr Al-Dimashqi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Dimashqi narrated to us, saying: Amer, on the authority of Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You will not continue to be well as long as there is someone among you. He saw me and accompanied me. By God, you will still be fine, as long as there is someone among you who saw someone who saw me, and accompanied someone who accompanied me. By God, you will continue to be well, as long as there are those among you who have seen those who have seen me, and have accompanied those who have accompanied those who have accompanied me.\n(Tabarani 207)"
"33085","(33085) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: They were commanded to seek forgiveness for the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, so they took them captive."
"33086","(33086) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Khalid, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who Cursing my companions, may God curse him. (Ahmad 1733)"
"33087","(33087) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, he said: I was standing with Al-Sha’bi one day, and a man came to him and said: What do you say about Ali and Othman? He said: I am self-sufficient if Ali and Othman will seek me on the Day of Resurrection for their oppressors."
"33088","(33088) Ismail Ibn Ali told us on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I was informed on the authority of Nafi’ that he narrated, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Whoever is able to die in Medina should die there, for I will intercede for whoever died there.\n(Tirmidhi 3917 and Ibn Hibban 3741)"
"33089","(33089) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: God named Medina Tayyab. (Muslim 1007, Ahmad 101)"
"33090","(33090) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abi Yazid, who heard Jabir bin Abdullah says: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The city is like a carpenter. It removes evil just as it rejects it. Kilo is iron slag. (Ahmed 385)"
"33091","(33091) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Fatima bint Qais, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: This is good, meaning Medina, and by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is no wide path in it. And there is no hardship except over him an angel brandishing the sword until the Day of Resurrection. (Abu Dawud 4327. Ahmad 373)"
"33092","(33092) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The terror of the Antichrist will not enter the city, for on that day seven Doors, each door has two places. (Bukhari 1879. Ahmed 47)"
"33093","(33093) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah narrating on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The city is like a brick. It removes its evil and fulfills its goodness.\n(Ahmad 392. Bukhari 1883)"
"33094","(33094) Ibn Numir told us, on the authority of Hashim bin Hashim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nastas, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever fears the people of Medina will be cursed by God, the angels, and all people, no. God will accept his free speech, not justly. Whoever fears her has feared what is between these two: what is between his two sides.\n(Abu Dawud 1760, Ahmed 357)"
"33095","(33095) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talhi, on the authority of Anas that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The Antichrist will encompass the entire earth except Mecca and Medina. He said: Then he will come to Medina. Then he will find rows of angels at each of its entrances, and the marshes of the cliff will come and hit its portico, then it will tremble. The city will undergo three tremors, and every hypocrite, male and female, will go out there. (Bukhari 1881, Muslim 2266)"
"33096","(33096) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Khubayb ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hafs ibn Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Faith extends to Medina as it extends to cedar trees. The snake to its hole. (Bukhari 1876, Muslim 233)"
"33097","(33097) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Zayd, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, it is good and it expels evil, meaning the city.\n(Bukhari 1884, Muslim 1006)"
"33098","(33098) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yusir bin Amr, on the authority of Sahl bin Hanif, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took shelter with his hand to Medina and said: It is a safe sanctuary. (Muslim 1003, Ahmad 486)"
"33099","(33099) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The people of Yemen have come to you. They are soft-hearted and tender-hearted. Faith is faith and wisdom. Yemeni, and the head of disbelief is towards the east. (Muslim 73. Ahmad 252)"
"33100","(33100) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Abu Masoud, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, indicated He, peace be upon him, greeted him with his hand towards the right, and said: Indeed, faith is here, and cruelty and hardening of hearts are among the deserts at the origins of The tails of camels in Rabia and Mudar. (Bukhari 3302, Muslim 71)"
"33101","(33101) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Faith is among the people of Hijaz, and cruelty and hardening of hearts is before the East in its spring. And harmful (Muslim 73 Ahmad 335)"
"33102","(33102) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Salamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Faith Yaman, and wisdom is Yemeni, and they are a people among whom there is modesty and weakness, and perhaps he said: Aya. (Bukhari 3499. Muslim 82)"
"33103","(33103) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Jubayr. Ibn Mut'im, on the authority of his father, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he said: He will rise. The people of Yemen are upon you as if they were clouds. They are the best of those on earth. Then a man from the Ansar said: Except us, O Messenger of God. Then he said a weak word: Except you. (Abu Dawud 945. Ahmed 82)"
"33104","(33104) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Jabalah bin Atiyya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Awf Al-Dimashqi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Faith is the faith in the worm and the leprosy. (Tabarani 857)"
"33105","(33105) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abdullah Imam Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Amr bin Mara, on the authority of Khaythamah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Which people are the best? He said: The people of Yemen. (Ahmad 1651)"
"33106","(33106) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: Abdullah said: Faith is faith."
"33107","(33107) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out Peace be upon him from the house of Aisha, and he said: The head of disbelief is from here, from where the horn of Satan rises, meaning The East\n(Muslim 2229. Ahmad 23)"
"33108","(33108) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Jundub Al-Azdi, he said: We went out He was with Salman to Al-Hira, so he turned to Al-Kufa and said: The dome of Islam, there are no particulars that can be repelled by what can be repelled from this. The special ones except the special ones that Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, had, and the world will not go away until every believer is gathered in it, or A man who loves God"
"33109","(33109) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, he said: Jundub narrated to me, he said: We were With Salman as we came from Al-Hira, he said: Kufa is the dome of Islam twice."
"33110","(33110) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: What is paid On the authority of his hiding place, he did not refute his hiding place that was in Kufa, not his hiding place that was with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted you."
"33111","(33111) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Umayla, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: A man from the people of Kufa and a man from the people of Syria disagreed and they bragged, so the Kufay said: We are the Companions of the Day Al-Qadisiyah, and such-and-such day, and such-and-such day, and such-and-such day, and the Syrian said: We are the companions of Yarmouk and such-and-such day. And on such and such day, Hudhayfah said: Both of them did not bear witness to God. Ad and Thamud perished, God did not conspire with them. When He destroyed them, and there is no town more worthy of repenting from it a great one, meaning Kufa."
"33112","(33112) Shababa told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Habib Al-Urani, that Omar bin Al-Khattab said: O people of Kufa, you are the head of the Arabs, and their skulls and arrows are the ones I shoot with if anything comes to me. From here and here, and I sent to you Abdullah bin Masoud and chose him for you and preferred him over myself. Afterwards"
"33113","(33113) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr, who said: Omar wrote Ibn Al-Khattab, to the people of Kufa, to the people."
"33114","(33114) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, that Omar wrote to the people of Kufa: to the head of the Arabs."
"33115","(33115) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Omar wrote to them: To the head of the people of Islam."
"33116","(33116) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah Abi Al-Hudhayl, he said: A time will come upon the people. Every believer camps in Kufa."
"33117","(33117) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, who said: Omar said: Kufa is the spear of God and the treasure of faith. And the population of the Arabs, crossing their borders and extending the lands."
"33118","(33118) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of his father, he said: Hudhayfy said: What Hidden after hidden, she was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Badr, and he was protected from her as he was defended from this. It means Kufa."
"33119","(33119) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Jundub, on the authority of Salman, who said: Kufa is the dome of Islam. A time will come upon the people in which no believer will remain except in it, or his heart will be devoted to it."
"33120","(33120) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: I asked Al-Hasan: The people of Kufa are more noble, or The people of Basra, he said: He used to start with the people of Kufa."
"33121","(33121) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar. He said: O people of Kufa, you are the happiest people with the Mahdi."
"33122","(33122) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ata bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, he said: He said to me: From where you are, so I said: From the people of Kufa, and he said: By the one in whose hand is my soul, he will travel from it. To the land of the Arabs you do not possess a qafiz or a dirham, then he will not save you."
"33123","(33123) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Rabbā ibn Abi Rashid, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: Insight is better than Al-Kufa"
"33124","(33124) Affan told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughiry told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Layla, He said: I traveled through the mountains, and I did not see an Egyptian more prosperous than the people of Basra."
"33125","(33125) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said, he said Hudhayfah: Indeed, the people of Basra will not open the door of guidance, nor will they leave the door of error, and the flood has been lifted from the entire earth. Except for sight."
"33126","(33126) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: A man came to Hudhayfah and said: I want to Going out to Basra. He said: Do not go out there. He said: Do you have a relative there? He said: Do not go out. He said: It is necessary to go out. He said: So remove her throat, and do not lower her navel."
"33127","(33127) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Qurayh, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If the people of Syria become corrupt, then there is no good for you. (Ibn Hibban 7303 and Ahmad 436)"
"33128","(33128) Yazid told us, he said: Sha’bi told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumayr, on the authority of Abu Zaid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub. Al-Ansari, he said: The thunder, the lightning, and the blessings will migrate to the Levant."
"33129","(33129) Yazeed told us, he said: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: The extension of the Euphrates was at the time of Abd. By God, the people thought that he was upset, so he said: O people, do not dislike the mud, for it is about to be touched with a basin of water, but nothing. It exists, and that is when every water returns to its element, so the water and the rest of the believers will be in the Levant on that day."
"33130","(33130) Yazid narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Sa’id informed us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: {And We took them both to A Lord of Grass with stability and a source.} He said: Damascus."
"33131","(33131) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr al-Ghasani, on the authority of Habib, who said: Ka’b said: I love the country to God is the Levant, and the most beloved of the Levant is Jerusalem, and the most beloved of Jerusalem is a mountain in Nablus. A time will come upon the people when they will touch it, or They touch it with ropes between themselves."
"33132","(33132) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The Muslims’ stronghold from the epics is Damascus, their stronghold from the Antichrist is the Holy House, and their stronghold from Gog. And Magog, Bayt Al-Tur."
"33133","(33133) Yahya bin Ishaq told us, saying: Yahya bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib that Abdul Rahman bin Shamasa Al Mahri told him, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, who said: While we were around the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. We compose the Qur’an from the patches when he said: Blessed is the Levant. It was said: O Messenger of God, and what is that and why is that? He said: Indeed The angels of the Most Gracious spread their wings over them."
"33134","(33134) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik: {The land which We have blessed} He said: The Levant."
"33135","(33135) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Khalid Al-Asri, he said: When Salman came to us, we came to him. Let us recite it, so he said: The Qur’an is Arabic, so recite it in Arabic. Zaid bin Suhan used to recite it for us, so if he made a mistake Salman took it upon him, and when he was correct, he said: I swear to God."
"33136","(33136) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ransom for an Arab On the day of Badr, it was forty uqiyahs, and he made the ransom of the servant twenty uqiyahs, and the uqiyah was forty dirhams."
"33137","(33137) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Kharash, who said: Omar said: The Arabs will be destroyed when their sons reach the age of daughters. Persian"
"33138","(33138) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn bin Omar, on the authority of Muharriq, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Uthman bin Affan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever deceives the Arabs will not be included in my intercession nor will he May you receive my affection. (Tirmidhi 3928)"
"33139","(33139) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Shabib ibn Gharqadiya, on the authority of Al-Mustadhali ibn Husayn, he said: Omar ibn Al-Khattab addressed us, He said: I know, by the Lord of the Kaaba, when the Arabs will be destroyed. Then a man from among the Muslims stood up to him and said: When will they be destroyed? Commander of the Faithful, he said: When the affairs of those who did not deal with the pre-Islamic era and did not accompany the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, are in trouble. And he greeted you."
"33140","(33140) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Husayn al-Muzani, who said: Omar ibn al-Khattab said: The example of the Arabs is Like a camel that follows its leader, let its leader see where he is leading. As for me, by the side of the Kaab, I will carry them on. The way"
"33141","(33141) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Amr ibn Maadi was experiencing distress for some days. Al-Qadisiyah, and we are standing in ranks. He says: O Arabs, be strong lions, for the lion is one of the richest in status. The Persian is only a goat after... He will meet his meteorite."
"33142","(33142) Suwaid Al-Kalbi narrated to us, saying: Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salma narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Kathir ibn al-Salt said: A client of ours had sex with an Arab woman, so he came to Umar ibn Abdul-Aziz and sought him out, and he said: By God The master of the family of Kathir has changed his path."
"33143","(33143) Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, that he forbade an Arab to marry a slave woman, and that he decreed that the Arabs should marry slave women. And their children to be ransomed: six female slaves, men and women alike, and the follower is like that if he does not know. Al-Zuhri said: An Arab and a Mawla are not equal in lineage."
"33144","(33144) Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Razin told us, he said: My mother told me, she said: She was a mother Al-Harir: When an Arab man died, that became difficult for her, so it was said to her: O Umm Al-Harir, we will see you when an Arab man dies. It became difficult for you. She said: I heard my master saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Verily, from the approach of the Hour there will be doom. Arabs\n Its master was Talha bin Malik. (Tirmidhi 3929)"
"33145","(33145) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ya’qub, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra. He narrates, on the authority of his father, that Al-Aqra’ ibn Habis came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: The pilgrim’s thieves pledged allegiance to you from He has become a Muslim, a Forgiver, an honorable person, and I think he is a Hell. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What do you think if he has become a Muslim? And Ghaffar, and I consider Jahinah to be better than Banu Tamim and Banu Amir, Asad, and Ghatafan, who were disappointed and lost. He said: Yes. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, they are better than them. (Bukhari 3516, Muslim 1955)"
"33146","(33146) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Have you seen if it was Heaven and peace? And Ghaffar is better than the Banu Tamim and the Banu Abdullah bin Ghatafan and Aamir bin Sa’sa’, and he extended his voice to her. They said: O Messenger God, they have been disappointed and lost. He said: They are better. (Bukhari 3515. Muslim 1956)"
"33147","(33147) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abu Salamah narrating, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: I submit to Islam, Forgiver, and Praise be to Him, and whoever is from the side of Jinnah, or Jaina is better than Banu Tamim and Banu Amir, and its two allies: Asad and Ghatafan. (Muslim 1955, Ahmad 468)"
"33148","(33148) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, and Ghaffar are loyal to God and His Messenger, and no He has entrusted them with something else."
"33149","(33149) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Omar bin Rashid, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: May God bless her and grant her peace, and may God forgive her. (Ahmed 48)"
"33150","(33150) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Ibn Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Hanzala bin Ali Al-Aslami, on the authority of Khafaf bin Ima’ bin Rahdha Al-Ghafari, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led us in prayer. When He raised his head from the last rak’ah and said: May God grant her peace and forgiveness, may God forgive her. Then he turned and said: It is not me. I said This, but God said it."
"33151","(33151) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Tariq, he said: narrated to me Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad said that Abu Al-Darda’ used to swear by God: There will not remain a tribe that will not intermarry with Christianity without any measure. O community of Muslims, love Qais. O community of Muslims, love Qais."
"33152","(33152) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Harish narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Muhammad, he said: I was on a campaign with Muslima bin Abdul-Malik with the Turks, so Khaqan’s messenger threatened him and wrote to him: I will meet you with the Turks’ tales, so he wrote To Muslimah: You will meet me at the Turkish Hazwara, and I will meet you at the Arab Hazwara, meaning Qais."
"33153","(33153) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: The common people told us, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: Come closer, O people of Mudar. Indeed, among you is the master of the children of Adam, and among you are the ancestors of horses like the ancestors of horses."
"33154","(33154) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mu’amil, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If people disagree, the truth is harmful. (Abu Ali 2513. Tabarani 11418)"
"33155","(33155) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: Omar said: He measured the epics of the Arabs."
"33156","(33156) Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Awn ibn Abi Juhayfy, on the authority of his father, he said: We came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Al-Abtah in a red dome, and he said: Who are you? We said: Banu Amir. He said: Welcome, you. From me\n(Tabarani 244, Bazzar 2831)"
"33157","(33157) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of the fight, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: In the pre-Islamic era we and you were Banu Abd Manaf, so today we are Banu Abdullah and you are Banu Abdullah. \n(Bukhari 12)"
"33158","(33158) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God Provide me with Amir and protect Banu Amir. (Abdul Razzaq 19884)"
"33159","(33159) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mus`ar, on the authority of Khasram al-Jaafari, that the Asnani governor Aamir ibn Malik was sent to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He asked him for a cure or cure for an illness that befell him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent him honey. Or a stick of honey."
"33160","(33160) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: She came to his son Khaled bin Sinan Al-Absi went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Welcome to my brother’s son, welcome to the son of a prophet whom he lost. His people\n(Bazzar 2361. Tabarani 12250)"
"33161","(33161) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: O my son. He frowned, what is your slogan? They said: Forbidden. He said: Rather, your slogan is permissible."
"33162","(33162) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Ad-Daris Uqba bin Ammar Al-Absi narrated to us, on the authority of Masoud bin Harash, a brother of Rabi’i. Ibn Harash narrated that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab asked the Abbasids: Which of the horses did you find to be the most patient in your war? They said: The Kumaite."
"33163","(33163) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, besieged the people of Taif, and his companions came to him and said: O Messenger of God, the arrows of Thaqif have burned us. Then pray to God for them, and he said: Oh God, guide Thaqif. (Ahmed 343)"
"33164","(33164) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I have decided that I will not accept anyone except from a Qurayshite, an Ansar, or a Thaqafi.\n(Abdul Razzaq 14521. Ibn Hibban 6384)"
"33165","(33165) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have decided that I will not accept my gift except from a Qurayshite, or Ansari, Thaqafi, or Dawsi. (Tirmidhi 3946)"
"33166","(33166) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Jamra, on the authority of Ibn Abbas that the delegation of Abdul Qais came to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: From the delegation, or from the people. He said: They said: Rabi’ah. He said: Welcome the delegation, or the people, neither disgraced nor regretful."
"33167","(33167) Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Walid, he said: Shihab bin Abbad Al-Asri narrated to me that his father narrated to him Omar bin Al-Khattab stopped by them at Arafat and said: Who is this information for? They said: By Abd al-Qais, so he supplicated for them and asked forgiveness for them."
"33168","(33168) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra mentioned, he said: Ashjaj Bani Asr: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: There are two creatures in you that God loves, so I said: What are they? He said: Dreaming and living, he said: I said: in the past, it was in me or recently? He said: Indeed, in the past, he said: I said: Praise be to God who created me with two creatures that He loves."
"33169","(33169) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Safwan ibn Mahriz al-Mazini, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, who said: Banu Tamim came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Rejoice, O Banu Tamim. They said: O Messenger of God, you gave us good tidings, so give us. (Bukhari 3190, Ahmed 433)"
"33170","(33170) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Al-Ma’rour bin Suwayd, on the authority of Ibn Fatik, who said: Ka'b told me: The most severe of the Arabs living against the Antichrist is your people, meaning Banu Tamim."
"33171","(33171) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Musafir al-Jassas, on the authority of Fasil ibn Amr, and he said: They mentioned Bani Tamim at Hudhayfah, and he said: They are the people who are the hardest against the Antichrist."
"33172","(33172) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Mandal, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of a man, who said: A man from the Ansar proposed marriage to a woman, and he said to him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: What harm would it do you, if she was religious and beautiful, not to be from the family of Hajib bin Zurarah?"
"33173","(33173) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: He recited to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Of every five people, a man was greeted. They differed in the language, so it was assumed that all of them recited it. Banu Tamim was an Arabic language. The people (Ibn Jarir 19)"
"33174","(33174) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Ibn Sirin that Abu Musa He wrote to Omar on the eighteenth day of a drought that befell her, so Omar wrote to him to place her in the bravest neighborhood among the Arabs. He said: So he placed it in Banu Riyah, a neighborhood of Banu Tamim."
"33175","(33175) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The first to pledge allegiance on the day of Al-Hudaybiyyah was Abu Sinan. The lion (Ibn Saad 100)"
"33176","(33176) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim ibn Bahdaliya, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, that a delegation The Banu Asad came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Who are you? They said: We are the sons of your adultery. He said: You are the sons of Rushda"
"33177","(33177) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid narrated to us, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, he said: I met two thousand of Banu Asad who had They witnessed Al-Qadisiyah in two thousand, and its banners were in the hands of Samak, the owner of the mosque."
"33178","(33178) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ali came with his sword, and he said: Take it, praised. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you fought well today, then Sahl bin Hanif and Asim bin Thabit, Al-Harith bin Sammah, Abu Dujanah, and on the authority of Ikramah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Uhud: Who took this? The sword is right, so Abu Dujana said: I am, and he took the sword and struck with it until he brought it with it bent over, so he said: O Messenger of God, I gave him what he deserved, he said yes. (Tabarani 6507. Hakim 24)"
"33179","(33179) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May the peace and blessings of God be upon him to Bilal: What did you do to the group of the Bijlis? Start with the Ahmasis before the Qasrinis. (Ahmad 1668)"
"33180","(33180) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mukhariq, on the authority of Tariq, he said: Forced delegations came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 3151 8211)"
"33181","(33181) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Six of the non-Arabs witnessed Badr, including Bilal. And Tamim."
"33182","(33182) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, who narrated it, saying: If The debt was hung on a chandelier for people from Persia to collect it. (Abu Ali 1434. Tabarani 901)"
"33183","(33183) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: If the debt were attached to the chandelier, some of the people of Persia would accept it. (Bukhari 4897, Muslim 231)"
"33184","(33184) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Qays, that Omar bin Al-Khattab made an obligation for the people of Badr. For their Arabs and their masters, it is five thousand five thousand, and he said: I will prefer them over all others."
"33185","(33185) Ahmad bin Al-Mufaddal narrated to us, saying: Asbat bin Nasr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Azdi, on the authority of Abi Al-Kanood, on the authority of Khabab bin Al-Art: (And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord in the morning and the evening, seeking His face.) He said: Al-Aqra’ ibn Habis al-Tamimi and Uyaynah ibn Hisn al-Fazari came and found the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sitting with Bilal. Ammar, Sahib, and Khabab bin Al-Art were some of the weak believers. When they saw them, they despised them, so they brought him and left with him. They said: We would like for you to make a gathering for us in which the Arabs would make known to us our virtue, for Arab delegations come to you and we are ashamed for you to see us. With this servant, so when we come to you, let them stay with us, and when we have finished, sit with them if you wish. He said: Yes, They said: Then write a letter for us. So he called for the manuscript to be written and called for Ali to write it. When he wanted to do that while we were sitting in About him, when Gabriel descended upon him and said: {And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord in the morning and the evening, desiring His face} to His saying {Then you will drive them out and be of the wrongdoers}"
"33186","(33186) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abi Al-Miqdam, on the authority of Hibba, who said: A man came to Ali bin Abi A student, and he said: I bought a camel and prepared it, and I want the sanctuary, so he said: Sell your camel and pray in this mosque, Abu Bakr: meaning the Kufa Mosque. There is no mosque more beloved to me after the Sacred Mosque than it. It was less than five hundred percent of what was established. An arm"
"33187","(33187) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, He said: Ka'b met me in the Holy House, and he said: Where did you come from? I said: From the Kufa Mosque. He said: Because I came from where I came is more beloved to me than giving two thousand dinars in charity. A dinar from it is in the hand of every poor person. Then he swore: It is in the middle of the earth like the bottom of a basin."
"33188","(33188) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Sakhr, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: Whoever comes to this mosque of mine, Abu Bakr said: He means the mosque of Medina, he will not come to it except For the good that he teaches him, or that he learns, then he is in the position of one who strives in the path of God, and whoever comes for other than that, then he is In the same manner as a man, he looks at other people’s possessions."
"33189","(33189) Shababah told us, he said: Laith bin Saad told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Ma’abad, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maimunah, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: A prayer in it, meaning The Mosque of Medina is better than a thousand prayers performed anywhere else except the Mosque of Mecca.\n Abu Bakr said: And it was narrated by Ibn Abbas that the people of Egypt will not enter it."
"33190","(33190) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Sahil bin Saad, On the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: The mosque that was founded on piety is my mosque."
"33191","(33191) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar, he said: Abu Al-Abard, the client of Banu Khatmah, narrated to us that He heard Usayd bin Dhahir Al-Ansari, who was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, speaking on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: A prayer in the Quba Mosque is like Umrah."
"33192","(33192) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, he said: Yusuf ibn Taman informed me, on the authority of Abu Umamiya ibn Sa’l bin Hanif, on the authority of his father Sa’l bin Hanif, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever performs ablution He performed his ablution well, then he came to the Quba Mosque and prayed four rak’ahs there. This was the parity of his life."
"33193","(33193) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubad Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He will come to Qaba’, riding and walking."
"33194","(33194) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha bin Rukan. Al-Muttalibi, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mutim, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is a prayer in this mosque. Better than a thousand prayers in any place except the Sacred Mosque."
"33195","(33195) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah informed us, on the authority of Dawud bin Mudarrak, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubair. On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One prayer in this mosque of yours is better than a thousand prayers in it. Other mosques except the Sacred Mosque."
"33196","Abu Abdul Rahman narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying:\n(33196) Waki’ ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God bless him and grant him peace?? Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, whoever obeys the Imam has obeyed me, whoever disobeys me has disobeyed God, and whoever disobeys the Imam has disobeyed God. Disobedient (Ibn Majah 2859. Ahmed 252)"
"33197","(33197) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever obeys my prince has obeyed me. (Bukhari 2957. Muslim 32)"
"33198","(33198) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: {Obey God And obey the Messenger and those in authority among you. He said: The princes."
"33199","(33199) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, he said: I heard Mus’ab bin Sa’d say: Ali bin Abu Talib: Words that he got right: It is the duty of the imam to rule according to what God has revealed and to fulfill what is entrusted to him. So if he did This is the right of Muslims to listen, obey, and respond when they are called upon."
"33200","(33200) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdul God: {And those in charge of authority among you} He said: Those who are endowed with jurisprudence, the possessors of goodness."
"33201","(33201) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, in his saying: {Obey God and obey the Messenger And those in authority among you.} He said: Mujahid used to say: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and perhaps he said: People of reason. And jurisprudence in the religion of God."
"33202","(33202) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja’far narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, he said: The scholars."
"33203","(33203) Waki’ and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb. Al-Kaaba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever pledges allegiance to an imam and gives him his share His hand and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him as much as he is able. (Muslim 1473. Ahmad 161)"
"33204","(33204) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of his grandmother, Umm Al-Husayn, she said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was giving a sermon in Arafah, and he was saying: If an Ethiopian slave is appointed over you, then listen. To Him and obey what He leads you by the Book of God. (Muslim 1468. Ahmad 70)"
"33205","(33205) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Izar bin Harith Al-Abdi, on the authority of Umm Al-Husain Al-Ahmasiyya, she said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was delivering the sermon with his cloak, wearing a cloak and wrapped in it. And he says: If an Abyssinian slave with a hairy face is commanded over you, then listen to him and obey what he leads you according to the Book of God. (Ahmed 403)"
"33206","(33206) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri: {Obey God and obey The Messenger and those in authority among you}, he said: the commanders of the palaces."
"33207","(33207) Yazid bin Harun told us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us that Al-Harith bin Yazid Al-Hadrami He told him that Abu Dharr asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the leadership, and that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, it is weak, and it is a trust, and on the Day of Resurrection, it will be a shame and a regret, except for the one who takes it as it is due and fulfills what he deserved. May God bless him and grant him peace.\n(Muslim 1457, Tayalisi 485)"
"33208","(33208) Abu Asama told us, he said: Burayd bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: I entered On the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I and two men from my cousins, and one of the two men said: O Messenger of God, command us to Some of what God has given you control over, and the other said something like that, he said: Then he said: By God, we will not entrust this work to anyone who asks Him, nor to anyone who is keen. Aliyah (Bukhari 7149. Abu Dawud 2923)"
"33209","(33209) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You will be keen on the leadership, and you will become sad and regretful, so I was blessed. The breastfeeding woman and wretched is the fatima. (Bukhari 7128. Ahmed 448)"
"33210","(33210) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Zayd bin Jud’an narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Samra told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Do not ask the Emirate. If you are given it for a request, you will be entrusted to it, and if you are given it for another request, you will help it with it.\n(Bukhari 6422. Abu Dawud 2922)"
"33211","(33211) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, he said: Al-Abbas said, O Messenger of God, did not You employ me? He said: O Abbas, O uncle of the Messenger of God, a soul that you save is better than an emirate that you cannot count. \n(Ibn Saad 27. Bayhaqi 96)"
"33212","(33212) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, who said: There is no An arbitrator who rules between the people, except that he will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, and an angel will take hold of him until he stands with him over Hell, then he will be raised. his head to the Most Gracious, and if he said to him: Throw it away, then he cast it in a shelter for forty sheep, he said: and Masruq said: to fulfill One day with justice and truth is more beloved to me than a year that I fight in the way of God."
"33213","(33213) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Fudayl bin Ghazwan told us, on the authority of Muhammad al-Rasibi, on the authority of Bishr bin Asim, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab wrote his covenant and said: I have no need for it, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The rulers will be brought to them on the Day of Resurrection, and they will stand on the brink of Hell. So whoever is obedient to God, God will take him. With his right hand until he saves him, and whoever disobeys God, the bridge will be pierced by him into a valley of blazing fire. He said: So Omar sent To Abu Dharr and to Salman. He said to Abu Dharr: Did you hear this hadith from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, by God, and after the valley there was another valley of fire. He said: And Salman asked his thoughts to tell something, so Omar said: Who He took it with what was in it, and Abu Dharr said: He whose nose and eyes are drawn to God, and whose cheeks are lowered to the ground. (Musnad 587)"
"33214","(33214) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Khaythama, he said : The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The emirate is a door, infidels, except those whom God has mercy on. (Tabarani 3603)"
"33215","(33215) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar said: No man was so keen. He took charge of the emirate and treated it fairly."
"33216","(33216) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Harun al-Hadrami, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, that Omar ibn Al-Khattab hired a man, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, advise me. He said: Sit down and speak to me."
"33217","(33217) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Ashhab Ja’far bin Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He hired a man, and he said: O Messenger of God, come down to me. He said: Sit. (Tabarani 493)"
"33218","(33218) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Talha bin Musrif al-Yami, saying: Khalid bin said: Al-Walid: Do not go on a date with a needle, do not walk three paces while standing on two legs, and do not seek the Imam of the Muslims by deceit."
"33219","(33219) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Marzuq, on the authority of Maimun, on the authority of a man from Abd al-Qais said: I saw Salman riding a donkey in a company, and he was its commander and his two female servants were shaking and the soldiers were saying: He has come. The prince came. The prince came and said: Then Salman said: The good and the evil are only after today. If you are able to eat from the dust, and do not be commanded. On two legs, so do so, and beware of the claim of the oppressed, for it will not be withheld."
"33220","(33220) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Issa bin Faid, who said: So-and-so narrated to me, On the authority of Saad bin Ubadah, he said: He told us on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: There is no prince of a group but he is brought to him. On the Day of Resurrection, he will be shackled, and no one will relieve him of that burden except justice. (Ahmad 284. Tabarani 5388)"
"33221","(33221) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is no leader of three but that on the Day of Resurrection he will be brought chained to his neck. The truth has set him free, or he has made him trustworthy. (Ahmad 431, Darami 2515)"
"33222","(33222) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ibn Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Ismail Al-Awdi, he said: Bint Maqil told me Ibn Yasar narrated that her father said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: There is no guardian like his mother, or It has increased, and nothing can be changed except for God to throw it on his face in Hell. (Bukhari 1072, Ahmed 25)"
"33223","(33223) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yassar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Abi Huraira, he said: There is no prince of the people but he will be brought to him on the Day of Resurrection if the truth has set him free, or he has made him trustworthy."
"33224","(33224) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Ishaq bin Hazim narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Muhammad bin Al-Akhnas narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad said: Saad said: It is enough for you that a woman does not add any good to a person in his religion."
"33225","(33225) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sa`dan al-Janni narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`d Abi Mujahid al-Tai’i, on the authority of Abu Mudalliyah, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The just Imam will not have his supplication rejected."
"33226","(33226) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, who said: The work of a just imam is better than One of you worked for sixty years."
"33227","(33227) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said In Paradise there is a palace called Eden, surrounded by meadows and towers, and five thousand gates that no one can live in, or no one can enter except him. A prophet, a truthful person, a martyr, or a just imam."
"33228","(33228) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Mikhraq, on the authority of Abu Kinana, on the authority of Abu Musa, He said: It is part of God’s reverence to honor the gray-haired Muslim and the bearer of the Qur’an who is not exaggerated in it, nor is he who is unjust and honorable. Possessor of just authority."
"33229","(33229) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ammar said: There are three who do not underestimate their rights except A hypocrite whose hypocrisy is evident: the just Imam, the teacher of goodness, and the one who has gray hair in Islam."
"33230","(33230) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Makin narrated to us, saying: I heard Zayd bin Aslam saying {Indeed, God has commanded you to Return the trusts to their rightful owners, and when you judge between the people, judge with justice. He said: It was revealed regarding the authority of the affairs."
"33231","(33231) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {Indeed, Allah He commanded you to deliver trusts to their families. He said: This is ambiguous for the righteous and the immoral."
"33232","(33232) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Marzuq, the client of Tajib, said: We invaded with Rufa’ bin Thabit Al-Ansari towards the West, and we conquered a village called Laha. He tried him, he said: Then he stood up and preached among us, and said: I do not say anything about you except what I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say. Among us on the Day of Khaybar: Whoever believes in God and the Last Day let him not ride any animal from among the Muslims until He should put it back in it, and he should not wear a Muslim garment, even if he has cleaned it, he should put it in it."
"33233","(33233) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, he said: Salman was on the verge of arrest of the immigrants, so he came A man with a fist came to him, who was with him, so he pushed him to him, then he turned away and returned to him and said: O Salman, it was in my garment. A rag, so she took a thread from this clutch and drew with it. He said: Everything and its destiny. He said: Then the man came and spread the thread from His dress, then he said: I am in need of this."
"33234","(33234) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of some of his companions that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: O, by the Lord of deceit, that a man should ride an animal until it is lost before it is led to the spoils, or wear a garment until He is created before he leads to the spoils."
"33235","(33235) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: We invaded Balanjar with Salman bin Rabi’a. So He made it difficult for us to carry the animals of the spoils, and made a concession for us to use the sieve, the sieve, and the rope."
"33236","(33236) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salam bin Abd al-Rahman al-Nakha’i, on the authority of Abu Zur’i bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to drive a pack of horses.\n(Muslim 1494. Abu Dawud 2540)"
"33237","(33237) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Ad-Daris Uqba bin Ammar Al-Absi narrated to us, on the authority of Masoud bin Harash, my brother. It is reported that Omar ibn al-Khattab asked the Abbasids: Which horse did you find to be the most patient in your war? They said: The Kumaite."
"33238","(33238) Waki’ told us, he said: Talha told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Good. The lively horses"
"33239","(33239) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ali narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating that a man came to a Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I want to tie up a horse, or buy a horse, he said: So he said: So on you, I will offer my inheritance. As a dead person, or a swollen person, divorced from the Yemeni language. (Tirmidhi 1697 and Ibn Hibban 4676)"
"33240","(33240) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Thawr al-Shami narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Wadhin bin Ata’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Do not trim the tails of horses, for they are their molt, and do not trim their manes, for they are their heat."
"33241","(33241) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Omar forbade the geldings of horses. He said: And I think he said: And about removing its tails."
"33242","(33242) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, that he used to hate horses being beaten."
"33243","(33243) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, or someone else, on the authority of Omar said: Do not cut the tails of horses."
"33244","(33244) Waki’ told us, he said: Abdullah bin Nafi’ told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of the testicles of horses and animals, and Ibn Umar said that it is the growth of character. (Ahmed 24)"
"33245","(33245) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Omar wrote a letter forbidding the characteristics of horses."
"33246","(33246) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir al-Bajlili, who said: Omar decreed that a horse should not be castrated. It does not apply to more than two hundred."
"33247","(33247) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Usama bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, he said: Omar bin Zayd wrote Abdul Aziz addressed the people of Egypt and forbade them from riding horses, and that boys should drive horses."
"33248","(33248) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Ja`far al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, he said: I heard Anas say: {And I will command them to change the creation of God} He said: the elite."
"33249","(33249) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: The eunuchs."
"33250","(33250) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Makin narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, that he hated the creatures of animals."
"33251","(33251) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawus, and Mujahid, and Al-Hasan, and it was reported that they disliked it. Castration"
"33252","(33252) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar that Umar forbade the elite, and said: Al-Nama’i. With the remembrance"
"33253","(33253) Asbat bin Muhammad and Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The characteristics of animals. A parable, then he recited: {And I will command them, so that they may change the creation of God}"
"33254","(33254) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us that his father castrated a mule of his own."
"33255","(33255) Waki’ told us, he said, Malik ibn Mughul told us, he said: I asked Ata’ about the characteristics of horses, he said: He was not afraid. There is nothing wrong with him and his bad character."
"33256","(33256) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir al-Madaini, on the authority of al-Hasan, he said: No?? It is valiant for the creatures of animals."
"33257","(33257) Some Basras narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: There is no harm in the horses’ geldings, if they are left The stallions eat each other."
"33258","(33258) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Abu al-Jarrah, on the authority of Umm Habiba, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell.\n(Ahmad 326, Darami 2475)"
"33259","(33259) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell, nor a dog.\n(Ahmad 2621, Muslim 1672)"
"33260","(33260) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit the client of Umm Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama, she said: Angels do not accompany a company in which there is a jingle. (Tabarani 23)"
"33261","(33261) Waki’ told us, he said: Ja’far bin Burqan told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, he said: Aisha used to hate it. The sound of the bell."
"33262","(33262) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I came to Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi To Layla with a sigh, he said: Could you please make them bells, for they are disliked?"
"33263","(33263) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, He said: For every bell there is a trace of the jinn."
"33264","(33264) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: Angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"33265","(33265) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Amir Al-Aslami narrated to us, saying: I heard an alcoholic saying: The angels You wipe out the animals of the invaders, except for an animal with a bell on it."
"33266","(33266) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Thawr narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled bin Ma’dan, he said: Go by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. With a camel with a bell around its neck, he said: This is the mount of Satan."
"33267","(33267) Rayhan bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Marzuq bin Amr, who said: Abu Farqad said: I saw the dryings of Abu Musa. Brocade and silk."
"33268","(33268) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: My father used to wear some brocade that he wore in war."
"33269","(33269) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in it if it is a garment or a weapon."
"33270","(33270) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in wearing silk in war."
"33271","(33271) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mundhir bin Tha’labiya Al-Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Alba’ bin Ahmar Al-Shakri, or Ibn Buraida Al-Mundhir doubted, saying: Some of the Muhajireen said to Omar: When we see the enemy and we see them have disbelieved Their weapons were covered with silk, and we saw that there was a fear, so Omar said: If you wish, make atonement for your weapons with silk. And the brocade."
"33272","(33272) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Muhammad about wearing brocade in war, and he said: Who Where did they find the preamble?"
"33273","(33273) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Makin bin Aban narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah; He disliked wearing silk and brocade in war, and he said: I hope that what a martyr would wear is what a martyr should wear."
"33274","(33274) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he disliked wearing silk in The war"
"33275","(33275) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Hisham, who said: I wrote to Ibn Muhayriz. I ask him about wearing silk and velvet in places of war? He said: So he wrote: Be as strong as you are in your hatred of what is disliked when fighting, when you expose yourself to witnesses."
"33276","(33276) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Awza’i, on the authority of al-Walid bin Hisham. On the authority of Ibn Muhayriz that he hated wearing it during war."
"33277","(33277) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, he said: We witnessed Yarmouk, he said: So Omar received us wearing brocade and silk, so he ordered us to be stoned."
"33278","(33278) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Ashhab, who said: I said to al-Hasan: O Abu Sa`id: A man should be naked. He wears a robe, or he is unarmed and free of weapons. He said: He does, so if he attends the oath, let him bring it."
"33279","(33279) Waki` narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan saying: When Muslims acquire weapons and animals and want to seek help, And they need it, there is no harm in it, even if they do not ask the imam for permission."
"33280","(33280) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Ubayy and Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: He said: Abdullah: I went to Abu Jalal on the day of Badr, and his leg had been struck and he was paralyzed, and people were defending him. with his sword, so I said: Praise be to God who has disgraced you, O enemy of God. So he said: Is there anything other than a man whose people killed him? So I made I handed him a sword, but it was useless, so his hand was hit and his sword dangled, so I took it and hit him with it until he became cold."
"33281","(33281) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudharib, on the authority of Ali, he said: You saw us on the day of Badr as we were seeking refuge with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was the closest of us to the enemy, and he was one of the most powerful. People will be miserable that day. (Ahmad 1261, Abu Ali 297)"
"33282","(33282) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: When the battle became red, we would protect ourselves from it. With it, and the brave is the one who follows it. (Muslim 1401)"
"33283","(33283) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hassan bin Faid Al-Absi, he said: Omar said: Courage and cowardice are instincts in men, so the brave fights on behalf of those who know and those who do not know, and the cowardly flees from his father. And his mother"
"33284","(33284) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Qubaisa ibn Jabir, He said: Omar said: The brave and cowardly are a characteristic or characteristic of men, so the brave fights on behalf of the one who does not care about not returning to him. And the coward flees his family, from his father’s son and his mother."
"33285","(33285) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ash’ath narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, is the bravest of people and the most generous of people. (Bukhari 2820, Muslim 48)"
"33286","(33286) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Ibn Saad 419)"
"33287","(33287) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: I heard Khaled bin Al-Walid saying: It has been cut off in My hands on the day of my death will be as large as nine swords, and will be covered with a Yemeni plate."
"33288","(33288) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hashim bin Hashim, who said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab saying: Sa’d was Ibn Malik was the most powerful of the Muslims on the day of Uhud."
"33289","(33289) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: No temptation, no junub."
"33290","(33290) Sahl bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husain, something similar, but he did not narrate it."
"33291","(33291) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ma’qil bin Ubaid Allah Al-Absi narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: There is no temptation or junub in Islam."
"33292","(33292) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Neither jabbah, nor junubah. (Abu Dawud 1587, Ahmed 180)"
"33293","(33293) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Jawni, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: The coward has two rewards."
"33294","(33294) Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abdul Karim, who said: Aisha said: If any of you feels something about himself cowardice; So they will not invade."
"33295","(33295) Muhammad ibn Mus’ab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Al-Fudayl ibn Fadhala, who said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: No, she slept. The eyes of cowards."
"33296","(33296) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: He ruled The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, during the pre-Islamic captivity, included in the boy eight camels, and in the mirror ten camels. Or a male or female slave deceived him."
"33297","(33297) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Omar said: No Arab has any kingship. We do not dispute from anyone anything that he has said to him, but we will present it to the mullahs: five camels, five camels."
"33298","(33298) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Sadiqa, on the authority of Rabah ibn Al-Harith, who said: Omar used to judge while the Arabs were on a sabbath. One upon another before Islam and before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent, that whoever knew one of his family He was owned by a neighborhood of the Arabs, so he ransomed a male slave for two female slaves and a female slave for two female slaves."
"33299","(33299) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: When Salman invaded The polytheists from the people of Persia. He said: Stop until I call upon them as I used to listen to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He called them, so he came to them and said: I am a man among you and you may know my place from these people, and we call you to Islam. If you submit, then you have the same as what we have, and you have the same as what we have, but if you refuse, then pay the tribute out of hand. And you are submissive, and if you refuse, we will fight you. They refused, so he said to the people: Go to them. (Ahmed 440)"
"33300","(33300) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraydah, on the authority of His father, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he sent an emir to command a convoy or an army, he would command him, and he said: If You meet your enemy among the polytheists, so invite them to one of three characteristics or characteristics, and you give them what they have responded to you, so accept. From them and desist from them: Invite them to Islam, and if they respond to you, desist from them and accept from them, then invite them to convert. From their home to the home of the emigrants, and inform them that if they do that, they will have the same as the emigrants, and that On the immigrants, and if they refuse and choose their home, inform them that they will be like the Bedouins of the Muslims. Upon them is the judgment of God which applies to the believers, and they will have no share in the spoils or the spoils except that They strive with the Muslims, but if they refuse, invite them to pay the tribute. If they respond, then accept from them and desist from them. And if they refuse, then seek help from God and fight them."
"33301","(33301) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, fought The people of this peninsula were among the Arabs who accepted Islam, and no one else accepted from them. He was the best of jihad, and he was after him. Another struggle against this group among the People of the Book: {Fight those who believe neither in God nor in the Last Day} etc. The verse, Al-Hasan said: Nothing besides them is heresy and misguidance."
"33302","(33302) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zaid bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wrote Peace and blessings of God be upon him and to the people of Yemen: Whoever performs our prayers, faces our qiblah, and eats our sacrifice, that is the Muslim, and he is subject to a liability. God has protected the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and whoever refuses to do so is subject to the reward. (Bukhari 391)"
"33303","(33303) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wael and Ibrahim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, Mu’adh was delivered to Yemen and he commanded him to take a tribute from every dreamer, a dinar, or a reward of reward from every dreamer."
"33304","(33304) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Omar’s client, he said: Omar wrote to Commanders of the Jizya: Do not impose the Jizya except on those on whom the razor has passed, and do not impose the Jizya on women, nor on men. Al-Sibyan, he said: Omar used to seal the people of the Jiziya on their necks."
"33305","(33305) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Fudail bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He fights the people of Religions are against Islam, and the People of the Book are fought for the tribute."
"33306","(33306) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, Mu’adh was sent to Yemen, commanding him to take from every dreamer a dinar, or a reward of reward. (Abu Dawad 3033)"
"33307","(33307) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Majliz, that Umar placed a burden on every head in the Sunnah. Twenty-four, and spared women and boys."
"33308","(33308) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Aslam, Omar’s client, that Omar He wrote to his workers: Do not strike the jizya on women and children, and do not strike it except on those on whom the razor has struck. And He will seal their necks, and place their tribute on their heads: The people of the paper are forty dirhams, and with that are provisions. The Muslims, and the people of the Levant are responsible for four dinars, and the people of the Levant are obligated to pay a handful of wheat and three installments of oil. And the people of Egypt are obligated to pay a grain of wheat, clothing, and honey, and no one can save the benefit. How much is that? And the people of Iraq are obligated to fifteen saa’s. Wheat, he said: Ubaidullah said: And he mentioned clothing that I do not remember. (Bayhaqi 195)"
"33309","(33309) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that Ibrahim bin Saad asked Ibn Abbas: What It is taken from the wealth of the people of religion. He said: forgiveness."
"33310","(33310) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan bin Sinan Abu Sinan narrated to us, on the authority of Antarah Abi Waki’ that Ali was He takes the offers in the reward, from the people of needles, from the people of the questionable, and from the people of the ropes, the ropes."
"33311","(33311) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Awn Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi, who said: Omar placed Ibn al-Khattab means, in terms of the tribute levied on the heads of men: for the rich man, forty-eight dirhams, and for the middle class, four. And twenty, and the poor man owes twelve dirhams."
"33312","(33312) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Ma’qil, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: It should not be taken from the people of The book is only a part of the Jizya, and it shall not be taken from a fugitive, nor from a dead person, nor shall the people of the land be taken from a fugitive."
"33313","(33313) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ali, he said: He wrote The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to the Magians of Hijr, offering them Islam. Whoever converted to Islam accepted it, and whoever refused was beaten. The penalty is that no slaughtered animal may be eaten for them, nor may a woman be married to them."
"33314","(33314) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the jizya from the Magians of Bahrain. (Ibn Zanjawiyah 125)"
"33315","(33315) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Anas narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the jizya from the Magi of the two seas, and Omar took it from the Magi of the people of Persia. Othman took it from the Berber Magi.\n(Malik 278. Bayhaqi 195)"
"33316","(33316) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Bajal, who said: Omar did not take taxes from the Magians. Abdul Rahman bin Awf even testified that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it from the Magians of Hijra.\n(Bukhari 3157, Abu Dawud 3038)"
"33317","(33317) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Siwar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and grant him the tribute from the Magians of the people of Hijr and from the Jews of Yemen and their Christians from every dreamer a dinar, and Omar took The jizya was from the Magi of the blacks, and Othman took the jizya from the Magi of Egypt, the Berbers."
"33318","(33318) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that Omar ibn al-Khattab asked about the reward of the Magians, and Abd said: Al-Rahman bin Awf: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: They followed the path of the People of the Book."
"33319","(33319) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Malik bin Anas narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that Omar bin Al-Khattab The people consulted the Magians about the tax, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: They followed the Sunnah of the People of the Book."
"33320","(33320) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, that he heard his Majesty speaking to Amr ibn Aws and Abu al-Sha’tha’i, He said: I was writing to Juz bin Muawiyah: Then the letter of Omar came to us saying, “Kill every sorcerer, male and female, and separate among every one of them.” Muhrim from the Magians, and he turned them away from Zamzamah, so we killed three sorcerers, and made a distinction between the man and his harem. In the Book of God"
"33321","(33321) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Qushayr bin Amr, on the authority of Bajal Ibn Abdah Al-Anbari, who was the scribe of Juza’ Ibn Mu’awiyah, and he was on the Ahwaz sect. It was narrated that Abu Musa and The Emir of Basra wrote to us that Omar ibn al-Khattab wrote to him ordering him to kill al-Zamazmiya until they spoke, and to Every woman will be removed from her harem, and every sorcerer will be killed. Abu Musa wrote about this to Juz’ ibn Muawiyah. So he called the reins and they talked. He said: And when the woman was young, We would remove her from her harem and marry her to another. And when she was old, we forbade her and forbade her."
"33322","(33322) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, who said: Abbad narrated to me, on the authority of Bajaliya bin Abdah, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa said, “Expose to the Magians before you that they should abandon the marriage of their mothers, their daughters, and their sisters, and eat All together, in order to catch up with the People of the Book and kill every sorcerer and soothsayer."
"33323","(33323) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, he said: I asked my wife about a man who makes purchases. Or does he take the Magi captive, then have intercourse with her before she learns Islam? He said: He is not fit. He said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr, and he said: He is not better than her if he does that."
"33324","(33324) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, he said: I asked Mara bin Sharahil Al-Hamdani and Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of a Magi mother who was afflicted by a man, did he have intercourse with her? He said: He will not have intercourse with her until she submits, and Sa`id bin Jubayr said: If he goes back to her, it is worse than her."
"33325","(33325) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: If she is a Magi’s child, then he should not marry her. Until you are safe."
"33326","(33326) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who heard him say: Do not approach the Magi until you say: There is no god. Except Allah, so if she says that, then it is Islam on her part."
"33327","(33327) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, who said: No. He has intercourse with her until she delivers."
"33328","(33328) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, he said: The Messenger of God wrote May God’s prayers and peace be upon him to the Magians of Hijr, offering them Islam. Whoever among them converts to Islam, it will be accepted from him, and whoever refuses will be beaten. He is subject to the penalty other than that no meat may be eaten from them, and no woman may be married to them."
"33329","(33329) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the Magi you are with the man? He said: He does not fold it."
"33330","(33330) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the Magi women and the idol worshipers are taken captive Islam was offered to them and they were forced to accept it. If they converted to Islam, they were settled and were used, and if they refused to convert, they were used and not He is settled."
"33331","(33331) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: There is no harm in A man buys a magician slave girl and is pleased with her."
"33332","(33332) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the Jewish and Christian women were taken captive Islam was offered to them and they were forced to do so. Whether they converted to Islam or not, they were settled in and used."
"33333","(33333) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If a man strikes a polytheist slave girl, So let him confirm it with his testimony that there is no god but Allah. If she refuses to acknowledge it, that will not prevent him from having intercourse with her."
"33334","(33334) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; Concerning a man, if he has a Jewish or Christian mother, then he should have intercourse with her."
"33335","(33335) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If he has a mother from the People of the Book, then he may He covers her if he wants and forces her to wash."
"33336","(33336) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Judaism and Christianity are the same."
"33337","(33337) Abdullah bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurayh, he said: It was Abdullah He hates his nation as polytheists."
"33338","(33338) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Hilal narrated to us, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: He hated to He had intercourse with his polytheist mother until she submitted."
"33339","(33339) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, who said: Jabir bin Zaid was asked about the man. He buys a slave girl from captivity and has sexual intercourse with her? He said: No, until he teaches her to pray, and to remove the impurity and shave the pubic hair."
"33340","(33340) Shazan narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Bakr ibn Ma’iz, on the authority of Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym. He said: If a polytheist mother comes to you, do not come to her until she has delivered and bathed."
"33341","(33341) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, that a woman asked Aisha and she said: We have some of the Magians. And it is a festival for them, so they will make sacrifices for us. She said: As for what has been slaughtered for that day, do not eat, but eat of Their trees"
"33342","(33342) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Hakim narrated to us, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Abu Barza Al-Aslami, that he was He had Magi residents who used to give him gifts on Nowruz and the festival, and he said to his family: There was no fruit. So they accepted him, and nothing else was that, so they rejected him."
"33343","(33343) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Barza, who said: We were on a campaign, and we met people. Of the polytheists, so We caused them to abort from a group of theirs, and we fell into it, and we began to eat from it, and we were listening to it. The ignorant one said that whoever eats bread becomes fat. He said: When we ate that bread, he made one of us look at his kindness. Ghee"
"33344","(33344) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Wa’il and Ibrahim, who said: When the Muslims came, they killed those who fed him. The Magi from their cheese and their bread, and they ate and did not ask about any of that."
"33345","(33345) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He hated to eat what the Magians cooked in Their pots, and he did not see any harm in eating any of their food other than that: ghee, or cheese, or kamakh, or shiraz. Or milk."
"33346","(33346) Wakī’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in their stinginess and their weakness. And their milk."
"33347","(33347) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Do not eat the food of the Magians except Fruits"
"33348","(33348) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, they said: The polytheists were They bring ghee in their packages, and the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, buy it and the Muslims eat it. And we eat it."
"33349","(33349) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: We used to eat ghee, but we did not eat wheat flour, and we did not ask About the circumstances."
"33350","(33350) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I asked Ibrahim about mountain ghee, and he said: Arabica is more beloved to me than it. And I will eat from the mountains."
"33351","(33351) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Idris, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah al-Khushaniya, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, we are invading the enemy’s land, and we are in need of your vessels. So he said: Dispense with them as much as you can, and if you do not find them. Change it, wash it, eat from it and drink."
"33352","(33352) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We used to fight with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, the land of the polytheists. We are not prevented from eating from their utensils and drinking from their water vessels."
"33353","(33353) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naji Al-Hadrami that Hudhayf He asked for something to drink, and a painter brought him a bowl containing wine, so he washed it cleanly, then drank from it."
"33354","(33354) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Urwa bin Abdullah bin Qushayr Abi Al-Mahl, on the authority of Ibn Sirin said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to prevail over the polytheists and eat from Their vessels and they drink from their water vessels."
"33355","(33355) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, he said: We used to eat from Their vessels and we drink from their vessels."
"33356","(33356) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They used to hate the vessels of the infidels. If they do not find any of it, they wash it and cook in it."
"33357","(33357) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you need the pots and vessels of the polytheists So wash it and cook it."
"33358","(33358) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Al-Walid Al-Shinni narrated to us, saying: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about the powers of the Magi. He said: Wash it and cook in it."
"33359","(33359) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said regarding their burmah and their sheets: Wash them and cook in them. And he used it."
"33360","(33360) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Qubaisa ibn Halab, on the authority of his father, He said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about Christian food, and he said: Do not let the food you have lost mix in your heart. It contains Christianity. (Ibn Majah 2830, Musnad 859)"
"33361","(33361) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar that he did not see their food It's unfortunate"
"33362","(33362) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Qais bin Sakan al-Asadi, he said: Abd said God: You camped between Persia and the Nabataeans, so when you buy meat, whether its sacrifice was a Jew or a Christian. Then eat it, but if a Magian slaughters it, do not eat it."
"33363","(33363) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: {And the food of those who were given the Book is lawful for you} They said: sacrifices."
"33364","(33364) Waki’ told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Dharais Al-Asadi told us, he said: I asked Al-Sha’abi, I said: We are invading the land of Armenia is a Christian land, so what do you think of their sacrifices and food? He said: Whenever we invaded a land, we would ask about its people, and if they said: Jews or Christians, we would eat of their sacrifices and food. And We cooked in their utensils."
"33365","(33365) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If the treasure is found in the enemy’s land, then one-fifth is due in it. If it is found in an Arab land, zakat is due on it."
"33366","(33366) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of the one who witnessed al-Qadisiyah, who said: Among us is a man who takes a bath when water comes to him. Dirt from brick of gold, so Saad bin Abi Waqqas came and told him, and he said: Put it among the spoils of the Muslims."
"33367","(33367) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Qays Abd al-Rahman bin Tharwan, on the authority of Huzayl, who said: He came A man went to Abdullah and said: I found two hundred dirhams. Abdullah said: I do not see Muslims whose wealth has reached this level. I think it is zakat on ordinary wealth, so pay a fifth to the treasury and you get what remains."
"33368","(33368) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Shuaib narrated to me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said about the five pillars."
"33369","(33369) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid and Zakaria, on the authority of al-Sha’bi that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: Concerning the five pillars."
"33370","(33370) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted the like."
"33371","(33371) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub and Waki’, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, both of them, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah With the like of it, and He did not raise it."
"33372","(33372) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, that an Arab boy found a camel containing ten thousand Dirhams. Omar brought them and took five thousand from them and gave him eight thousand."
"33373","(33373) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, that a man found one thousand and five hundred dirhams in Kharbiyah, so he came. Ali, and he said: Pay five and you get three-fifths, and we will give you the remaining fifth."
"33374","(33374) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The rikaz is the ordinary treasure, and in it is the fifth."
"33375","(33375) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Omar Al-Dhabi, he said: While men with sabers softened, or stirred up the earth when they struck A treasure, and it was in the possession of Muhammad bin Jabir al-Rasibi, so he wrote about it to Adiyy, and Adiyy wrote to Omar bin Abdulaziz, so he wrote Omar, take the fifth from him."
"33376","(33376) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said about the five pillars."
"33377","(33377) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Kathir bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said about the five pillars."
"33378","(33378) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He decided The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the five pillars."
"33379","(33379) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about the five pillars. (Bukhari 1499 and Muslim 1332)"
"33380","(33380) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun that Omar appointed the people of Every garib is a qafiz and a dirham."
"33381","(33381) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Awn Muhammad bin Ubaidullah Al-Thaqafi, he said: Omar appointed Ali The people of Sawad owe each Jarib Aamir or Ghamir a qafiz and a dirham, and each Jarib al-Rutbah is charged five dirhams and five aqafs. And upon the person of the tree were ten dirhams and ten pounds, and upon the person of the vineyard were ten dirhams and ten pounds, and he did not He mentions palm trees."
"33382","(33382) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Awn Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi, he said: Omar put Ibn Al-Khattab Ali Al-Sawad is responsible for every land area that is full of water, or a large amount of dirhams and a large amount of food, and the gardens. He owes each garib ten dirhams and ten grains of food, and the price of moisture for each garib of land is five dirhams and five dirhams. He gave you ten dirhams of food, and ten dirhams for the vineyards, and did not impose anything on the palm trees. He made it dependent on the earth."
"33383","(33383) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Omar sent Uthman bin Hanif to He surveyed the land. He said: So Othman allocated ten dirhams to the one who planted the vineyard, and eight dirhams to the one who planted the palm trees. And on the spore of reeds there are six dirhams, meaning rutbi, and on the spore of land there are four dirhams, and on the spore of barley. Dramin"
"33384","(33384) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Majliz that Omar was placed on a palm tree. Eight dirhams."
"33385","(33385) Waki’ told us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam that Omar ibn Al-Khattab sent Uthman ibn Hanif On the black, so it was placed on every grazing and inhabiting person, and the water would receive him a dirham and a qafiz, meaning wheat and barley, and on Each grape vineyard is given ten, and the grape vine is given five."
"33386","(33386) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Aban bin Taghlib, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Omar, that he placed it on palm trees. A dirham is charged for the two raqlats, and a dirham for the Persian one."
"33387","(33387) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, who said: I came and behold, Omar was standing on Hudhayfah and Uthman ibn Hanif, and he said: You are afraid that you will burden the earth with what it cannot bear. Hudhayfah said: If you had wished, you could have weakened My land, he said: And Othman bin Hanif said: My land has carried a matter that is worthy of it, and there is not much bounty in it, so he said: Consider what you have, lest you have burdened the earth with what it cannot bear. (Bukhari 3700)"
"33388","(33388) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun, he said: Uthman ibn Hanif entered upon Omar. So I heard him say: Because I have added two dirhams to every head of the land, and to every land-grabber a dirham and a qafiz of food that will not harm them. That, and he did not argue with them, or speak something like it. He said: Yes. He said: So there were forty-eight on each head. So he made them fifty."
"33389","(33389) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Talha narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Sulaiman, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz to Abdul Hamid bin Abdul Rahman: I command you to embroider their land, meaning the people of Kufa, and not carry Devastation is upon the one who lives in it, and no one who lives in it is devastated, and when you see the devastation, take from it what you can bear and repair it until it is lived, and do not take from Al-Amer except the duty of the tax in providing comfort and tranquility to the people of the land, and I command you not to take from the tax anything except the weight of seventy There is no money, nor the fees of the miners, nor the melting of silver, nor the gifts of Nowruz and the festival, nor the price of newspapers, nor the fees for the holidays. Nor house rents, nor marriage dirhams, nor tax levied on any of the people of the earth who converted to Islam."
"33390","(33390) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Shibl, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, his saying {musawimin} teachers is partial. The tails of their horses have mold and wool on them."
"33391","(33391) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair bin Ishaq, who said: They were told on the Day of Badr. Be steadfast, for the angels have basked. They said: The first thing that was made of wool was that day."
"33392","(33392) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah ibn Mudharib al-Abdi, on the authority of Ali He said: The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were distinguished by their white wool on the Day of Badr."
"33393","(33393) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of a man from the descendants of Al-Zubayr, called: Yahya. Ibn Abbad, he said: Al-Zubair was wearing a yellow turban on the day of Badr, wearing it, so the angels descended on them, wearing yellow turbans."
"33394","(33394) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Abbad ibn Hamza, on the authority of al-Zubayr, in a similar manner."
"33395","(33395) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Suhaib, he said: Anas bin Malik narrated to us, he said: People from Arinah came to They invaded Medina, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: If you wish, you can go out to the camels of charity and drink. Of her urine and her milk, they acted and became healthy. He said: Then they turned against the shepherds and killed them, and they took water from the animals of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And they disbelieved after their conversion to Islam, so he sent to trace them and brought them, cut off their hands and feet and nailed them. They were helped and left in the heat until they died. (Muslim 1296; Abu Ali 3982)"
"33396","(33396) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something like that.\n(Muslim 1296. Tirmidhi 72)"
"33397","(33397) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: Whoever changes his religion, kill him."
"33398","(33398) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, that Muadh bin Jabal came to Abu Moses, and with him was a Jewish man, and he said: What is this? He said: This is a Jew who converted to Islam, then he apostatized, and he sought repentance from him. Abu Musa said two months, and Muadh said: I will not sit down until I behead him, according to the decree of God and the decree of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"33399","(33399) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, he said: He apostatized. Alqamah bin Ulathah, about his religion after the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Muslims fought him. He said: He refused to commit suicide. For peace, and Abu Bakr said: Nothing will be accepted from you except a shameful peace, or a disgraceful war. He said, and he said: And there is no peace. Shameful. He said: You bear witness that those who killed us will be in Paradise, and that those who killed you will be in Hell, and you will bear witness that those who killed us will be in Paradise, and that those who killed you will be in Hell, and you will take note of those we killed, and there will be no equal. They killed you, so they chose a shameful ladder."
"33400","(33400) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, who said: A delegation came Asad invaded and went to Abu Bakr to ask him for peace, so Abu Bakr gave them a choice between the final war. And the shameful ladder. He said: They said: We have known this glorious war, so what is the shameful ladder? He said: Abu Bakr: You provide for the ring and the livestock, and you leave people following the tails of camels until God sees the successor to His Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and the Muslims, there is a matter for which they will excuse you, and you will write down our dead, and there will be no compensation for your dead, and our dead in Jinnah and kill you in the Fire, and you will return what you afflicted from us and we will take away what we afflicted from you. So Omar said, and he said: You have seen a vision. And We will advise you, as for them performing the halqa and the ankles, then yes, that is what you have seen. As for them leaving people who follow them... The tails of camels until God sees the successor of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Muslims a matter for which they will excuse them, so yes. What you saw. As for us taking spoils of what we took from them, and they returning what they took from us, then yes, what you saw was good. As for their killing in Fire, and We killed them in Paradise, so what you saw was good. As for us not making up for their dead, what you saw was good. And as for them being destroyed. They killed us, but no, those who killed us were killed by the command of God, so no blood money is owed to them, so the people continue on that matter."
"33401","(33401) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Alqamiya bin Ulathah apostatized, so he sent Abu A virgin to his wife and his child, and she said: If your mother is an unbeliever, then neither I nor my child have been an unbeliever, so he mentioned that. To Al-Shaabi, and he said: This is what he did to them, meaning the people of apostasy."
"33402","(33402) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, something similar to it and adding to it: Then he committed a misdemeanor. To embrace Islam during the time of Omar, so he converted to Islam and returned to his wife as he had been."
"33403","(33403) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Abu Bakr said: If they withhold from me a They gave it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, because of my struggle with them, then he recited: (And Muhammad is only a messenger. Messengers have passed away before him) to The last verse"
"33404","(33404) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, he said: Omar said: By the one who is my soul. By his own hand, if Abu Bakr had obeyed us, we would have disbelieved in one morning when they asked for a reduction in the zakat, but he refused them, and said: If they had denied me a right, I would have fought against them."
"33405","(33405) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Jews and Christians will not live among you. Your fates. Whoever among them submits to Islam and then backs away, do not strike anyone except his neck."
"33406","(33406) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, who said: Amer narrated to us that Anas bin Malik He told him that a group of Bakr bin Wa’il had abandoned Islam and joined the polytheists and were killed in the fighting. When I came to Omar bin Al-Khattab, with the opening of cover, said: What did the group of Bakr bin Wa’il do? He said: I said, “I mentioned it in another hadith to distract him from mentioning them.” He said: What did the group of Bakr bin Wa’il do? He said: I said: Kill them, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: If I had taken them safely, it would have been more beloved. To me, upon which the sun rose, yellow and white. He said: I said: O Commander of the Faithful, and their way would not have been if I took them to death, a people who had abandoned Islam and joined polytheism. He said: I was advising that they should enter through the gate from which they left. And if they do that, I will accept that from them, and if they refuse, I will put them in prison."
"33407","(33407) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Saeed bin Hayyan, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dhani, he said: Abu Al-Tufayl told me, he said: I was in the army that Ali bin Abi Talib sent to Banu Najiya. So we came to them and found them in three groups. He said: Then our leader said to a group of them: Who are you? They said: We are a Christian people and we converted to Islam, so we remained steadfast in our Islam. He said: Retire, then he said to the second: What are you? They said, “We are a Christian people. We did not see a religion better than ours, so we remained steadfast in it.” He said, “Stay away.” Then he said to another group: What are you? They said, “We are a Christian people,” but they refused. So he said to his companions: “When I wipe my head three times.” They were harsh on them, so they did so, killing the fighters and taking them captive. The offspring, so I brought the offspring to Ali, and Musqalah ibn Hubira came and bought them for two hundred thousand, so he brought them for a hundred thousand. To Ali, but he refused to accept, so Masqaliya set off with his cloaks, and Masqaliya went to them, freed them and joined Muawiyah. Then it was said to Ali: Don’t you take the offspring? He said: No, so he did not offer it to them."
"33408","(33408) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Alaqah, Omar bin Al-Khattab sent a convoy, and they found a man among the Muslims who had converted to Christianity after his conversion to Islam, so they killed him. Omar was informed of that, and he said: Did you invite him to Islam? They said: No. He said: Indeed, I disavow his blood before God."
"33409","(33409) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibn Ubaid Ibn Al-Abras, on the authority of Ali Ibn Abi Talib that He brought a man who was a Christian and converted to Islam, then he converted to Christianity. Omar asked him about his words, and he said to him, so Ali stood up to him and kicked him. By his foot, he said: Then the people rose up to him and beat him until they killed him."
"33410","(33410) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Qaboos ibn Al-Mukhariq, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali sent Muhammad ibn Abu Bakr was the Emir of Egypt, so he wrote to Ali asking him about his heretics, some of whom worshiped the sun and the moon, and some of them Whoever worships other than that, and among them is he who claims Islam, then he wrote to him and commanded him among the heretics to kill whoever he was. He claims Islam, and leaves the rest of them to worship whatever they want."
"33411","(33411) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudharib, who said: A man came out He rode his horse and passed by the mosque of Banu Hanif, where he prayed, and their imam read to them in the words of the false Muslim. So Ibn Masoud came and told him, so he sent for them and brought them, and they asked for repentance from them, and they repented, except for Abdullah Ibn Al-Nawahih, for he He said to him: O Abdullah, had I not heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Were it not for the fact that you were a Messenger, I would have beheaded you. As for today, you are not a messenger. O Kharsha, get up and behead him. He got up and beheaded him. (Abu Dawud 2756. Ahmad 384)"
"33412","(33412) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Qays, who said: A man came to Ibn Masoud. He said: I passed by the mosque of Banu Hanifa and I heard their imam reciting the revelations that God had revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so I heard him say: The women who grind grinding, then the kneaders, kneading, so the bakers, then bread, then the ones who refrigerate, then the morsels, a morsel. He said: So Abdullah sent and brought to them seventy and a hundred men of Muslim religion, their imam Abdullah Ibn al-Nawahih, and he ordered that So he was killed, then he looked at the rest of them and said: We are not the slaughterers of Satan. The rest of the people were deported to the Levant, perhaps. May God protect them from the plague. (Abdul Razzaq 18708)"
"33413","(33413) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: Amr ibn al-Aas wrote to Omar ibn al-Khattab that a man changed into disbelief after believing, so ‘Umar wrote to him: Seek repentance from him. He repents, so accept from him. Otherwise, behead him."
"33414","(33414) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ubaid al-Amiri, on the authority of his father, he said: There were people They received gifts and provision and prayed with the people, and they worshiped idols in secret, so Ali bin Abi Talib was brought to them. So he put them in the mosque, or he said in the prison, then he said: O people, what do you see in a people who used to take Do you not have the gift and the provision and worship these idols? The people said: Kill them. He said: No, but do to them as they did to our father Abraham, so he burned them with fire."
"33415","(33415) Al-Bakrawi told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, who said: Umar ibn Abdul Aziz wrote about a Christian people who had apostatized. So it was written that you should seek investigation from them, but if they repent, otherwise, kill them."
"33416","(33416) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding the apostate, he is asked to repent, and if he repents, he is left, even if he refuses. He was killed"
"33417","(33417) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr bin Dinar informed me; Concerning a man who disbelieves after his belief, he said: I heard Ubaid bin Umair say: He will be killed."
"33418","(33418) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: He said: A gift in a person who disbelieves after his belief: He is called. To Islam, if he refuses, he will be killed."
"33419","(33419) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Barda, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Musa said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me and Muadh to Yemen. He said: He came to me one day, and with me A Jew who was a Muslim turned from Islam to Judaism and said: I will not come down until you have beheaded him. Hajjaj said: His leaders told me that Abu Musa prayed for forty days."
"33420","(33420) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Shayban al-Nahwi, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Thawban narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in his last sermon: This The village, meaning the city, is not suitable for two religions, so whoever is Christian converts to Islam, then converts, behead him."
"33421","(33421) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays, on the authority of someone who heard Ibrahim say: The apostate shall be asked to repent. Whenever he backs away"
"33422","(33422) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Some of our companions narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of the ruling, who said: The apostate shall be repented whenever he apostatizes."
"33423","(33423) Shababā told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Utbah, he said: There were some people from the Hanifites who were with the lying Muslim, and they were distorting his hadiths and distorting them, so Ibn Masoud, so Ibn Masoud wrote to Uthman, and Uthman wrote to him, saying: I invite them to Islam, so whoever among them bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he chose faith over disbelief, so accept that from them and leave their way. If They refused, so cut off the necks of them, so they asked for forgiveness. Some of them repented, but others refused, so cut off the necks of those who refused. (Abdul Razzaq 18707)"
"33424","(33424) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, who said: When he came to Omar, he opened the cover and cover. From the land of Basra, he asked them: Are there any Westerners? They said: A man from among the Muslims who joined the polytheists, so we captured him. He said: What? What did you do to him? They said: We killed him. He said: Why did you not bring him into a house, close a door on him, and feed him every day? A loaf of bread, then you asked him to leave for three days, and if he repented, otherwise you would kill him. Then he said: Oh God, I did not bear witness, nor did I command, nor did I approve when he informed me. Or he said: When he informed me."
"33425","(33425) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, on the authority of Uthman, he said: He should be asked to repent. The apostate three times."
"33426","(33426) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He will be called to Islam three times. Bitter, if my father is struck, he will be beheaded."
"33427","(33427) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ali, he said: The apostate must be asked to repent three times."
"33428","(33428) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Ali said: The apostate must be asked to repent three times, and if he returns, he will be killed."
"33429","(33429) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of someone who heard Ibn Umar say: The apostate must be asked to repent three times."
"33430","(33430) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, who said: A worker wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz from Yemen: A man was a Jew and converted to Islam, then he converted to Judaism and left Islam, so Umar wrote to him to invite him to Islam. If he converts to Islam, then go on his way, and if he refuses, then call on the wood, then call him. If he refuses, then lie on it, then Call him, and if he refuses, then bind him, then put the war on his heart, then call him, and if he returns, then leave him on his way, and if he refuses So he killed him, and when the letter came, he did that to him until he put the war on his heart, then he called him and he converted to Islam and let him go."
"33431","(33431) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: The apostate must be asked to repent three times. If he returns, otherwise he will be killed."
"33432","(33432) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amer and al-Hakam, who said: Concerning a Muslim man who abandons Islam and goes to the enemy’s land. They said: His wife shall observe the waiting period of three menstrual cycles if she is menstruating, and if If she does not menstruate, then three months, and if she is pregnant, she may give birth, and his inheritance will be divided between his wife. And she inherited from him among the Muslims, then she can be married off if she wishes, and if he returns and repents before her waiting period ends, then they remain with him. Their marriage"
"33433","(33433) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a man who committed polytheism and joined the land of polytheism. He said: Do not marry his wife, and Hammad said: Marry his wife."
"33434","(33434) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ali, that he brought an imported Al-Ijali had apostatized, and Islam was offered to him, but he refused. He said: So he killed him and placed his inheritance among his Muslim heirs."
"33435","(33435) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of the ruling that Ali divided the apostate’s inheritance among his heirs from Muslims"
"33436","(33436) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin Juma’, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If the apostate apostatizes, his children inherit from him."
"33437","(33437) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir ibn Hazim, who said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote about an inheritance. The apostate belongs to his Muslim heirs and not to his religious people."
"33438","(33438) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar and Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Sabbah, who said: I heard Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab say: The apostate. We inherit from them, but they do not inherit from us."
"33439","(33439) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa ibn Abi Kathir, who said: I asked Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab about an inheritance. Is the apostate to be joined when he is killed? He said: And what is connected to him. He said: He and his heirs inherit. He said: We will inherit from them, but they will not inherit from us."
"33440","(33440) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He will be killed and his inheritance will be Among his Muslim heirs."
"33441","(33441) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Sha’bi and al-Hakam, who said: His inheritance shall be divided between His wife and heir are among the Muslims."
"33442","(33442) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali, in The apostate: you will be tortured, and Hammad said: you will be killed."
"33443","(33443) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman and Waki` told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: Women should not be killed if they abandon Islam, but rather they should be imprisoned and invited to Islam and forced to do so."
"33444","(33444) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ regarding the apostate, he said: Do not kill him."
"33445","(33445) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Do not be killed."
"33446","(33446) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Women should not be killed if they turn away from Islam. Islam, but they will be called to Islam, but they will be taken captive and made slaves for the Muslims, but they will not be killed."
"33447","(33447) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Why does a woman abandon Islam? He said: You will not be killed, you will be imprisoned."
"33448","(33448) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Do not be killed."
"33449","(33449) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning an apostate: she must be asked to be repented, if she repents, otherwise she will be killed."
"33450","(33450) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, that the mother of a man’s child was from She apostatized from the Muslims, so he sold her to people other than her religion for the price of Al-Jandal."
"33451","(33451) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, in the mirror, abandoning Islam. He said: She must be asked for repentance, so if she repents, otherwise she will be killed."
"33452","(33452) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, in a similar manner."
"33453","(33453) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: The people of knowledge used to say: If the warrior is safe, he will not be taken. With something that happened to him during the war, unless it was something that happened to him before that."
"33454","(33454) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; Concerning a man who crosses the punishment, then comes repentant. He said: The punishment will be imposed on him."
"33455","(33455) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who commits a crime and catches up with the enemy and they are safe. He said: They believe unless something becomes known. With his own eyes, it will be taken from them and returned to his companions, and as for him, it will be taken for what the jinn had before he joined them."
"33456","(33456) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, about a man who injured someone, then he went out to fight, then he sought He was safe, so he was safe. He said: The punishment that he had inflicted on him will be meted out."
"33457","(33457) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man, if he crosses the road and commits a sin, then returns repentant, the punishment will be imposed on him, and his repentance is between him and his Lord."
"33458","(33458) Abu Asama told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: Qays bin Saad told me that Ata used to say: If a man from among the Muslims killed another man, then disbelieved and joined the polytheists, and was among them, then returned repentant, it would be accepted. He repented from his polytheism, and retaliation was imposed on him, even if he joined the polytheists and was not killed, so he disbelieved, then fought Muslims, and he killed one of them, then he came repentant, and he was accepted from him, and nothing was wrong with him."
"33459","(33459) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, who said: Harith bin Badr al-Tamimi was one of the people of Basra. He spread corruption on earth and fought, so he spoke to Al-Hasan bin Ali, Ibn Jafar, Ibn Abbas and others from Quraysh, and they spoke to Ali. He did not believe him, so Sa`id bin Qais al-Hamdani came and spoke to him, so Sa`id went to Ali and succeeded him in his house. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, what do you say about one who wages war against God and His Messenger and strives to spread corruption on earth, then he recited, “The recompense of those who They fight Allah and His Messenger) until he recited all of the verses, and Sa`id said, “Have you seen the one who repents before We are able to defeat him?” Then Ali said: I say as he said and it will be accepted from him. He said: Indeed, Harithah bin Badr repented before he was defeated, so he was sent Then he brought him in and made him safe, and wrote a letter for him. Harithah said:\nShall I not inform Hamdan if I meet her?\nBy the age of your father, Hamdan is pious.\nMy head has turned gray and our dreams have diminished\n\nPeace, for no enemy who reproaches her will be safe.\nGod and He decides by the Book His fiancé\nThe thunders of the rains and their lightnings around us\nIndeed, our souls become sweet with desires.\n\nAnd we will leave the afterlife as we will never taste it.\nIbn Amir said: I narrated this hadith to Ibn Jafar, and he said: We were more deserving of these verses than Hamdan."
"33460","(33460) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ash`ath, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Ali: something similar to it, and he did not mention poetry in it."
"33461","(33461) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who claimed that a man from Murad prayed, so when Abu Musa greeted him, He got up and said: This is the place of the repentant one who seeks refuge. He said: Woe to you, what is yours? He said: I am so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, Al-Muradi, and I was I fought against God and His Messenger and strived to spread corruption throughout the land. This is when I came, and I had repented before I was defeated. He said: Then Abu Musa is the place in which he stood, then he said: This is so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, Al-Muradi: And he fought against God and His Messenger, and he fought hard. wreaking havoc on earth, and indeed he had repented before it was possible for him to do so, so if he is truthful then the path of one who is truthful is A liar, God caught him for his sin. He said: So he went out among the people, so he went away and was saved, then he came back and was killed."
"33462","(33462) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: {It is only a reward Those who wage war against God and His Messenger and strive to spread corruption on earth - that they be killed, or be crucified, or have their hands cut off. And their feet on opposite sides} until he concluded the verse, saying: If a man fights and kills and takes the money, his hand and foot will be cut off on opposite sides. And he was crucified, and if he was killed and did not take the money, he was killed, and if he took the money and did not kill, his hand and foot were cut off from opposite sides. He did not kill and did not take the money. He was exiled."
"33463","(33463) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, in these verses: {The recompense of those They fight Allah and His Messenger.} He said: If he kills and takes the money, he will be killed, and if he takes the money and fears the path, he will be crucified, and if he kills and does not He is considered to be killed, but if he takes the money, he is not considered to be killed, and if he commits corruption, he is exiled."
"33464","(33464) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Abraham: {The recompense of those who wage war against Allah is only And His Messenger} said: If he goes out and fears the path and takes the money, his hand and foot will be cut off on opposite sides, and if he fears the path and does not If he takes the money, he will be exiled, and if he kills, he will be killed, and if he fears the path and takes the money and kills, he will be crucified."
"33465","(33465) Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: It was narrated, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, he said: Whoever fights will be defeated. A warrior, and Saeed said: If he injures blood, he will be killed, and if he injures blood or property, he will be crucified, for crucifixion is worse, and if he injures money and does not If he pours blood, his hands and feet are cut off, according to His saying {or their hands and feet are cut off on opposite sides}. Then if he repents, then I repent in this regard. Between him and God, and the punishment will be imposed on him."
"33466","(33466) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his commanders, on the authority of Muwarriq al-Ijli, who said: If the warrior takes Then he was brought to the Imam, and if he took the money and did not kill, he will be cut off and not killed, and if he took the money and killed, he will be killed and crucified, and if If he did not take the money and did not kill, he would not be cut off, and if he did not take the money and did not kill and disobeyed the Muslims, he would be banished."
"33467","(33467) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The warrior is polytheism."
"33468","(33468) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, they said: The imam has a choice. The warrior"
"33469","(33469) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He recited these verses: “The recompense of those who wage war against Allah is only And His Messenger} He said: That is up to the Imam."
"33470","(33470) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: The Sultan is the guardian who kills whoever fights. Religion: And if he kills a man’s brother and father, then there is no way for anyone who fights religion and strives to spread corruption on earth, meaning without Sultan, and do not neglect the punishments after they reach the imam, for establishing them is part of the Sunnah."
"33471","(33471) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab regarding the warrior: If it is raised To the Imam and he can do with him whatever he wants."
"33472","Abu Abdul Rahman Buqi bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying:\n(33472) Sa’id bin Amir told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hurr, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Because he goes and returns the person most beloved to him, and he asked him and wanted a brother of his to fight him."
"33473","(33473) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: No sandals or sandals should be buried with the dead person."
"33474","(33474) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The fur and socks should be removed from the murdered person. And the two socks and the socks are complementary, so they are left on."
"33475","(33475) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Al-Eizar bin Harith Al-Abdi, who said: Zaid bin Suhan said: No. Remove from me any garment except the socks."
"33476","(33476) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, who said: Whenever Muhammad was asked about The martyr Yaghusl narrated on the authority of Hujr ibn Adiy when he was killed by Mu’awiyah. He said: Hujr said: Do not release iron from him and do not wash him. I have shed blood, bury me in my bonds and my blood, for I will meet Muawiyah on the road tomorrow."
"33477","(33477) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I heard Yahya bin Abbas telling Qais Ibn Abi Hazim, on the authority of Ammar Ibn Yasser, that he said: Bury me in my clothes, for I am quarreling."
"33478","(33478) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbas, on the authority of Ammar bin Yasser. Like it"
"33479","(33479) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul bin Rashid Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Al-Eizar bin Harith Al-Abdi, he said: Zaid bin Suhan said on the Day of the Camel: Throw me in the ground as a sand, and do not wash away the blood from me, and do not remove from me Any clothing except for the socks, for I am a pilgrim. I perform pilgrimage."
"33480","(33480) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar and Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Al-Muthanna Al-Abdi, Sufyan said: On the authority of A man, on the authority of Zaid bin Suhan, and Mas’ar said, on the authority of Mus’ab, on the authority of Zaid bin Suhan that he said on the Day of the Camel: Bury us, and what The wealth was afflicted by our blood."
"33481","(33481) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: Saad bin Ubaid, the reciter, said on the Day of Al-Qadisiyah: We will meet the enemy tomorrow, God willing, and we will be martyred, so do not wash away our blood. We will not be shrouded except in a garment that was on us."
"33482","(33482) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Thabit bin Ammarah narrated to us, saying: I heard Ghanim bin Qais saying: It is said: Al-Shahid He will be buried in his clothes and not washed."
"33483","(33483) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that a man from Abdullah’s companions was killed by the enemy, so we buried him in his clothes."
"33484","(33484) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the dead person is raised, he is buried in his clothes. And when it is raised and with it a spear is done with it what would be done with anything else."
"33485","(33485) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Uzza, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who was killed by thieves. He said: He should be buried in his clothes and not washed."
"33486","(33486) Shababā told us, saying: Laith bin Saad informed us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik said that Jabir bin Abdullah told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray over anyone who had been killed and they were not washed."
"33487","(33487) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If the martyr is in battle, he is buried in his clothes and not washed."
"33488","(33488) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded Hamza when He was martyred and washed."
"33489","(33489) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, that Hanzala ibn al-Rahib was purified by the angels."
"33490","(33490) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of a murdered person, if he had a period of mourning, he should be washed."
"33491","(33491) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan, they said: Al-Shahid He is washed. No one dies except a non-mahram person."
"33492","(33492) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Umar was washed, shrouded, and embalmed."
"33493","(33493) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed Hamza (Abu Dawud 427. Daraqutni 78)"
"33494","(33494) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. He greeted Hamza and said “Allahu Akbar” nine times. (Bazzar 1796, Hakim 197)"
"33495","(33495) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adi, on the authority of Ata’ that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May peace and blessings be upon those killed at Badr."
"33496","(33496) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: Amer was asked: Should the funeral prayer be offered over the martyr? He said: He is more worthy than the one upon whom the martyr’s blessings be upon him."
"33497","(33497) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ishaq bin Sulaiman Al-Shaybani told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Amr bin He refused to read it, he said: A letter came to us from Omar ibn al-Khattab stating that some people are taking from this money and striving for the sake of God, then They disagree, but they do not argue. Whoever of them does that, we have more right to his money, even if we take from him what he took. Abu Ishaq: So I went to Sir bin Amr and said: Don’t you see what Amr bin Abi Qurayh told me about, and I told him about, and he said: He spoke the truth, the Book of Omar was brought to him."
"33498","(33498) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The wealth of the prisoner and his wife shall be waived. Until they both surrender, or die."
"33499","(33499) Muhammad bin Musaab narrated to us, he said: Al-Awza’i narrated to me, he said: I asked Al-Zuhri about the captive in the enemy’s land when. He married his wife, and he said: Do not marry her as long as you know that he is alive."
"33500","(33500) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of a prisoner in the hands of the enemy, if he gives a gift, or bequeaths a bequest and bequeaths a third of it, then it is permissible."
"33501","(33501) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: A prisoner is not permitted to take his property except One-third"
"33502","(33502) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: He is most in need of an inheritance. And he is a captive."
"33503","(33503) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Regarding the prisoner’s inheritance, he said: He is in need of his inheritance."
"33504","(33504) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The captive inherits."
"33505","(33505) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: He inherits."
"33506","(33506) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of someone who heard Abraham say: The prisoner does not inherit."
"33507","(33507) Ibn Al-Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Al-Musayyab, who said: He does not inherit. A prisoner in the hands of the enemy."
"33508","(33508) Affan narrated to us, he said: Wahib narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, that he was not inherited. The captive"
"33509","(33509) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He should not be taken into account for what he did there. It means the prisoner is held captive and speaks."
"33510","(33510) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: Good news was given to Omar. With open mouth, he prostrated."
"33511","(33511) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah, that Abu Bakr came to him and prostrated."
"33512","(33512) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awn Al-Thaqafi Muhammad bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of a man who did not It is called: When Abu Bakr came to him and opened the dove, he prostrated."
"33513","(33513) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: I saw Ali when the newborn was brought, he prostrated. He prostrated with gratitude."
"33514","(33514) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays al-Hamdani, on the authority of a sheikh of theirs who called me Abu Musa, he said: I testified that Ali prostrated when the conceived man was brought."
"33515","(33515) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Ubaid al-Ijli narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Mu’min al-Wathili, he said: I witnessed Ali coming. He was conceived and prostrated."
"33516","(33516) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awn al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. A man passed by him and he prostrated. So did Abu Bakr and Omar."
"33517","(33517) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: A short man passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he prostrated with a prostration of gratitude, and said: Praise be to God who has not made me like an adulterer."
"33518","(33518) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Bingash prostrated and said: Ask God for well-being."
"33519","(33519) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I narrated that Abu Bakr prostrated with the prostration of gratitude, and Abraham was He hated her."
"33520","(33520) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The prostration of gratitude is a supplication."
"33521","(33521) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Kalbi told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When marriage was revealed Zainab Zayd ibn Harithah set off until he asked permission to come to Zainab. He said: Then Zainab said: What do I have to do with Zayd? He said: So he sent To her, I am the messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So she gave her permission, so he gave her the good news that God had married her to his Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: So I fell down and prostrated, thanking God."
"33522","(33522) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: He used to hate his prostration with joy, and he says There is no bowing or prostration in it."
"33523","(33523) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Zarbiyy narrated to us, saying: Al-Rayyan bin Sabriah Al-Hanafi narrated to us that He witnessed the day of Nahrawan. He said: I was among those who extracted the mammal and was given the good news of it to Ali before he reached the end. He said: So we came to him and he was prostrating and rejoicing in him."
"33524","(33524) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Ubaidy informed us, on the authority of Qays ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa`sa`a, on the authority of Sa`d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of his grandfather Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, who said: I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace while he was prostrating. When he left, I said: O Messenger of God, you prolonged your prostration. He said: I prostrated out of gratitude to God for it. He caused me to fail in my nation."
"33525","(33525) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, who said: A man asked a gift about a man whom Daylam had captured, so they took From God’s covenant and covenant that they would send him, so if he is sent to them with a ransom they have named, then he is innocent, but if he is not sent To them it was his covenant and covenant that he would return to them, but he did not find it, and he was insolvent. He said he would fulfill the covenant, so he said : They are people of polytheism, so Ata’ refused except to fulfill his covenant."
"33526","(33526) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Jami` ibn Abi Rashid, on the authority of Maimun ibn Mihran, who said: Three people will be brought to The righteous and the immoral: the kin connects the person whether she is righteous or immoral, and trusts lead her to the righteous and the immoral, and the covenant is fulfilled. It is for the righteous and the ungodly."
"33527","(33527) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, he said: Abu Al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: Hudhayfah bin narrated to us. Al-Yaman, he said: Nothing prevented me from witnessing Badr except that I and Abu Husayl went out. He said: Then the infidels of Quraysh captured us. They said: You want Muhammad. We said: We do not want him. We only want Medina. So they took from us God’s covenant and covenant. We will go to Medina and not fight with him. So we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him the news, and he said: They departed, we banished them, and we seek God’s help against them. (Muslim 1414. Ahmad 395)"
"33528","(33528) Issa ibn Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abd ibn Abi Lubab that he said regarding the servant if Depart to enemy land: He will not come until he has taken refuge in Harz and returned to his master."
"33529","(33529) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shibl, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If the servant is left to the enemy’s land, he will be absolved of responsibility.\n(Ahmad 357, Hamidi 806)"
"33530","(33530) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of Al-Sha’biy, on the authority of Jarir, he said: With every last Infidelity"
"33531","(33531) Waki’ told us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Jarir, he said: If he stays to the enemy His blood has been shed, meaning to the house of war."
"33532","(33532) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: Either A slave who was sent to the enemy's land has been absolved of his duty. (Tabarani 2360, Ahmad 365)"
"33533","(33533) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his followers, he said: Ali was asked about letters. He was taken captive by the enemy, then a man from among the Muslims bought him, he said: And he said: If his master wishes to let him destroy him, then he will be with him as he is. He remained to communicate with him and he would be loyal to him, even if he disliked that, he would be with the one who bought him in this state."
"33534","(33534) Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, he said: Abbad told us, he said: Makhoul told me, he said in the offices of someone who was captured by the enemy. So a man from the merchants bought it and wrote to him, saying: He will do the first thing you write to, then he will do the last thing you wrote."
"33535","(33535) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr informed us, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He came to meet Omar from Bahrain. He said: I came to him and prayed the evening prayer with him. When he saw me, I greeted him, and he said: What? I brought it. I said: I brought five hundred thousand. He said: Do you know what you are saying? He said: I brought five hundred thousand. He said: I said: a hundred thousand. And a hundred thousand and a hundred thousand and a hundred thousand and a hundred thousand until he counted five. He said: You are sleepy, go back to your house and sleep, then go out in the morning. Ali, he said: So I went out to him, and he said: I did not bring it. I said: Five hundred thousand. He said: Good. I said: Good, I only know That, he said: So he said to the people: A lot of money has been presented to me, so if you wish, we can count it for you, and if you wish, we can We will give you every measure, and a man said: O Commander of the Faithful, I saw these foreigners writing down a record. And they give to the people in exchange for it. He said: So he recorded the Diwan and allocated for the Muhajireen five thousand five thousand and for the Ansar four thousand. Four thousand, and he allocated twelve thousand for the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"33536","(33536) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, who said: The obligation of ‘Umar for the family of Badr was an Arab among them and their master, five thousand five thousand, and he said: I will certainly prefer them over anyone else."
"33537","(33537) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d that Omar bin Al-Khattab made an obligation for the family of Badr was for six thousand six thousand, and he assigned for the mothers of the believers ten thousand ten thousand, so he preferred Aisha with two thousand. Due to the love of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for the two Sabbaths, Safiyah bint Huyya and Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith, it is obligatory There are six thousand, and an allotment for the women of the believers in a thousand, of which a thousand is Umm Abd."
"33538","(33538) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Qais, on the authority of his father, who said: I brought Ali as a cousin of mine. So I said: O Commander of the Faithful, make an assumption for this. He said: Four, meaning four hundred. He said: I said: Four hundred is not sufficient. Something, increase the two hundred that the people increased. He said: That is for him. He said: He had increased the people by two hundred."
"33539","(33539) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Abu Ma’shar told me, he said: Omar, the servant of Ghufari and others told me, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, money came to him from the two seas, and Abu Bakr said: Whoever has a Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If you have anything or a gift, let him stand, let him take it.” Then Jabir stood up and said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: If money came to me from the two seas, I would give you such and such three times, and he urged me with his hand, and he said Abu Bakr told him: “Get up and take it with your hand.” Then he took it and saw five hundred dirhams. He said: “Count it to a thousand,” and he divided it among the people. Ten dirhams, ten dirhams, and he said: These are only promises that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, promised to the people.\n2. Until the next year, more money came to him than that money, so he divided among the people twenty dirhams and twenty dirhams. And some of it remained, so he distributed five dirhams to the servants, and said: You have servants who serve you and treat you. To you, so We acquiesced to them, and they said: If I had given preference to the Muhajireen and the Ansar, I would have preceded them, and would have taken their place in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: The reward of those is upon God. Indeed, this livelihood for the poorest in it is better than the wealth.He said: So he fulfilled his mandate until the thirteenth year of Jumada al-Akhirah, during the nights of which he remained satisfied, and he died. May God protect him\n3. So Omar bin Al-Khattab worked and conquered the conquests and money came to him, so he said: Abu Bakr had an opinion about this matter, and he decided on it. Another opinion: I do not make whoever fought the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as one who fought with him, so it is an obligation for the Muhajireen and Ansar among those who Five thousand five thousand attended Badr, and Islam was made obligatory for those who had it, just like the Islam of the people of Badr, who did not witness Badr for four days. One thousand four thousand.\n4. He stipulated that the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were twelve thousand, except for Safiyya and Jurayyat. When there were six thousand, six thousand, but they refused to come, so he said\n To them: It was only made obligatory for them for migration, so they said: It was only made obligatory for them for their place from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We had the same, so Omar knew that and assigned them twelve thousand twelve thousand.\n5. He allocated twelve thousand to Al-Abbas, four thousand to Asama bin Zayd, and three thousand to Abdullah bin Omar. He said: O my father, why did you increase him for a thousand more than what his father had of virtue that my father did not have, and what he had that I did not have?He said: The father of Asama was more beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than your father, and Asama was more beloved to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon you, and he assigned five thousand five thousand to Hassan and Hussein, whom he joined to their fathers because of their place in the country. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.\n6. He allotted two thousand for the children of the Muhajireen and Ansar, so Omar bin Abi Sallam passed by him and said: Increase it by a thousand. So he said to him: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Jahsh: His father did not have what our father did not have, and he did not have what we did not have, so he said: I I allotted to him two thousand Salamahs for his father, and I increased for him a thousand Salamahs from his mother, Umm Sallama, if you had a mother like his mother. I increased you a thousand.\n7. He allotted eight hundred and eight hundred for the people of Mecca and for the people, so Talhah bin Ubaid Allah came to him with his brother Uthman, and he allotted for him Eight hundred, then Al-Nadr ibn Anas passed by him, and Omar said: Allocate for him two thousand, and Talha said: I brought you something like it, so you allotted for him. Eight hundred dirhams, and I allocated two thousand for this man, and he said: This man’s father met me on the day of Uhud and said to him: What did the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, do? May God bless him and grant him peace. I said: I do not see him except that he has been killed.He drew his sword and broke its sheath and said: If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has been killed, then God is living and does not die. So he fought until he was killed, and this man was grazing sheep in such-and-such a place.\n8. So Omar began the beginning of his caliphate until it was the age of twenty-three. Hajj of that year reached him that the people were saying: If the Amir had died... Believers: We went to so-and-so and he pledged allegiance to him, but if Abu Bakr had pledged allegiance to him, then he wanted to talk about it."
"33540","(33540) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Ata Abdullah was Six thousand"
"33541","(33541) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Omar’s obligation For the people of Badr, there are six thousand, six thousand, and a similar amount was prescribed for the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"33542","(33542) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Sami’, on the authority of Ammar al-Dhani, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad said that Omar gave Salman six thousand."
"33543","(33543) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Amr bin Salma al-Hamdani, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Ubaidah Al-Salmani, he said: Omar said to me: How much do you think a man’s giving is sufficient for him? He said: I said: Such and such. He said: Because I stayed to make the man’s contribution four thousand: a thousand for his weapons, a thousand for his expenses, and a thousand for him to put in his house. And a thousand such-and-such. I think he said to his horse."
"33544","(33544) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of a sheikh of theirs, who said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab says: If I remain until Qabil, I will join the bottom of the emigrants in two thousand two thousand."
"33545","(33545) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Saad told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab says: If I were to remain until Qabil, I would join the last parts of the people with their first ones, and I would make them one single statement."
"33546","(33546) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qays narrated to us, saying: My mother, Umm al-Hakam narrated to me, that Ali joined her in Hundreds of gifts"
"33547","(33547) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Huwairith that Omar assigned Abbas seven thousand, And for Aisha and Hafsah, ten thousand, and for Umm Salma, Umm Habib, Maimunah, and Suda, eight thousand, eight. Thousands, and he assigned to Juwayriyah and Safiyya six thousand six thousand, and he assigned half of what was assigned to Safiyya bint Abd al-Muttalib So, Umm Salama and her companions sent to Uthman ibn Affan and said to him: Speak to Umar about us, for he has favored us. Aisha and Hafsiya. Then Othman came to Omar and said: Your mothers are telling you: Be equal between us, do not give preference to one of us over the other. So he said: If you live until the next year, you will add two thousand to the next year. When the next year came, he made Aisha and Hafsa twelve. One thousand twelve thousand, and He made Umm Salamah and Umm Habibah among ten thousand, ten thousand, and He made two pure ones among them. And his slaves were eight thousand, eight thousand, so when they saw that, they remained silent about it."
"33548","(33548) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: My father told me that Omar bin Al-Khattab made an obligation for Jubayr bin A feeder and his servants are four thousand four thousand."
"33549","(33549) Muhammad Ibn Bakr told us on the authority of Ibn Juraij, he said: Abu Bakr said: I see him mentioned with a chain of transmission: that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab He allocated three thousand and five hundred for Asama bin Zayd, and three thousand for Abdullah bin Omar. Abdullah said to Omar: I assigned for Asama. Three thousand and five hundred, and he is not older than me in Islam, nor did he bear witness as long as I did not bear witness. He said: So he said: Omar: because Zaid bin Haritha was more beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than your father, and Osama bin Zaid was more beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless you and grant you peace, so I have added five hundred to you. (Bazzar 1500, Abu Ali 157)"
"33550","(33550) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Abu Al-Zannad, who said: Omar gave us a dirham for a dirham, then He gave us two dirhams, meaning he divided among them."
"33551","(33551) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, and Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab said that Omar ibn al-Khattab appointed the Muhajirs as five thousand and the Ansar as four thousand, and whoever did not witness Badr would The children of immigrants numbered four thousand, and among them were Usama bin Zayd, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Jahsh, and Omar bin Abu Salamah, and Abdullah bin Omar. Abdul Rahman bin Awf said: Abdullah is not like these people. Indeed, Abdullah is the one who commanded him. Who ordered him? Abdullah bin Omar said to Omar: If it is rightfully yours, then give it to me. If not, do not give it to me. Omar said to Abdul Rahman. Ibn Awf: So appoint me for four thousand, and Abdullah for five thousand, and God does not bring you and me together for five. Thousands, so Abdullah bin Omar said: If it is true, then give it to me, otherwise do not give it to me."
"33552","(33552) Ghassan bin Mudar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, on the authority of Jabir, who said: When Omar became the ruler He imposed the religious duties, wrote down collections, and introduced the scholars. Jabir said: So he introduced me to my companions."
"33553","(33553) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Mukhlid Al-Ghafari that three kings They witnessed Badr, and Omar used to give each man three thousand three thousand for each year."
"33554","(33554) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Harun bin Antar, on the authority of his father, who said: I witnessed Uthman and Ali providing sustenance. The finest people."
"33555","(33555) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Yusuf bin Saad, on the authority of Wahib that Zayd bin Thabit was Regarding Othman’s rule over the treasury, he said: Then Othman entered and saw Wahab helping them, and he said: Who is this? He said: He is owned by me. He said: I see him helping them. Allocate two thousand for him. He said: So allocate one thousand for him."
"33556","(33556) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ayyad Al-Ash’ari, that Omar was blessed with Slaves, female slaves and horses."
"33557","(33557) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz did not make it obligatory except for those who recited The Qur’an, he said: My father was among those who read the Qur’an and it was made obligatory for him."
"33558","(33558) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yasir bin Amr that Saad bin Malik imposed For whoever recites the Qur’an in two thousand years, then that age reaches age, and he writes to him not to give any reward for the Qur’an."
"33559","(33559) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that Omar used to provide for the boy If it is started"
"33560","(33560) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Harun bin Antar, on the authority of his father, who said: I witnessed Uthman taking his time. With the gifts of people, if it is said to him: So-and-so will give birth this night, and he says: Look how much you do. If she gives birth to a boy or a slave girl. Take it out with the people."
"33561","(33561) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad bin Zayd, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that when Omar was born after him in a hundred years."
"33562","(33562) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Jahhaf Dawud bin Abi Awf, on the authority of a man from Khath’am, who said: A baby boy was born to me during the night, so I went to Ali in the morning and he joined him in a hundred days."
"33563","(33563) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Bishr bin Ghalib, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr asked Al-Hasan Ibn Ali, on the authority of the newborn, and he said: If it begins, it is obligatory to give and provide for it."
"33564","(33564) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Fitr narrated to us, saying: I was sitting with Zayd bin Ali, and I said: How did I do? This man is coming to you, Omar bin Abdul Aziz. A young son of his passed by and said: May God reward him well. He added this In two thousand"
"33565","(33565) Ismail bin Shuaib Al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Umm Al-Ala, that his father took her to Ali and made an assignment for her in The gift was small. He said: And Ali said: What is the boy who ate the food and bitten off the broken pieces more deserving of this gift than The newborn who sucks the breast."
"33566","(33566) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Al-Qasim bin Ma’n narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that Omar wanted to impose to the people, and his opinion was better than theirs, so they said: Start with yourself. He said: No, so he started with the closest, then the closest to the Messenger. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made an assignment to Abbas, then to Ali, until he ruled among five tribes until he came to the Banu Adi bin Heel"
"33567","(33567) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ali bin Rabah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that Omar bin Al-Khattab addressed the people in The tax collector thanked God and praised him, then said: Whoever would like to be asked about the Qur’an, let him come to Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and whoever Whoever would like to be asked about religious duties, let him come to Zayd bin Thabit, and whoever would like to be asked about jurisprudence, let him come to Muadh bin Jabal. And whoever likes to ask about money, let him give it to me, for God has made me a treasurer and a divider. Indeed, I will begin with the first immigrants. Me and my companions, so We will give to them, then starting with the Ansar who lived in the land and the faith, so We will give to them, then starting with the wives. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and We will give them to you. Whoever is quick to emigrate will be quick to give, and whoever is slow to do so will be quick to give. Migration slows down giving, so none of you can blame anything but the climate of your camel."
"33568","(33568) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Ubaidah narrated to me, saying: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to me. Al-Taymi, and his grandfather was one of the immigrants, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he delegated to the owner of the two seas, and he said: So he sent with me With eight hundred thousand dirhams to Omar bin Al-Khattab, I came to him, and he said: You did not bring him to us, O Abu Hurairah. So I said: For eight hundred thousand dirhams, he said: Do you know what you are saying that you are a Bedouin? He said: So I counted it to him in my hand until I fulfilled it. He said: So he called the immigrants and consulted them about the money, but they disagreed over it, so he said: Stay away from him until, at noon, he sent To them, and he said: I met a man from my companions and consulted him, but his opinion did not spread to him, so he said: (What has God done for him? His Messenger from among the people of the town, to God and to the Messenger and to the relatives and the orphans and the needy and the wayfarer.” So Omar distributed it according to a book. God"
"33569","(33569) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, he said: When Omar ibn al-Khattab wrote the collections, He consulted the people and said: Who should I start with? He said: Start with yourself. He said: No, but I will start with the closest, so the closest to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he began Why?"
"33570","(33570) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that Omar came from Jalula With six thousand, he imposed a bid and consulted about it, so Abd al-Rahman bin Awf said: Start with yourself, for you are more deserving. Therefore, he said: No, rather I will start with the person closest to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who witnessed Badr until that was over. To me, he said: So he began and allocated five thousand to Ali, then to Banu Hashim from among those who witnessed Badr, then to their masters, then To their allies, then the closest and the closest until that comes to an end."
"33571","(33571) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Antar, on the authority of his father, who said: His father was a friend of Qanbar. He said: I went with Qunbar to Ali, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, get up with me, I have hidden something hidden for you, so he went with him. To his house, then I saw a basket full of bowls of gold and silver, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, you will not leave Nothing unless you divide it, or spend it. Then he drew his sword and said: Woe to you, you would have loved to bring fire into my house. It was large, then he displayed it with his sword and struck it, and it was scattered among a vessel, half of which was cut out and a third of which was cut. He said: Ali with the seers. So they came, and he said: Divide this in portions. He said, so they did, and he said: O yellow, O white, change it. He said: And he started saying: \n This is a crime and his choice is in it, as every jinn has a hand in it.\n He said: In the treasury there are points and needles, and he used to take from every people their tax from the work of their hands. He said: And he said to the fortune tellers: Divide this. They said: We have no need for it. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, we will divide the good with the evil."
"33572","(33572) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam Al-Nakha’i, he said: My mother told me, on the authority of Umm Affan, the mother of Ali’s son. She said: I came to Ali with a clove of cloves buried in the open space, and I said: O Commander of the Faithful, give my daughter some of the “These cloves are a necklace,” and he said thus, and tapped his hand. Throw a dirham, for this is the property of the Muslims. Otherwise So be patient until our share comes so that we can give your daughter a necklace."
"33573","(33573) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Salih, who used to serve Umm Kulthum bint Ali, he said: She said: O Abu Salih, how would it be if you saw the Commander of the Faithful and a citron was brought, so he went Hassan or Hussein was taking some of it, so he took it from his hand, ordered it to be taken, and it was divided among the people."
"33574","(33574) Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Dinar, on the authority of al-Hasan, that a man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a rein of hair made of faye. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: They will ask me for a rein of hellfire. What it was? You should ask me, but I should not give it to you. (Abu Ishaq 476)"
"33575","(33575) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim Al-Ahmasi. He said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a handful of hair from the spoils, and he said: O Messenger of God, Give it to me, for I am a household that treats poetry. My share of it said to you. (Saeed bin Mansour 2726)"
"33576","(33576) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Fudayl, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of his grandfather, Abi Rafi’, who said: I was a treasurer for Ali. He said: I decorated his daughter with pearls of money. He recognized her, saw her, and said: Where did she get this from? It is God’s command that I cut off her hand. He said: When I saw that, I said: O Commander of the Faithful, you adorned my brother’s daughter with her. Wherever she was able to do so, when he saw that, he remained silent."
"33577","(33577) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Ajlan al-Barjami narrated to us, on the authority of his grandmother, she said: It was Ali. He divides the ibzaar among us with its sararah: the saraa of cumin and the letter, and such and such."
"33578","(33578) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Rabi’ bin Hassan narrated to us, on the authority of his mother, she said: Ali used to divide the land among us. And saffron. He said: Ali once entered the chamber and saw scattered seeds, so he began to pick them up and say: You are satisfied, O family of Ali."
"33579","(33579) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan bin Sa`id bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh of theirs, that Ali was brought with a pomegranate. So he divided it among the people, and seven or eight pomegranates struck our mosque."
"33580","(33580) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali was brought with a paint of paint from He divided forests among the Muslims."
"33581","(33581) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Uyaynah bin Abd al-Rahman bin Jawshan informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra said: Nothing came to me from our treasury until he separated from us except a stuffed garment and a khamis. Darabjrdiyah"
"33582","(33582) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: When Abu The firstborn of his illness, the one who died there, said: Look what has increased in my wealth since I entered the Emirate, so send it to the Caliph from After me, I used to consider it permissible, and I used to suffer from your friendliness in a way that I used to suffer from in commerce. She said: When he died, we looked and saw a Nubian slave who was carrying the two boys, and a mature man who was watering on him, so he sent them to Omar, she said: Then my neighbor, meaning: my representative, told me that Omar cried and said: May God have mercy on Abu Bakr, he is tired. He was very tired after him."
"33583","(33583) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qais, he said: We were sitting at Omar’s door, when his maid came out and we said: Omar’s concubine. She said: She is not Omar’s concubine. I am not permissible for Omar. It is from the wealth of God, so we discussed among us what is permissible for him from the wealth of God. He said: He distributed that to him, so he sent for us and said: What Did you remember? We said: A slave girl came out to us. We said: Omar’s concubine. She said: She is not Omar’s concubine. She is Omar’s concubine. It is not permissible for Omar, it is from the wealth of God, so we discussed between us what is permissible for you from the wealth of God? He said: I will inform you of what I deem permissible of God’s wealth: my provisions for winter and hot weather, what I perform Hajj on, what I perform for Umrah at noon, and my sustenance. My family is like a man from Quraysh, neither the richest nor the poorest of them. I am a man from among the Muslims. Something befalls me. What happened to them?"
"33584","(33584) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qays, that they were He was sitting at the door of Omar, then a female servant came out to them, and some of the people said to her: The Commander of the Faithful has intercourse with you. She said: I am not permissible. For him, meaning that she is one of the five, so Omar came out and said: Do you know what I consider permissible from this group to perform Hajj on this afternoon? I perform Umrah, and I wear two garments: winter and summer, and the sustenance of the family of Omar is the sustenance of the family of a man from Quraysh, who are not as good as them, nor are they With the worst of them."
"33585","(33585) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah ibn Mudharib al-Abdi, he said: Omar said: Indeed, I have given myself the same place from God’s wealth as the wealth of an orphan. If I do not need it, I maintain self-control, and if I am poor, I eat sensibly."
"33586","(33586) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak narrated to us, saying: Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Akhi narrated to me. Alba'a, on the authority of Alba'a, said: Ali said: I passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one of the camels of Al-Sadaqah, so he took and freed some of the camels. A camel appeared and said: It is not permissible for me to take any of your spoils that weigh this, except a fifth, and it will be returned to you. (Ahmed 88)"
"33587","(33587) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Nabih, who said: Ibn Umar bought Two camels and he threw them into the camels of charity, and they became fat and arrogant, and their appearance was beautiful. He said: Then Omar saw them and disapproved of their appearance. He said: To whom are these two? They said: To Abdullah bin Omar, so he said: Sell them and take your capital, and return the surplus to the treasury."
"33588","(33588) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: When Utbai came to Azerbaijan in Al-Khabis So he tasted it and found it sweet, so he said: If only you would do this for the Commander of the Faithful. He said: So he made for him two great baskets, then He loaded them on a camel with two men and sent them to him. When they came to Omar, he said: What is this? He said: This. It was bad, so he tasted it and found it was sweet, so he said: Can all Muslims be satisfied with this on their journey? They said: No. He said: He sent them back, then wrote to him: As for what follows, he is not from your toil, nor from your father’s toil, nor from your toil. Your mother, satisfy the Muslims with what you are satisfied with on your journey."
"33589","(33589) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, saying: Utba narrated to me. Ibn Farqad Al-Salami, he said: I came to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab with a basket full of bones. I have never seen anyone better and more skilled than him, so he said: What is this? I said: Food I have brought to you. You fulfill people’s needs at the beginning of the day, so when you come back you will get some of it. He said: Expose. On the authority of a basket of it, he said: So it was revealed, he said: I determined that when you return, I would provide every Muslim man with a basket of it, he said: I said: By the one who is right with you, O Commander of the Faithful, if you had spent all of Qays’ money, it would not have amounted to that. He said: I have no need for it. Then he called for a bowl containing porridge of coarse bread and thick meat, and he was eating delicious food with me, so I made I reach for the piece of white meat, thinking it is a hump, so I touch it, and behold, I am nervous, and I take the piece of meat. So he chewed it and could hardly make it swallow. When he neglected to do so, I placed it between the bowls and the bowl. Then he said: O Utbab! We slaughter large animals every day, and as for its slaughter and its spices, they are for those who are present among the Muslims, and as for its neck, it is for Umar."
"33590","(33590) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Sulaiman, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahhab, on the authority of Hudhayfa, he said: I passed by while people were eating porridge and meat, so Omar invited me to his dinner, and he was eating thick bread and oil, so I said: You prevented me from eating porridge with the people, and you invited me to this. He said: I only invited you for my food, and that is for the Muslims."
"33591","(33591) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Asim ibn Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of Ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: When Umar employed a man who had a group of the Ansar and others testify against him, he would say: I did not employ you. For the blood of the Muslims, nor for their honor, but I used you over them so that you might divide among them justly and reside among them. prayer, and stipulated that he should not eat anything pure, should not wear thin clothes, should not ride wearing clothes, and should not close his door without People's needs"
"33592","(33592) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, on the authority of Abu Firas, who said: Omar ibn Al-Khattab delivered a speech, He said: By God, I will not send workers to you to beat your people, nor to take your money, but I send them to you to teach you your religion and your Sunnahs, so whoever does anything other than that, let him refer it to me. By the One in whose hand is my soul, I would have saved him from it. Then Amr ibn al-Aas jumped up and said: O Commander of the Faithful, have you seen if it was A man of the Muslims is in charge of his subjects and he disciplines some of his subjects. Would you be excluded from him? He said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Omar, I will exclude him from it. Indeed, I will not exclude him from it, and I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said to himself: Do not strike Muslims and humiliate them, and do not deprive them of their rights and make them infidels. Do not gather them together and tempt them, and do not bring down the furnace on them and cause them to be lost. (Abu Dawud 4525. Tayalisi 54)"
"33593","(33593) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari that Cut off your knees, and get out on your horses, and throw away your sandals, and put on your sandals, and throw away your trousers, and gather yourselves and throw away your belongings. And you should wear the traditional clothing, and beware of the gift of a non-Arab, for the worst of the gifts is the gift of a non-Arab."
"33594","(33594) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraydah, on the authority of His father, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would send an emir to command a convoy or an army, he would entrust it to his elite. himself with the fear of God and with goodness to those who are with him among the Muslims. He said: Fight in the way of God. Fight those who disbelieve in God. Fight. And do not exaggerate, do not betray, do not mutilate, and do not kill a newborn."
"33595","(33595) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, saying: I heard Zayd bin Aslam mention, on the authority of His father, he said: I saw Omar ibn Al-Khattab appointing his master, Haniyya, to the mother-in-law, he said: I saw him say like this: Woe to you O Here, keep your wings separate from the people, and fear the call of the oppressed, for the call of the oppressed is answered. Enter, Lord of the world. And the spoils, and he left me among the blessings of Ibn Affan and Ibn Awf, for Ibn Awf and Ibn Affan, if their livestock were destroyed, they would return. To Medina for palm trees and crops, and this poor fellow, if his livestock were to perish, would come to me crying, O Amir. The believers, O Commander of the Faithful, water and pasture are easier for me than to fall in love with gold and paper. By God, by God, by God. It is their country, for the sake of God. They fought for it in the pre-Islamic period and greeted it with Islam. Were it not for this blessing The one who is burdened for the sake of God, as long as I have protected anything from the people of their country."
"33596","(33596) Abu Bakr bin Ayash narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Iyad bin Laqit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Qais, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab sent me to Salman bin Rabi’i to command him to break his fast, and he Besieged"
"33597","(33597) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Mu’awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Rabi’ ibn Yazid narrated to me. Al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Qaz’a, said: I asked Abu Sa’id about fasting while travelling, and he said: We traveled with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and fasted, and we fasted until we came to a certain place, and he said: You have come close to your enemy, and mushrooms are stronger for you.\n(Muslim 1020, Abu Dawud 2398)"
"33598","(33598) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: Al-Zubayr entered upon Ammar, or Uthman, after Abdullah’s death, and said: Give me the gift of Abdullah, for Abdullah’s children are more deserving of him than him. The house of money, he said: So he gave him fifteen thousand."
"33599","(33599) Waki’ told us, he said: Ali bin Salih told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of the sheikhs of the neighborhood, they said: A man died Two-thirds of the year had passed, so Omar bin Al-Khattab ordered two-thirds of his donation to him."
"33600","(33600) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abbas informed me that Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Qais Ibn Makhramah told him that a woman complained to Aisha Al-Hajj, and she said: What is the matter with you? She said: We used to take the gift of a dead person and raise it. Aisha said: Why did you do that? You took out an arrow from God’s arrow. He comes upon you whom you expelled from among you, and that was in the time of Omar ibn al-Khattab."
"33601","(33601) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Miqdam Hisham bin Ziyad, a client of Uthman, narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that Uthman He was bequeathing gifts."
"33602","(33602) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no harm in being taken. To the dead is his gift."
"33603","(33603) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of a servant of Ali bin Husayn, on the authority of Ali bin Husayn He said: There is no harm in taking the gift of the dead."
"33604","(33604) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Ma’qil, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to die when a man had He completed the year and gave all his gifts to his heirs."
"33605","(33605) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, that Omar bin Abdul-Aziz advised his commander in the battle not to He rides any animal, except for one that is walking, the weakest animal in the army."
"33606","(33606) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Umayyah al-Shami, who said: Makhoul and Raja’ ibn Huywah used to choose the female barmaid rather than He leaves her."
"33607","(33607) Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Juma’ bin Abdullah al-Muqri, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz forbade the post. He put a sharp edge on the end of the whip so that an animal can poke it with it. He said: And he forbade biting bits."
"33608","(33608) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Dhul bin Aws, on the authority of Tamim bin Masih said: I left the house and had no child, so I injured a foundling, so I informed Omar about him, and he joined him in a hundred years."
"33609","(33609) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair Al-Ansi, that a man picked up a foundling and brought him to Ali. So he freed him and joined him in a hundred years."
"33610","(33610) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Musa the Jinni, he said: I saw a child of adultery committed by Ali. A hundred"
"33611","(33611) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, that two men from the family of Alice converted to Islam during the reign of Omar. He said: So they came Omar informed him of their conversion to Islam, so he wrote to Uthman ibn Hanif to lift the tax from their heads, and he took Weather from their land."
"33612","(33612) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Al-Zubair ibn Adiyy Al-Yami that Diqaan converted to Islam during Ali’s covenant. Then Ali said to him: If you stay in your land, we will lift the tribute from your head and take it from your land, but if you turn away from it We have more right to it."
"33613","(33613) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays, on the authority of Abu Aoun Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Omar And Ali, they said: If he converts to Islam and has land, we will waive the tax on his behalf and take the tax from it."
"33614","(33614) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, that Deqan of The people of Nahr al-Malik converted to Islam, so Omar said: Give her her land and she will pay the tax on its behalf."
"33615","(33615) Waki’ narrated to us, Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Qays bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, that Deqan She converted to Islam, so Omar wrote that they had given her a choice."
"33616","(33616) Wakī’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, that Al-Rufayl Diqan Al-Nahrain converted to Islam, so it was presented to him. Omar lived in two thousand years, and he lifted the tribute from his head, and gave him his land to pay the tax on it."
"33617","(33617) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man from his family converts to Islam Blackness, then he resided on his land, the tax was taken from him, but if he left it, the tax was not taken from him."
"33618","(33618) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: The people of Sawad did not have a feast, so when They were satisfied with the reward, and it became a covenant for them."
"33619","(33619) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no covenant for the people of Sawad, they only descended Ali Al-Hakam"
"33620","(33620) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Part of blackness is goodness and part of it is goodness. Title:"
"33621","(33621) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: When Al-Hurmuzan and Al-Firzan converted to Islam, he said Lama Omar: It is only upon you that you are subjected to the penalty. Indeed, Islam truly seeks refuge from the penalty."
"33622","(33622) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace. He looks to this radiance."
"33623","(33623) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Alqamiya and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla came out to Nomads to them."
"33624","(33624) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Alqamiya used to travel to Najaf."
"33625","(33625) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, who said: Masruq and Urwah bin Al-Mughirah to their Bedouins."
"33626","(33626) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib Al-Taifi narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Sa’d, who said: I went out with Omar bin Abd. Al-Aziz to Suwayda, moving forward."
"33627","(33627) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurayh, he said: It was said: Bedouins are two months, so whoever adds more is Arabization."
"33628","(33628) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Ibn Munabbih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He who starts is ignorant, and he who follows the hunt is ignorant. (Abu Dawud 2853. Tirmidhi 2256)"
"33629","(33629) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They started with Alqamiya, and it was Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla is close to us."
"33630","(33630) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, that a man bought a mother on the Day of Qadisiyah for spoils, so she brought him With some jewelry that she had with her, he came to Saad bin Abi Waqqas and told him, and he said: Put it among the spoils of the Muslims."
"33631","(33631) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, who said: I bought a female slave for five. She found with her fifteen dinars, so she brought them to Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid bin al-Walid, and he said: This is yours."
"33632","(33632) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who bought captives from the spoils and found some silver with them. He said: He will return them."
"33633","(33633) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in selling to Yazid. Fifths were also sold."
"33634","(33634) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz sent Umayra bin Zaid The Philistine sells the captives to whomever is more."
"33635","(33635) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they disliked selling to Yazid. Except for selling inheritances and spoils."
"33636","(33636) Issa bin Yunus and Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Akhdar bin Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Anas bin Malik reported that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sold beans and a cup to Yazid, except that he was performing Umrah. He said: On the authority of Anas, On the authority of a man from the Ansar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"33637","(33637) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Khattimi that Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba He sold the spoils to Yazid."
"33638","(33638) Waki’ told us, he said: Hizam bin Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I witnessed Omar selling one of the al-Sadaqah’s camels. Who is Yazid?"
"33639","(33639) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: There is no harm in selling at auction."
"33640","(33640) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, that he disliked selling to anyone except partners. Between them."
"33641","(33641) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, who said: There is no harm in selling to someone who increases: You can increase the price if you want. To buy"
"33642","(33642) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of someone who heard Mujahid and Ata say: There is no harm in selling to more than one person."
"33643","(33643) Otham bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Mudarib, who said: The age of Al-Sawad was divided among the people of Kufa, so each man attacked three farmers, and Omar said to him: Who will be among them after them? So he left them."
"33644","(33644) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Qais, who said: Bujaila would have had a quarter of the black, so Omar said: Had it not been for Indeed, I am the judge and responsible. You have not adhered to what was apportioned to you."
"33645","(33645) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of a man from the Prophet’s companions. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, defeated Khaybar, Khaybar became the property of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace and the Muslims, they failed to work on it, so they handed it over to the Jews. They work on it and spend on it on the condition that it is theirs. Half of what came out of it was divided by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, into thirty-six shares, each share having a hundred An arrow, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, allocated half of that to the Muslims, so that half was the arrows of the Muslims. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shared his share with them and allocated the other half to those to whom delegations, affairs, and representatives of the people were sent. (Abu Dawud 3004)"
"33646","(33646) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, he said: Omar said: If I stayed to take the surplus of the wealth of the rich, and to divide it among the poor immigrants."
"33647","(33647) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Wasil Al-Ahdab, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: I sat with Shaybah ibn Othman, and he said to me: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab sat in this gathering of yours, and he said to me: I have decided not to leave yellow on the Kaaba, nor White, unless you divide it among the people. He said: I told him: This is not up to you. Your two companions preceded you and they did not do that. He said: These are the Qur’an to be imitated by. (Bukhari 1594, Ahmed 410)"
"33648","(33648) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Aslam, he said: I heard Umar say: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Omar, had not the last of the people been left behind, they would have nothing, not a single village would have been conquered for the Muslims. The infidels, except you divided it into two shares, just as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore an equal share, but I wanted it to be I dared to run against them and I hated to be left behind as the last of the people, having nothing to do with them. (Bukhari 2334. Ahmad 40)"
"33649","(33649) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sha’ithi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith Abi Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab saying: There is not one of the Muslims who does not have a share in this wealth. Except for a slave-owner, and if you remain, the shepherd will get his share of this sheep in the mountains of Sana’a."
"33650","(33650) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Malik ibn Aws ibn Al-Hadathan, on the authority of Omar, he said: The wealth of Banu al-Nadir was from what God had bestowed upon His Messenger, and the Muslims did not charge it miserly, nor A stirrup. It was the Prophet’s, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, private possessions. He used to withhold from it a year’s worth of it, and whatever remained, he put it in Arms and weapons as equipment for the sake of God. (Bukhari 2904, Muslim 1376)"
"33651","(33651) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Saad told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab was presented with some of the spoils of Jaloula, which contained gold and silver, so he set about dividing them among the people, then a son of his came, and it is said To him: Abd al-Rahman. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, give me a seal. He said: Go to your mother to give you something to drink from a stalk. He said: By God, he did not give him anything."
"33652","(33652) Affan told us, he said: Abdul Wahid told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said: Abu Hanzala bin Nu’aym told us Sa`d wrote to Omar saying: We took a land whose people did not fight us. He said: So Omar wrote to him: If you wish, you could divide it. Among yourselves, divide it up, and if you wish to call upon it, then its people will inhabit it, and whoever enters among you after that shall have possession of it. share, for I fear that you will quarrel over it and drink it, and some of you will kill one another. So Saad wrote to him: Indeed, the Muslims They were unanimously agreed that their opinion followed your opinion, so he wrote to them to return the slave to a woman who had become pregnant by a man from Muslims"
"33653","(33653) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hanash, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: It was said to Ibn Abbas: The non-Arabs. That they bring about a builder or a seller in the Muslim lands, and he said: As for Egypt that the Arabs have seized, it is not for the non-Arabs to build. There is a building therein, or he said: a sale, and they shall not strike a gong therein, nor drink anything in it, nor take anything therein. A pig, or they enter it, and as for Egypt, the non-Arabs confiscated it. God will grant victory to the Arabs and they camped, meaning on Their ruling is that the non-Arabs are entitled to what is in their covenant, and the non-Arabs are entitled to the Arabs to fulfill their covenant, and not to burden them with anything more than Their energy"
"33654","(33654) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayy bin Abdullah, who said: The letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz came to us: Do not destroy. Neither a church, nor a church, nor a house of fire were reconciled over it."
"33655","(33655) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about churches being demolished. He said: No, except for some of them in the Sacred Mosque."
"33656","(33656) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked for the sale to be left in Egypt. Muslims"
"33657","(33657) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: They had made an agreement on the condition that they would be separated from the Fire. And idols in other countries."
"33658","(33658) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Ibn Suraqi narrated to me that Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah It is decreed for the people of the monastery that I have guaranteed you that your blood, your property, and your churches will not be destroyed."
"33659","(33659) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Habib bin Shahid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, that He did not leave any idol to the people of Persia without it being broken, nor any fire without being extinguished."
"33660","(33660) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Awf, who said: I witnessed Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Muammar bring a Magi who built a house of fire. With Basra, he beheaded him."
"33661","(33661) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Ahwal, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, Rafi`ah, he said: Expel the polytheists from the Arabian Peninsula. (Bukhari 3053, Muslim 1257)"
"33662","(33662) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Maimun, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Sa`d ibn Samurah ibn Jundub, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, he said: The last words spoken by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was: He said: Take them out. The Jews are from the land of Hijaz and the people of Najran are from the Arabian Peninsula. (Ahmed 1958 Darmi 2498)"
"33663","(33663) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar said: Do not abandon The Jews and Christians in Medina for more than three times what they sell their goods for, and he said: No two religions will meet on one island. Arabs"
"33664","(33644) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not live with Jews or Christians unless They greet them."
"33665","(33665) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, that he witnessed Omar bin Abdul Aziz in his caliphate. He expelled the non-Muslims from Medina and sold their Muslim slaves."
"33666","(33666) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If I remain, I will expel the polytheists from the Arabian Peninsula. When Omar took office, he expelled them.\n(Muslim 1388, Abu Dawud 3024)"
"33667","(33667) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, he said: We said to Jabir bin Abdullah: The Magians entered the sanctuary. He said: As for the people of our protection, yes, yes."
"33668","(33668) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent an army, then he said: Indeed, I am disassociated from every Muslim who resides with a polytheist. Their Fire will never be denied. (Abu Dawud 2438. Tirmidhi 1604)"
"33669","(33669) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Aslam, the servant of Omar, that Omar was He seals their necks, meaning the people of the Dhimma."
"33670","(33670) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, he said: Maimoon ibn Mihran narrated to us, he said: Omar was sent Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman and Ibn Hanif imposed the tax on the people of Sawad, saying: Whoever does not come from the people of Sawad. Then he will be sealed around his neck, saying, “I am absolved of sin.”"
"33671","(33671) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Miniya, who said: A man from the people of Al-Yamama bequeathed a mare to For the sake of God, then a cousin came to me, and I said: I will carry my brother’s burden on him, for my brother is a righteous man. He said: Until I ask Al-Hasan, so he asked Al-Hasan, so he said: Make a man your husband, and do not favor anyone over him. He said: I said to Al-Hasan: If he needs it, he said: Let him sell it to someone Soldiers, and do not give him this property lest one of them leave it to support his family."
"33672","(33672) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who comes from the people of war, he said: Either he should honor him, or he should convey him to his place of safety."
"33673","(33673) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked a man getting married in the land of war and leaves his children in it."
"33674","(33674) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ was asked about a man from among the people of the non-Muslim being taken into account. People of polytheism, so he says: I did not want their help against you, and they have stipulated that he should not come to them without the idea of killing him. With clear evidence, he said: Then he said to Ata, some of the people of knowledge: If he renounces even one thing of what he had agreed upon, then he has renounced the peace agreement."
"33675","(33675) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the people of dhimma, if they break the covenant, then there is no blame on the offspring."
"33676","(33676) Omar bin Bishr told us, he said: Ibn Mubarak told us, he said: Safwan bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Jubayr Ibn Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Awf Ibn Malik, he said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came He divided the fay from his day, so he gave the family two shares and gave the single person one share. (Abu Dawud 2946. Ahmed 29)"
"33677","(33677) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sadiqah Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And let it cool down."
"33678","(33678) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, that Omar ibn Abdul Aziz was cooling, and he said: So he carried a slave. He had a man on the post without his permission, so he called him and said: Do not leave until we straighten him out, then put him in the treasury."
"33679","(33679) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said To his princes: If you send me a message, send it with a good face and a good name. (Bazzar 1985)"
"33680","(33680) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of his father, that Muawiyah wrote to Abdul Rahman Ibn Khalid to bring Jareer to me on the post and he carried him."
"33681","(33681) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jabalah, on the authority of Tawus that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Indeed, God sent me with the sword in the hands of the pursuer, and placed my livelihood under the shade of my spear, and made the lowly and the small On whoever disagrees with me, and whoever imitates a people is one of them."
"33682","(33682) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jabali, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then mentioned something similar to it."
"33683","(33683) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Ali, he said: It was When Al-Mugheerah ibn Shu`ba went on a campaign with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he carried a spear with him, and when he returned he threw it out to be carried. To him, so Ali said: I will mention this to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do not do it, for if you do it it will not be lifted. lost\n(Ibn Majah 2809. An-Nasa’i 5807)"
"33684","(33684) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mus’ab bin Sulaym narrated to us, saying: I heard Anas bin Malik saying: Abu Musa wanted to Al-Bara' bin Malik asked him to do so, but he refused, so Al-Bara' bin Malik said to him: Give me my sword, my shield, and my spear."
"33685","(33685) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: It was only The spear is carried with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so that he may pray with it."
"33686","(33686) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mus’ab bin Sulaym al-Zuhri told us, he said: Anas bin Malik told us, he said: When Abu Musa was sent to Basra. He was among those who sent Al-Bara’ ibn Malik and he was one of his ministers. He used to say to him: Choose a job. He said: Al-Baraa’ and you give me what I asked of you. He said: Yes. He said: But I do not ask you for the Emir of Egypt, nor for the collection of a tax. But give me my bow, my horse, my spear, and my sword, and leave me to fight in the way of God. So he sent him to an army, and it was The first to be killed."
"33687","(33687) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Thabit narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Atiyya narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Munib al-Jarshi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has placed my livelihood under the shade of His spear and made Humiliation and humiliation are upon whoever disobeys my command. Whoever imitates a people is one of them."
"33688","(33688) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Saad told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar said: Gather together for this matter so that we may look into it, for indeed I have read verses from the Book of God with which I have been satisfied. God said: {How good is He? May God be upon His Messenger from among the people of the villages - to Him and to the Messenger and to his relatives and the orphans and the poor and the wayfarer} to his saying : {Indeed, God is severe in punishment} And God is not for these alone, then he read: {For the poor emigrants who were expelled from Their homes and their wealth} up to his saying: {They are the truthful} and by God, it is not for these alone. Then he read: {And those who came After them} until the end of the verses."
"33689","(33689) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Al Hassan, on the authority of Al Suddi, on the authority of Omar Bin Abdul Aziz, he said: I found the money. He divided among these three groups the Muhajireen, the Ansar, and those who came after them."
"33690","(33690) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Al-Hasan, like that."
"33691","(33691) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Aroub narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Talha that When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, defeated a people, he liked to stand in front of them three times. (Ahmad 29. Darmi 2459)"
"33692","(33692) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Talha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Muslim 2204, Ibn Abi Asim 1891)"
"33693","(33693) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ziyad bin Anam, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, he said: I said to Al-Qasim bin Muhammad and Salem bin Abdullah: We have a boy who works pottery in the enemy’s land, then he sells it and the money is collected for him. And he spends on us. He said: There is no harm in that."
"33694","(33694) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ziyad, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, he said: I said to al-Qasim Bin Muhammad and Salem bin Abdullah: A man will be among us in the enemy’s land, and he will catch whales and sell them, and dirhams will be collected for him. He said: There is no problem with that."
"33695","(33695) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, handed over a piece of land from the land of Banu al-Nadir, in which were palm trees and trees, and Abu Bakr and Umar plotted it."
"33696","(33696) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: Al-Zubayr allotted a piece of land from the land of Banu al-Nadir, which had palm trees, and that Abu Bakr allotted a Jurf from al-Zubayr, and that Omar The aqeeq cut him off completely."
"33697","(33697) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cut off land from al-Zubayr. There are palm trees in it."
"33698","(33698) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, who said: I asked Musa bin Talha, and they told me that Othman cut off He searched the land, served Allah on the land, Saad on the land, and Sahib on the land."
"33699","(33699) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, that Uthman cut off five of the Prophet’s companions. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Ibn Masoud, Sa’d, Al-Zubayr, Khabab, and Asama bin Zaid."
"33700","(33700) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that Omar cut off Ali’s yanabu and added to it Change it."
"33701","(33701) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi, who said: Omar came, a man from Thaqif. It was said to him: Nafi’ Abu Abdullah. He said: He was the first to visit the man with insight. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, If we accept a land in Basra that is not part of the land of the tax, and it does not harm any of the Muslims, then if you wish, you may cut it off from us. Should I take it as a harness for my horses, then do so. He said: Then Omar wrote to Abu Musa: If it is as he said, then cut it off for him. (Abu Ubaid 687)"
"33702","(33702) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: A man from Banu Zurayq told us, he said: Abu Bakr cut off He gave him a land and wrote a letter for him about it, and he brought witnesses to it, including Omar, so Talha brought Omar the letter and said: Seal it. This one, he said: I will not seal him, this is yours, not the people. He said: So Talhah went off in anger, and came to Abu Bakr, and said: By God, I do not know whether you are the Caliph or Omar. He said: No, Omar, but he is my father."
"33703","(33703) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a vow to Ali. Al-Fakirin, Bir Qais, and Al-Shajarah."
"33704","(33704) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Qays Al-Maribi, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abyad ibn Hammal reported that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, collected the salt in Ma’rib, so he wanted to collect it, so he said A man told the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was like water at a count, but he refused to cut him off. (Bukhari 1482 and Abu Dawud 3059)"
"33705","(33705) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Neither Abu Bakr nor Omar cut it off. Not even Ali. The first one to allocate the herds was Othman, and lands were sold during the emirate of Othman."
"33706","(33706) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, that Abu Bakr allotted land from Al-Aqra’ bin Habis and Aynah bin Hisn, and wrote a letter for them over it."
"33707","(33707) Waki’ told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Muzani told us, he said: A man whose father had told me told me The people with this blackness are called: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Hurr, on the authority of his father, that Omar ibn al-Khattab chose ten lands. From the land of Al-Sawad, he said: I counted seven and forgot three: Al-Ajam, Mawdhir Al-Mai, the land of the Kasri family, Deir Al-Barid, and the land of Whoever was killed in the battle, and the land of whoever fled, he said: And it remained pure in the Diwan until Al-Hajjaj burned the Diwan. So each people took what came to them."
"33708","(33708) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that agents for his Muslims took two men from the Muslims. So they brought them to him, and he said to one of them: Do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God? He said: Yes, then he said: Do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God? He said: Yes. He said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of God? He said: So he turned to His ears and said: I am deaf. He said: What is the matter with you if I say to you: You bear witness that he is the Messenger of God? I said: I am deaf. So he ordered him to be killed, and he said to the other: Do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God? He said: Yes. He said: Do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God? He said: Yes. So he sent him, and he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, you have perished. He said: What is the matter with you? So tell him. With his story and the story of his companion, he said: As for your companion, he continued his faith, but you took the concession."
"33709","(33709) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mukhariq ibn Khalifa, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salman, he said: A man entered Paradise because of a fly, and a man entered Hell because of a fly. Two men passed by a people who had devoted themselves to an idol of theirs, and they said: No. No one is upon us today unless he offered something. They said to one of them: Offer something, but he refused and was killed. They said to the other: Offer something. So they said: He presented even a fly, and he said: How many flies, so he presented a fly and entered the Fire, and Salman said: So the jinn entered the Garden in a fly, and he entered This fire is in flies. (Bayhaqi 7343. Abu Na’im 203)"
"33710","(33710) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, on the authority of a gift in the name of a man who was captured by the enemy. So they forced him to drink wine and eat pig. He said: If he eats and drinks, he will be rewarded, but if he is killed, he will be rewarded with goodness."
"33711","(33711) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, he said: There is no concession in alcohol because it does not narrate"
"33712","(33712) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Umar ibn Atiyya, who said: I heard Abu Ja`far say: Piety is not permissible. Except as death is lawful for the one in need."
"33713","(33713) Marwan told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Piety is permissible for the believer until the Day of Resurrection except He did not consider killing to be pious."
"33714","(33714) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Piety is only With the tongue, not with the hand."
"33715","(33715) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Jafar, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah (Unless you fear them. Taqiyya, he said: Taqiyyah comes from the tongue, not from the deeds."
"33716","(33716) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: I heard him say: There is no faith. For those whom you do not have piety for."
"33717","(33717) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: There are no words that I speak in the hands of an authority that turns away from me, between one and two whips, except that I am speaking. With it"
"33718","(33718) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Taqiyyah is as wide as the length of the heavens. The earth"
"33719","(33719) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Marzuq, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Abi Al-Hasan, who said: Verily, piety is cheap. The virtue is doing the command of God."
"33720","(33720) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: Hudhayfy said: I am buying my religion. Some of it for fear that it will all go away."
"33721","(33721) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Misra, on the authority of Al-Nazzal bin Sabrah, he said: Ibn Masoud and Hudhayfy entered upon Uthman, and Uthman said to Hudhify: I have heard that you said such-and-such. He said: No, by God. You said it, and when he came out, Abdullah said to him: He asked you, but you did not confirm to him what I heard you say, so he said: He bought my religion part for part out of fear. Let it all go away."
"33722","(33722) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Omar used to raid a single man and take the resident’s horse. So he gives it to the traveler."
"33723","(33723) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abu Saad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi, who said: It was For the life of four thousand horses on an ariya with a kufa marked on its thighs for the sake of God, if it was in the gift of a man He gave him his right, or he was in need, and he gave him the horse, then said: If you reward him and make him tired, or lose any fodder, you are responsible. If you fight for him and he is injured, or you are injured, then you do not owe anything."
"33724","Abu Abdul Rahman Buqi bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying:\n(33724) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: When Salman invaded The polytheists from the people of Persia. He said: Stop until I call upon them as I used to listen to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He called them, so he came to them and said: I am a man from among you, and you may see my position among these people, and we call you to Islam. If you submit, then you have the same as what we have, and you have the same as what we have, but if you refuse, then pay the jizyah, on hand. And you are submissive, and if you refuse, we will fight you. They said: As for Islam, we will not submit, and as for the tribute, we will not give it. Fighting, for indeed we are fighting you. He said: So he called them like that for three days, but they refused, so he said to the people: Call them."
"33725","(33725) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraydah, on the authority of His father, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would send an emir to command a convoy or an army, he would entrust it to his elite. He blessed himself with the fear of God and those who were with him among the Muslims well, and said: “Fight in the name of God. In the way of God, you fight those who disbelieve in God.” Conquer, and do not commit excesses, and do not betray, and do not mutilate, and do not kill a child, and when you meet your enemy from among the polytheists, invite them to your side. One of three characteristics, or characteristics, so give them what they have answered you, accept from them and desist from them, then invite them to Islam. If they answer you, then accept and desist from them, then invite them to move from their home to the home of the immigrants and inform them that they If they do that, it means that they will have what the immigrants have, and they will have what the immigrants have, even if they refuse and choose their homes. So inform them that they will be like the Bedouins of the Muslims, and the judgment of God that He applies to the believers will apply to them. And they will have no share in the spoils or spoils unless they fight with the Muslims. If they refuse, invite them to Giving the reward, and if they respond, then accept it and desist from them, and if they refuse, then seek help from God, then fight them."
"33726","(33726) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam Al-Nakha’i narrated to us, saying: Abu Sabara Al-Nakha’i narrated to us, on the authority of Narrated by Ibn Masik Al-Muradi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When you come to a people, call them, who will answer you? So accept, and from my father, do not be hasty until you speak to me about it. (Abu Dawud 3984. Tabarani 836)"
"33727","(33727) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Dharr narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Ali that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He sent him on a mission, and he said to a man with him: The truth and do not leave him behind him, so say: Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded you to wait for him. He said: So he waited for him until he came, and he said: Do not fight the people until you invite them. (Tabarani 8261)"
"33728","(33728) Wakī’ narrated to us, Shu’bā’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ghalib al-Abdi, on the authority of a man from Banu Numayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, or his father’s grandfather, is that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Do not fight the people until you invite them."
"33729","(33729) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When you meet the enemy So invite them."
"33730","(33730) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, that he used to love To invite them."
"33731","(33731) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sakhr, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to the people of Daylam. He invites them."
"33732","(33732) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When you fight the polytheists, call upon them."
"33733","(33733) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dani, on the authority of Abu Al-Tufayl, he said: Ali was sent Maqal took Al-Taymi to Bani Najiya, and he said: When you go to the people, invite them three times."
"33734","(33734) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Al-Jaham that Ali sent Al-Bara’ bin A single man to a Haruriyah, so he invited them three times."
"33735","(33735) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, that he said regarding supplications The polytheists before the fighting: We used to supplicate and supplicate."
"33736","(33736) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: We used to supplicate and supplicate."
"33737","(33737) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, who said: I love that he invites you."
"33738","(33738) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God did not fight God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never even invites a people. (Ahmad 231, Darmi 2444)"
"33739","(33739) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about Daylam, and he said: He has They know what they are called to."
"33740","(33740) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in not calling on the polytheists when he met them, and he said: They have known your religion, and they did not You invite them to it."
"33741","(33741) Waki’ told us, saying: Abu Hilal told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about the enemy: Do they pray before fighting? He said: Islam has reached them since God sent Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted you."
"33742","(33742) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I wrote to Nafi’ asking him about the supplications of the polytheists. He said: : Then he wrote to me: Ibn Umar informed me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, attacked the Banu al-Muttaliq while they were jealous. And their camels are watered by water, and Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith was one of the things that happened. He said: And she was among the horses.\n(Bukhari 2541, Muslim 1356)"
"33743","(33743) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar Al-Yamami, on the authority of Iyas bin Salma bin Al-Akwa’, on the authority of his father, He said: We went on a campaign with Abu Bakr, who ruled over the covenant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we brought water to the Banu, so he visited him and we hosted a wedding. Even when the morning came, We launched a raid on them. (Muslim 1375. Abu Dawud 2589)"
"33744","(33744) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Salih bin Abi Al-Akhdar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to a village called Yabna, and he said: Come to it in the morning, then Burn\n(Abu Dawud 2409. Ahmed 205)"
"33745","(33745) Waki’ told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, he said: We fought with Abu Bakr, Hawazin, so we came to the people of Ma'i, so we made them spend the night, and we killed nine of them, or seven of the people of Abyat."
"33746","(33746) Ali bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He walked to Khaybar and arrived there at night. Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to a people, he would not attack them until In the morning (Bukhari 371, Muslim 1044)"
"33747","(33747) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Junai, on the authority of a man, who said: We used to raid them and get a share of them, and Abu Musa heard our voices."
"33748","(33748) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Nadr ibn Arabi, who said: Umar ibn Abdul Aziz used to write to the commanders of the soldiers. He forbade them from the winter attacks."
"33749","(33749) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Nawfal ibn Musahiq, on the authority of a man from Muzainah, on the authority of his father, He said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent convoys, he would say to them: If you see a mosque, or hear a muezzin, do not You kill someone. (Abu Dawud 2428. Tirmidhi 1549)"
"33750","(33750) Ali bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. When he goes to a people, if he hears a call to prayer, he catches them. (Bukhari 610, Ahmed 236)"
"33751","(33751) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of al-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu al-Aliya that Abu Bakr When he sent an army to the people of al-Rada, he would say: Sit close by, and if you hear the call until the sun rises, otherwise, attack. May God bless you"
"33752","(33752) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Medina, who said: It was There was friendship and acquaintance between me and the writer of Ubaid Allah bin Abu Awfa said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not ask to meet the enemy, but when you meet them, be patient. And know that Paradise is under the shade of swords, and it was waiting. When the sun went down, it would call out to its enemy."
"33753","(33753) Affan and Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Jawni, on the authority of Alqamah Ibn Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Maqil Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Al-Numan Ibn Muqrin, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: When he fought, he would not fight at the beginning of the day or at the end of the day until the sun had set, the winds had blown, and victory had descended. (Abu Dawud 2448. Tirmidhi 1613)"
"33754","(33754) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Nu’aym ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Ibn Samurah ibn Jundub, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever kills, the spoils are his. (Ibn Majah 2838. Ahmed 12)"
"33755","(33755) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever kills will be plundered. (Bukhari 3051, Abu Dawud 2646)"
"33756","(33756) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, On the authority of Anas that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Hunayn: Whoever kills a dead person will have the right to plunder him, so he killed Abu Talha. At that time there were twenty men, and he took their spoils. (Abu Dawud 2712, Ahmed 114)"
"33757","(33757) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, he said: When It was the day of Badr that I killed Saeed bin Al-Aas and took his sword, and his sword was called the Katifah. He said: And he was killed. My brother Umayr, so I brought the sword to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Go and throw him into custody. I returned with nothing. Only God knows who killed my brother and took my loot. I only stayed a short time before Surah Al-Anfal was revealed, and the Messenger of God called me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: So he said: Go and take your sword. (Ahmed 180)"
"33758","(33758) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Ibn Umar invaded Iraq, and he said Omar said: “It has reached me that you have confronted a monster. He said: Yes. He liked that, so he carried out his plunder.”"
"33759","(33759) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qays, on the authority of Shubr ibn Alqamiya, who said: I fought a man one day. Al-Qadisiyyah was one of the non-Arabs. She killed him and took his plunder, so she went to Saad. Saad addressed his companions, then said: This is the plunder of a span. It is better than twelve thousand dirhams, and indeed We have granted it to him."
"33760","(33760) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun and Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, Ibn Aoun: Al-Bara’ bin Malik attacked Al-Bara’ bin Malik, and Hisham said: Al-Bara’ bin Malik attacked the marzban of the pilgrimage on the day of the visit, and stabbed him. He stabbed you, Qarbus beat his saddle, killed him, and took away his bracelets and his girdle. When we came, he prayed the Umar Fajr prayer, then he came to us, and said: He sinned. Abu Talha? So he came out to him and said: We did not give a fifth of the plunder, and if the innocent plundered money, then a fifth of it, so it amounted to six thousand, then it reached thirty thousand, Muhammad said: Anas bin Malik told me that it was the first five-figure robbery in Islam."
"33761","(33761) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said The plunder was not a fifth, so the first plunder of a fifth in Islam was the plunder of Al-Bara’ ibn Malik, and he was charged with the duty of the visitor. So he stabbed him with the spear until it struck Qarbus from the lamp, then he came down to him and cut off his girdle and bracelets. He said: When we came to Medina Omar bin Al-Khattab prayed the lunch prayer, then he came to us and said: Peace be upon you. Abu Talha sinned, so he said: Yes, so he went out to him. Then Omar said: We did not give a fifth of the loot, and if Al-Bara’ bin Malik robbed money and I am the fifth of it, so he called the assessors, so make thirty. A thousand, then he took six thousand from it."
"33762","(33762) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, he said: I narrated, On the authority of Abu Qatada al-Ansari that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever kills a dead person will have his plunder. He said, So I said: O Messenger of God, I killed a man who plundered, then you prevented me from fighting him, but I do not know who plundered him. A man from the family said: Mecca: He has spoken the truth, O Messenger of God. He killed a man, so I robbed him, so I took him away from him. Abu Bakr said: No, by God, do not do that. You will go. To one of the lions of God who fought on his behalf, he would share it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He spoke the truth, give him his plunder.\n(Bukhari 2100 mm 1370)"
"33763","(33763) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah bin Ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, on the authority of his father, he said: I fought a man and killed him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who killed this? They said: Ibn Al-Akwa', he said: He has plundered him. (Muslim 1374. Abu Dawud 2447)"
"33764","(33764) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah; Al-Zubair went out with a man and killed him. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ransacked him. (Abdul Razzaq 9477. Tahawi 226)"
"33765","(33765) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of God granted us permission. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is his sword, meaning Abu Jahl. (Abu Dawud 2716; Abu Ali 5209)"
"33766","(33766) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais Al-Abdi, on the authority of Shubr bin Alqamiya, he said: On the Day of Al-Qadisiyah, a man from the people of Persia rose up and called for a duel. He mentioned his bone, so a short man called Shubar bin Alqamah stood up to him. He said: The Persian said: Thus, it means that he endured it, then he struck the ground with it and it knocked him down. He said: Then he took a span of the dagger that the Persian had with him, and he said with it: In his stomach like this, meaning he subdued him, then he turned against him and killed him, then he brought his plunder to Saad, and twelve people sat in front of him. A thousand, so he granted it to him."
"33767","(33767) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Nafi’ saying: We have never stopped hearing when he met Muslims and infidels. If a man of the Muslims kills a man of the infidels, then his robbing him is his, unless he is with you in the fighting. For it is not known who killed the dead person."
"33768","(33768) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about looting. He said: There is no plunder except from a voluntary act, and in the voluntary act there are five."
"33769","(33769) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Harry, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but God. Then They said: They protected their wealth and their blood by it, and their account is with Allah."
"33770","(33770) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i Saad bin Tariq, he said: I heard my father say: I heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Whoever is one with God and disbelieves in what is worshiped other than Him, his property and blood will be forbidden, and his reckoning will be on him. God"
"33771","(33771) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid, who said: We sent the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to the burnings from Jinnah. He said: “Then we woke up in the morning and the people had been warned of us.” He said: “So we went out in their wake.” Then I met a man among them, and when I caught up with him, he said: There is no god but Allah. He said: So I thought that he was just saying it in discord. He said: So she got pregnant. Ali, so I killed him, and I was in my mind about his situation, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: To the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He said: There is no god but God. Then you killed him. I said: O Messenger of God, he did not say it on his own initiative. He only said it to a group of weapons, he said: so he said: he said: there is no god but Allah, then you killed him, so why not break his heart until you know He only said it with a detachment of weapons. Osama said: He kept repeating it to me: He said: There is no god but Allah. Then I killed him until I wish I had not converted to Islam until that day."
"33772","(33772) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Asama, who said: We sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash."
"33773","(33773) Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Samimi narrated to us, saying: Hatim bin Abi Saghira narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim that Amr bin Aws told him that his father Aws told him: We are sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he is telling us a story. And he reminds us when a man came to him and asked him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Go and kill him. When the man turned to him, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him and said: Do you bear witness that there is no god but God? He said: Yes. He said: Go and be alone. His way. I was commanded only to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. If they do that, their blood will be forbidden to me. And their money."
"33774","(33774) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. If they say: There is no god but Allah, they will be protected from my blood. And their wealth is only for its due, and their account is with Allah. Then he recited: (You are only a Reminder, and you have no control over them.)"
"33775","(33775) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salih, the client of the twins, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but God. When they say: There is no god but God, Their blood and their property are inviolable to me except according to what is due, and their reckoning is with God."
"33776","(33776) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amrah, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, he said: Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad went out on a expedition and said: They passed a man among his spoils and wanted to kill him, so he said: There is no god but God. So Miqdad killed him, and it was said to him: I killed him while he says: There is no god but Allah. So Miqdad said: He wished to flee with his family. And what about him? He said: When they came, they mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was revealed: “O you who have believed, when you strike For the sake of God, seek knowledge and do not say to the one who greets you, “You are not a believer”; you seek to gain the life of this world.} He said: The spoils {For with God are many spoils. Thus you were before} He said: You conceal your faith from the polytheists. {So, from God’s favor upon you} so they proclaimed Islam {so you understood} the promise of God {Indeed, God is ever aware of what you do}"
"33777","(33777) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He passed A man from Banu Sulaym was with a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had some of his sheep with him. He greeted them, and they said: What? He greeted you, except to seek refuge from you. So they went to him, killed him, and took his sheep and brought them to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. upon him and grant him peace, then God Almighty revealed: {O you who have believed, when you strike in the way of God, then investigate and do not say to whom I extend my greetings to you. You are not a believer. You seek the reward of the life of this world; for with Allah are many spoils. Until the end of the verses."
"33778","(33778) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, something similar to it, and no Mention, they brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"33779","(33779) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, saying: Laith ibn Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Zayd. Al-Laythi, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Adi bin Al-Khayar, on the authority of Al-Miqdad, that he informed him that he said: O Messenger of God What do you think if I met a man from the infidels and he fought me and struck one of my hands with a sword and cut it off, then he took refuge from me under a tree and said: I have submitted to God. I will kill him, O Messenger of God, after he said it. He said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do not kill him. So I said: O The Messenger of God cut off my hand, then he said that after he cut it off, should I kill him? He said: Do not kill him, for if you kill him, it is In your position before you killed him, and you are in your position before he said the words that he said."
"33780","(33780) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: Abu Al-Aliyah came to me and to a companion of mine, and he said: Come on, you are younger than me and more knowledgeable of hadith than me. He said: So we set off until We came to Bishr bin Asim Al-Laythi, and Abu Al-Aliyah said: He narrated these two hadiths of yours, and he said: Uqba bin Malik narrated to me. Al-Laythi said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a convoy who raided the people, and a man from among the people strayed, and a man from among them followed him. The prisoner had a sharp sword with him. He said: The deviant one of the people. Indeed, he is a Muslim. He did not consider what he said. He said: He struck him and killed him. Then the hadith was transmitted to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said a strong word, and it reached the killer. While the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was delivering a sermon, the killer said: By God, O Prophet of God, he did not say that except as a means of seeking refuge. From killing, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from it, and from those among the people who distracted him, he did that twice, all of that. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from him and did not have patience. The third man said something like that, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from him. May God bless him and grant him peace by his face. The evening will be known by his face. He said: God has rejected me regarding whoever kills a believer three times. He says that"
"33781","(33781) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Aban bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Jarir narrated to me, on the authority of Jarir, he said: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me to Yemen. I will fight them and call upon them. When they say: There is no god Except Allah, their wealth and their blood are forbidden to you."
"33782","(33782) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Sufyan bin Husayn informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, he said: When someone who apostatized against the covenant of Abu Bakr, Abu Bakr wanted to militate against them, so he said Omar: Should I fight them when I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Who bears witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger? God has forbidden his wealth except according to His rights and judgment is with God. Abu Bakr said: I will fight whoever differentiates between prayer and zakat, by God. I will fight whoever separates them until they are united. Omar said: So we fought with him, and he was of sound mind. So when he defeated whoever of them defeated him, He said: They chose two qualities from me: either a shameful war or a shameful sin. They said: This is a shameful war. We know it, so what is the shameful situation? He said: You bear witness that those who killed us are in Paradise and that those who killed you are in Hell, so they did so."
"33783","(33783) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was ordered to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. (Bukhari 392, Abu Dawud 2634)"
"33784","(33784) Abdullah bin Numayr and Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, He said: I found a woman killed in one of the raids of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, regarding the killing of women and children. (Bukhari 3014, Muslim 3)"
"33785","(33785) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqasam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade killing women. (Ahmad 2561. Tabarani 12082)"
"33786","(33786) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: I heard a man narrating Manna, on the authority of his father, who said: He was sent The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He forbade us from killing the unjust and the poor.\n(Ahmad 13. Saeed 2628)"
"33787","(33787) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Ka’b, on the authority of his uncle, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When he sent to Ibn Abi Al-Haqiq, he forbade him from killing women and children. (Abdul Razzaq 9385. Malik 447)"
"33788","(33788) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said : Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would send a convoy or an army, he would say: Do not kill a newborn."
"33789","(33789) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Murqi` bin Abdullah bin Sayfi, on the authority of Hanzala the writer said: We attacked with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we passed by a woman who had been killed, and he had gathered over her. The people, he said, so they let him go. He said: This woman does not fight. Who should she fight for? Then he said to a man: Go to Khalid bin The newborn, so say to him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commands you: Do not kill his offspring or a violent man. (Abu Dawud 2462 and Ahmad 488)"
"33790","(33790) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Farz, he said: Anas bin Malik, he said: I was carrying the luggage of my companions, and when we were mobilized, we would camp in the back of the city, until he came out to us. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Go in the name of God, and in the way of God you fight the enemies of God in the way of God, no You shall kill neither an old man nor a mortal, nor a young child, nor a woman, and do not go to extremes. (Abu Dawud 2607)"
"33791","(33791) Abdullah bin Numir told us, he said: Ubaid Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar wrote to the princes The soldiers are not to kill a woman or a child, but to kill those who have been subjected to grief."
"33792","(33792) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, who said: The letter of Omar came to us. Do not exceed, do not betray, and do not kill a child, and fear God regarding the farmers."
"33793","(33793) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: I narrated that Abu Bakr sent armies to the Levant. Then the follower of Yazid bin Abi Sufyan came out and said: I command you to do ten things: Do not kill a child, a woman, or old and old, and do not cut down a fruitful tree, and do not destroy an inhabited land, and do not barrow any sheep or herds, except for food, and do not drown them. Palm trees, and do not burn them, or break them, or cowardly."
"33794","(33794) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A boy shall not be killed in war, nor Neither the woman, nor the mortal old man, nor food shall be burned, nor palm trees, nor houses shall be destroyed, nor shall fruitful trees be cut down."
"33795","(33795) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He hated being killed in a place of war, the great sheikh. And the child and the woman, and it was disliked for the man if he carried any of these with him and it was too burdensome for him to throw it into. The way"
"33796","(33796) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, he said: I heard Atiyya al-Qurazi He says: We presented it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Qurayz, and whoever sprouted was killed, and whoever did not sprouted was abandoned. On his way\n(Ibn Majah 2541)"
"33797","(33797) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Fazara, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Amri al-Ansari. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a killed woman, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who killed This, then a man said: I, O Messenger of God, put her behind me and she wanted to kill me, so I killed her, so he ordered her to be buried. (Abu Dawud 333)"
"33798","(33798) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sadiqa al-Dimashqi narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Yahya al-Ghassani, saying: I wrote To Omar bin Abdul Aziz, I ask him about these verses: {And fight in the way of Allah those who fight you, but do not transgress. God does not like aggressors. He said: Then he wrote to me: This applies to women and offspring and whoever among them does not wage war."
"33799","(33799) Kathir bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, saying: Thabit bin Al-Hajjaj Al-Kalabi narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr stood up among the people and thanked and praised God, then said: The monk should not be killed while fasting."
"33800","(33800) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri and Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Yazid. Ibn Hurmuz said: Najda wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about the killing of infants, and he said in his letter: Indeed, the world The companion of Moses had killed the newborn. He said: Then Yazid said: I wrote the letter of Ibn Abbas with my own hand to help him: You have written You ask about infanticide, and you say in your book: The scholar who was the companion of Moses killed the newborn, and if you had known what the infants were, That scholar knew about that child. You killed him, but you do not know. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade He killed them and isolated them. (Tirmidhi 1556, Muslim 1444)"
"33801","(33801) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Aslam, Omar’s client, that Omar wrote to His workers forbade them from killing women and children and commanded them to kill those who suffered consolation."
"33802","(33802) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: They were not They kill the merchants of the polytheists."
"33803","(33803) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of al-Aswad ibn Saree’, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: What is the matter with people who have gone so far in killing, to the point of killing children? ! He said: Then a man from among the people said: They are only the children of the polytheists, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Isn’t it? The best of you are the children of the polytheists?! No child is born, except according to his natural disposition, until he reaches puberty and expresses himself, or is converted by his parents. Or make him Christian. (Ahmad 435, Darmi 2463)"
"33804","(33804) Humaid bin Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Medina who was a client of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would send out his armies, he would say: Do not kill The owners of the silos. (Ahmad 3000, Bazzar 1677)"
"33805","(33805) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: He used to forbid killing women and old men. The big one"
"33806","(33806) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Arta, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd bin Jad’an, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Muti’ reported that Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq sent an army and said: Conquer in the name of God, O God, make their death A witness in your path, then he said: You will come to a people in their cells, and they have called upon them, and they have not done theirselves for it. And you come to a people who have examined the middle of their heads like nerves, so strike what they have examined from the middle of their heads."
"33807","(33807) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade And peace be upon him, regarding the killing of women, children, and the old man who cannot move."
"33808","(33808) Affan told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Abu Ruq Atiya bin al-Harith told us, he said: Abu Al-Ghuraif Ubaidullah bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Assal, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent Secretly, he said: Do not kill a newborn. (Ibn Majah 2857. Ahmed 240)"
"33809","(33809) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The hard one informed me. Ibn Juthama reported that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about one of the homes of the polytheists who spend the night and among them are women. And the two children, and he said: They are among them. (Bukhari 3012, Muslim 1364)"
"33810","(33810) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Kill the polytheist sheikhs and spare their elders alive.\n(ابوداؤد ۲۶۶۳۔ احمد ۱۲)"
"33811","(33811) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace"
"33812","(33812) Muhammad bin Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: I asked Al-Zuhri about the enemy, if he appears against them, should he be killed? Alawuj, he said: Omar used to kill the Alawuj when he appeared among them, and they were taken captive in addition to that."
"33813","(33813) Zaid told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a woman from among the polytheists goes out to fight, let her be killed."
"33814","(33814) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Bukair Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Ibrahim Al-Dawsi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah Al-Dawsi, he said: We sent a messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was in secret, and said: If you defeat so-and-so and so-and-so, burn them with fire, even if they are The next day he sent for us. I had ordered you to burn these two men and I saw that he should not be tortured."
"33815","(33815) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas that he mentioned people whom he burned. Ali, and he said: If it had been me, I would not have burned them with fire, because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Do not torture them with the punishment of God.” If it were me, I would have killed them, according to the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever changes his religion, kill him."
"33816","(33816) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: He told us on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdul Allah bin Masoud, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not torture with fire, for he does not torture with fire. Except her Lord. (Abu Dawud 2468, Hakim 239)"
"33817","(33817) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent He greeted his concubines, so they looked for a man who climbed a tree, so they burned it with fire. When they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, they informed him. With that, he changed?? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him and said: I was not sent to be punished with the punishment of God, but I was sent to strike necks and severely The bonds"
"33818","(33818) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham al-Dastawwi told us, on the authority of Sa’id al-Bazzaz, on the authority of Uthman bin Hayyan, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’. She saw a man taking a lice or a flea and throwing it into the fire, and she said: No one should be tortured with torture. God"
"33819","(33819) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated that you be burned. The scorpion in fire, and they say: the same."
"33820","(33820) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, Abi Hubaira, that he hated to be burned. Scorpion with fire."
"33821","(33821) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi and Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cut down the palm trees of Banu al-Nadir and burned them. (Ahmad 8. Bukhari 3021)"
"33822","(33822) Waki’ told us, he said: Salih bin Abi Al-Akhdar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Asama, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to a land called Abna, and he said: Come to it in the morning, then burn it."
"33823","(33823) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I was informed on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz that he ordered the burning, or He burned"
"33824","(33824) Abu Bakr ibn Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafli that Ali burned his heretics in the market, When he threw fire at them, he said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Then he left, and I followed him. He turned to me. Suwayd said: I said: Yes, so I said: O Commander of the Faithful, I heard you saying something, so he said: O Suwayd, I am with a ignorant people, so if you hear me say: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the truth."
"33825","(33825) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ubaid, on the authority of his father, he said: There were people They received gifts and provision and prayed with the people, and they worshiped idols in secret, so Ali bin Abi Talib was brought to them. So he put them in the mosque, or he said in the prison, then he said: O people, what do you see in a people who used to take With you are gifts and provision, and they worship these idols. The people said: Kill them. He said: No, but do to them as they did. Through our father Abraham, so he burned them with fire."
"33826","(33826) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Jarir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Won’t you give me relief from Dhu Al-Khalasah, the house that belonged to Khath’am, where she used to worship? The Jahiliyya, it is called the Yamani Ka’bah. He said: So it came out with fifty and a hundred riders. He said: So we burned it. Until We made it like a mangy camel. He said: Jarir sent a man to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to give him good tidings. When he came Ali, he said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I did not come to you until We left it like a mangy camel. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, blessed him. May God bless Ahmose, her horses and men, five times."
"33827","(33827) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ibn Abdullah bin Al-Hasan, on the authority of his father, that he did not see By burning and cutting down trees in the enemy's land."
"33828","(33828) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah {whatever linah you cut} he said: The palm tree without the palm tree."
"33829","(33829) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Amr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr {what you have cut off from Soft}, he said: This is the palm tree."
"33830","(33830) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {Whatever linah you cut}, He said: This is the palm tree."
"33831","(33831) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muslim bin Saeed told us, he said: Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman told us Ibn Khubayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out to go and I came to him. And a man from my people. We said: We are ashamed for our people to witness a battle that we would not witness with them. He said: Have you both converted to Islam? We said: No. He said: We do not seek help from the polytheists against the polytheists. He said: So we submitted to Islam and witnessed with him. (Ahmad 454, Hakim 121)"
"33832","(33832) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Mundhir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out May God bless him and grant him peace to Uhud. When he left the farewell prayer, he looked behind him and saw a rough booklet. He said: Who are these? They said: Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul and his followers were Jews. He said: They have embraced Islam. They said: No. He said: We do not seek help. By the infidels against the polytheists."
"33833","(33833) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, he said: Someone who heard al-Qasim narrated to me, on the authority of Salman bin Rabi’a Al-Bailili said that he invaded Balanjar, and he invaded, so he sought help from people from the polytheists against the polytheists, and he said: To carry The enemies of God are the enemies of God."
"33834","(33834) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Yazeed, on the authority of Ibn Nayyar, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We do not seek help from a polytheist. (Muslim 1449. Abu Dawud 2726)"
"33835","(33835) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invaded with people from the Jews and made peace with them. (Bayhaqi 53)"
"33836","(33836) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to attack the Jews and deal them arrows like the arrows of the Muslims. (Abu Dawud 282)"
"33837","(33837) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, attacks the Jews and makes them happy. (Abu Dawud 281, Tirmidhi 1558)"
"33838","(33838) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, that Saad bin Malik invaded a people of The Jews submitted to them."
"33839","(33839) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I asked Amir about Muslims fighting against the People of the Book? Amer said: I realized that the Imams, both jurists and non-jurists, fight against the people of Dhimmah, and they divide among them and give away from them part of their tribute, so that is it. May they have a good deed."
"33840","(33840) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, he said: I have overtaken the Imams."
"33841","(33841) Abu Asama and Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, granted the horse two arrows and one arrow for the man. (Bukhari 2863. Muslim 1383)"
"33842","(33842) Muhammad bin Fudayl and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, granted the knight three shares; One arrow for him, and two for his horse. (Abu Ali 2522)"
"33843","(33843) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Umari narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided two shares for the horse and one share for the man, three shares for the man and his horse. Names (Daraqutni 106)"
"33844","(33844) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, contributed two hundred horses on the Day of Khaybar, each horse receiving two shares. (Saeed bin Mansour 2744 and Abdul Razzaq 9323)"
"33845","(33845) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhail, he said: Our companions narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad’s companions. May God bless him and grant him peace; They said: The horse has two arrows, and the man has two arrows."
"33846","(33846) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Usama bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Makhul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He handed over two arrows to the horse and one arrow to the man. (Saeed bin Mansour 2769. Abdul Razzaq 9319)"
"33847","(33847) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made two arrows for the horses. And the knight gets an arrow."
"33848","(33848) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: The first person to assign two arrows to the horse was Omar. A man from Banu Tamim. (Saeed bin Mansour 2770)"
"33849","(33849) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, who said: He gave a share to Al-Zubayr. Four shares; Two arrows for his horse, one arrow for him, and one arrow for his mother and his relatives. (Nasa’i 4434. Tahawi 283)"
"33850","(33850) Abdul Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to us while we In Khorasan: We have reached the trustworthy news on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He gave the knight three shares; He made two arrows for his horse, two arrows for him, and he made two arrows for the man, and he said about horses: the godfather, the harriers, and the rodents. Either way (Saeed bin Mansour 2773)"
"33851","(33851) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Siwar, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, who said: They were They invaded and captured the spoils. They divided three shares from the spoils to the knight when they were divided. Two arrows for his horse, one arrow for him, and one arrow for the foot."
"33852","(33852) Waki’ told us, Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, contributed. He handed two arrows to the horseman, and one to the footman."
"33853","(33853) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Sha’ithī narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, he said: The Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, grants the horse two arrows, and two arrows to the man. (Bayhaqi 53)"
"33854","(33854) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Amr bin Maimun told us, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to People of the island: As for what follows, the arrows were at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, two arrows for the Persians. And an arrow for the man, and I did not think that anyone intended to deprive him of his obligation, until men from among those who were fighting did so. Fortresses, so return our arrows to what they were during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Two arrows for the horse and one arrow for the man, and how the arrows of horses are placed, and by God’s permission they will be put to rest at night. And to make peace with them by the fire, and to seek what they seek. (Saeed bin Mansour 2761)"
"33855","(33855) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad; Zubayr was given four shares: two shares for his horse, one share for his mother, and one share for a relative."
"33856","(33856) A lecturer told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Aamir, he said: When Saad bin Abi Waqqas conquered, Jalulaila attacked the Muslims. Thirty thousand mithqals, so he divided to the horseman three thousand mithqals, and to the man a thousand mithqals."
"33857","(33857) Muadh told us, he said: Habib bin Shihab told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Musa; He contributed two shares to the horseman, and he contributed two shares to the man."
"33858","(33858) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Mujma’ bin Yaqoub narrated to us, saying: My father informed me, on the authority of his uncle Abdul Rahman. Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Mujma’ Ibn Jariyah, who said: We witnessed the Hudaybiyah with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so it was divided He had eighteen arrows, and the army was one thousand and five hundred: three hundred knights, so the knight had two arrows.\n(Abu Dawud 2730, Ahmed 420)"
"33859","(33859) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hani bin Hani, on the authority of Ali, who said: To Al-Faris Saman Shu`ba said: I found it written there."
"33860","(33860) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Maymun informed us, saying: Ja’un bin Al-Harith wrote, and he By the borders of Malatiya, to Omar bin Abdul Aziz: There are men who fight with horses with a weak trunk or two, which do not have the strength. A response from the Muslims. A man fights with a strong bardhun, which is not inferior to a horse, but it is said: Bardhun, so what? Does the Commander of the Faithful think of her? So Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to him: Look at what is one of those weak horses that have no response to them. Muslims, so inform its companions that you have changed its name, whether they set off with it or left it, and what one of those two buds is is wonderful. Running and looking, so make your contribution to the good-looking horse."
"33861","(33861) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The bardhun is in the same position as the horse."
"33862","(33862) Abbad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The owner of the paradise will receive an arrow from the spoils."
"33863","(33863) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sha’ithī narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, he said: The Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, grants two shares to the godfather, and two shares to the hybrid. (Abu Dawud 286)"
"33864","(33864) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Rashid narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, who said: Abu Musa wrote to Omar: We When we conquered Tustur, we were struck by horses that were ashamed, so he wrote to him: These are the rodents, the emancipation of which is disgusting, so break them, and cancel them. Nothing else"
"33865","(33865) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qais, and Ibrahim ibn Al-Muntashir, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aqmar, who said: The horses raided the Levant, and they overtook the horses that day, and the horses overtook them tomorrow morning, so Ibn Abi said: Khamisa: I do not consider the one who catches you as one who does not catch you. So he wrote to Omar, and Omar said: Al-Wadi’i’s mother has gone mad. I was reminded of it, they followed what he said. (Fazzari 244)"
"33866","(33866) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Sabah bin Thabit Al-Bajli narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Sha’abi saying: Al-Mundhir bin Al-Darr bin Hamisa went out in search of the enemy, and the horses followed the freedman, and the horses were cut into pieces, so he contributed to the godfather, Samin. And for the two camels an arrow, then he wrote about that to Omar, and he liked that, and a year for horses was carried out after that."
"33867","(33867) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy (h) and Sharik, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, On the authority of Kulthum bin Al-Aqmar: Al-Mundhir ibn al-Dahar ibn Hamisa went out in pursuit of the enemy, and the horses chased after the liberation, and the birds were cut off, so he was defeated. For the horses, but he did not contribute to the rodents, so he wrote about that to Omar, and Omar was pleased with that, so Omar said in the hadith of one of them: Al-Wadaei is saddened by his mother. She is reminded of him."
"33868","(33868) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The disgusting person has an arrow, and he is the hajin, and his companion has an arrow."
"33869","(33869) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Shaykh Hamdan, on the authority of Omar; Similar to the hadith of Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy."
"33870","(33870) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul He said: The hybrids have an arrow."
"33871","(33871) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Horses and parrots are the same."
"33872","(33872) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: None of our scholars used to contribute to Al-Bardhun."
"33873","(33873) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave the mule an arrow. And to the man an arrow."
"33874","(33874) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The mule is a man."
"33875","(33875) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, He said: They did not make shares for a mule, nor for a paradise, nor for a donkey."
"33876","(33876) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who is on a campaign, and the horses are with him: the spoils are not divided among him, except for two horses."
"33877","(33877) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, He said: It is not permissible to contribute to more than two horses if they belong to one man, and anything other than that is considered a corpse."
"33878","(33878) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, and Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: We witnessed a battle with Sa’id. Ibn Othman, and with me was Hani Ibn Hani, and with him were two horsemen, and with Hani two horsemen, so he contributed five shares for himself and the two horsemen. He gave five shares to Hani and his horse."
"33879","(33879) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: No arrow for more than two horses. There were horsemen with the man who had five arrows; Four for his horse, and an arrow for him."
"33880","(33880) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: If a man trained horses, he Every horse has an arrow."
"33881","(33881) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Umair, the servant of Abi al-Lahm, who said: I witnessed Khaybar. And I am a slave-owner, so when they conquered it, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me a sword, and he said: Imitate this, and he gave it to me. Of the heirloom goods, and he did not strike me with an arrow. (Abu Dawud 2724; Ahmed 223)"
"33882","(33882) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd bin Muhajir bin Qunfud, on the authority of Umair. The master of Abi Lahm. He said: I witnessed with the master of Khaybar while I was your master, but he did not divide any of the spoils for me. And He gave me a sword from among my possessions, which I would reward when I acquired it. (Ibn Majah 2855)"
"33883","(33883) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, said: The slave does not get any of the spoils."
"33884","(33884) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He has no share in the spoils. share"
"33885","(33885) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin. They said: Who witnessed the battle? Whoever is free, or a slave, or a hired worker, has a share."
"33886","(33886) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Hasan, Ibn Sirin, and al-Hakam. They said: The servant And the hired servants, when they witness the battle, will be given part of the spoils."
"33887","(33887) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the merchant and the slave bear witness, It was divided for him, and it was divided for the servant."
"33888","(33888) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: Shares are given to the slave."
"33889","(33889) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of his maternal uncle Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Qurayh, He said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq swore to me as he swore to my master."
"33890","(33890) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the spoils taken by the army, he said: If the merchant and the slave help them, they will be struck with their arrows along with the army."
"33891","(33891) Waki` bin al-Jarrah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Rashid narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon women, boys and horses. (Abu Dawud 289. Bayhaqi 53)"
"33892","(33892) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, and Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Zayd bin Hurmuz said: Najdad wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about women, whether they were attending the war with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Will he hit them with an arrow? He said: Then Yazid said: I wrote a letter from Ibn Abbas with my own hand to help you. You wrote to ask me about women. Are they? Will they attend the war with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Did he hit them with an arrow? They were present with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but as for him hitting them with an arrow, no, and it was He submits to them."
"33893","(33893) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of al-Awwam ibn Muzahim, on the authority of Khalid ibn Sihan, he said: I witnessed with my father. Musa had four or five wives, one of whom was the mother of Majza’ bin Thawr, and they used to give him water to drink and treat the wounded. So he contributed to them."
"33894","(33894) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Sufyan Ibn Wahhab Al-Khawlani said: Omar divided their spoils among the people, and gave each person a dinar, and made a share for the woman and the man. Equally, if a man is with his wife, he gives her a dinar, and if he is alone, he gives her half a dinar."
"33895","(33895) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abbas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nayyar. On the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with beads on a gazelle, and he divided them among the free and female slaves, and Aisha said: It was My father divides between the freeman and the slave. (Abu Dawud 2945, Ahmed 156)"
"33896","(33896) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: We came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after the conquest of Khaybar with three, so he swore an oath for us, and he did not swear to anyone who had not witnessed the conquest. We changed it. (Bukhari 3136, Muslim 1946)"
"33897","(33897) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, who said: Omar wrote to Saad on the day Al-Qadisiyah: Indeed, I have sent to you the people of the Hijaz and the people of the Levant, so who of them caught up with the fighting before they agreed? So make peace with them."
"33898","(33898) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Habib; That Abu Bakr sent Ikrimah bin Abi Jal as a support for Al-Muhajir bin Abi Umayyah and Ziyad bin Labid Al-Bayadhi. So they came to the people, and victory had been granted to them, and the people were in their blood. He said: So share with them in their spoils."
"33899","(33899) Yazeed bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Al-Hikam; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, swore an oath to Ja’far and his companions on the Day of Khabar, but they did not witness the event. (Abu Dawud 277)"
"33900","(33900) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab Al-Ahmasi, who said: The Banu Attarid attacked a hundred of the people of Basra and supplied Ammar from Kufa. Ammar came out before the battle and said: We Your partners in the spoils. Then a man from the tribe of Atarid stood up and said: O proud servant! You were injured in the name of God. Do you want us to divide our spoils with you? Ammar said: You reproached me for what I love or for what is best for my ears. He said: And he wrote about that to Omar, so Omar wrote: The spoils For those who witnessed the event."
"33901","(33901) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: Omar said: But The spoils are for those who witness the event. (Bayhaqi 50, Abdul Razzaq 9689)"
"33902","(33902) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Shu`ba narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hikam, on the authority of Abraham; Some people came to Ali on the day of the camel after the fall, and he said: These are the deprived, so swear to them."
"33903","(33903) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, he said: The Messenger of God was sent May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he led a group of people, and they captured some of his spoils, and after them a people came, and the following verse was revealed: “In their wealth there is a known right.” For the beggar and the deprived}"
"33904","(33904) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Qais bin Kurkum, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {For the beggar and the deprived}, he said: the distorted words. (Tabari 29)"
"33905","(33905) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Qais bin Kurkum, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {For the beggar and the deprived}. He said: The deprived is the one who has no share in Islam."
"33906","(33906) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Salma bin Nubait narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent He handed over the vanguards, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took his spoils and divided them among the people. He did not divide anything to the vanguards, so when The vanguards came, and they said: He divided the spoils and did not divide them for us, so it was revealed: {And it is not for a prophet to deceive}. (Tabari 156)"
"33907","(33907) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The deprived one who has no money. The spoils are something."
"33908","(33908) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: The deprived who is not He has something in the spoils."
"33909","(33909) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I wrote to Nafi’ asking him about a man who is in secret. He got pregnant without the permission of his princess? So he wrote: The permission of his prince will not change it."
"33910","(33910) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Hassan, who said: If two limbs meet, it is not for the man to carry. Without the permission of his Imam."
"33911","(33911) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He does not travel in a concubine, except with the permission of its prince. And to them is what He bestows upon them of anything."
"33912","(33912) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the expedition spreads, they will not succeed. Or spoils, if the Imam wishes, he may give them as spoils, and if he wishes, five of them."
"33913","(33913) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a convoy goes out with the permission of the Imam and they take spoils, he takes The five imams, and the rest of them."
"33914","(33914) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: I mentioned to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I invaded the route, and when we led convoys there, they sent out the companies after we directed convoys, and it was said: What you have taken is nothing but spoils. One-fifth, and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: People did not perform voluntary voluntary prayers except by one-fifth."
"33915","(33915) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Which one? A woman who raided without the permission of her prince is fraudulent."
"33916","(33916) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I asked Ibrahim about the Imam sending the secret. So you take sheep? He said: If he wishes, he can grant them all of them, and if he wishes, five of them."
"33917","(33917) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If they departed with the permission of the Imam, he took a fifth, and it was They have what remains, and if they leave without the Imam’s permission, then it is the worst of the army."
"33918","(33918) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, on the authority of Imran al-Qattan, on the authority of Ali bin Thabit, who said: I asked an alcoholic person and a giving person about The imam will let the people know what happened to them? He said: That is for them."
"33919","(33919) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He was asked about plundering the spoils if their prince gave them permission? He thought that"
"33920","(33920) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ransomed two men from the Muslims for one man from the polytheists from Banu Aqeel. \n(Tirmidhi 1568, Muslim 1262)"
"33921","(33921) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah bin Ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Iyas bin Salma bin Al-Akwa’, on the authority of his father, he said We went on a campaign with Abu Bakr as a supporter of the covenant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so a maid from his children sent off to me and we visited him. She is one of the most beautiful Arabs. She had a garment on her, and I did not reveal her garment until I came to Medina, and we met the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He was in the market, and he said: To God is your father. He gave it to me. So I gave it to him. He said: So he sent it away. So he ransomed her among the Muslim captives who were in Mecca."
"33922","(33922) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’, who said regarding a captive of the polytheists: On him, or may he be redeemed."
"33923","(33923) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Juwayriyah, and Asim ibn Kulayb al-Jarami; Omar bin Abdul Aziz ransomed a man from among the Muslims from the crime of the people of war in the amount of one hundred thousand."
"33924","(33924) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad: If the slave girl or the boy is taken captive by the enemy, there is no harm in taking him captive. To benefit them"
"33925","(33925) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; In the prisoner: he is bestowed upon him, or he is ransomed."
"33926","(33926) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: On the day of Badr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What do you say about these captives? He said: Then he said: None of them will escape except by ransom, or by beheading. (Tirmidhi 1714. Ahmad 383)"
"33927","(33927) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God wrote May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a decree between the immigrants and the Ansar: that they should relieve their strongholds, and that they should ransom their suffering. By virtue and reconciliation among Muslims."
"33928","(33928) Waki’ told us, he said: Usama bin Zayd told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: He said: Omar: Because I rescue a Muslim man from the hands of the infidels is more beloved to me than my Arab counterpart."
"33929","(33929) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Mujahid, who said: Abu Bakr said: If you take anyone from The polytheists, so you were given for it an amount of dinars, so do not redeem it."
"33930","(33930) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Yahya; Khalid bin Zayd, whose eye was infected with a tick, said: We besieged its city, and we met a soldier, and the Commander of the Muslims Abu Musa, and Al-Dhaqan took his covenant and the covenant of those with him, so Abu Musa said: Isolate them, so he proceeded to isolate them, and Abu Musa made Moses says to his companions: I hope that God will deceive him about himself, but he isolated them and remained the enemy of God. So Abu commanded him to do so. Moses ransomed and spent a lot of money, but he refused and beheaded him."
"33931","(33931) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A person was killed. On the Day of the Trench, the Muslims defeated the polytheists over his corpse, so they said: Give us his corpse and we will give you ten Thousands of dirhams. This was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: We have no need of his dead body or blood money. An evil person, an evil person, an evil person. (Ahmad 248. Bayhaqi 133)"
"33932","(33932) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hikam; A man from the polytheists was injured on the day of the ditch, so they gave the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, his corpse until they reached Blood money, but he refused. (Ahmed 248)"
"33933","(33933) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace; In the same way (Tirmidhi 1715. Ahmad 326)"
"33934","(33934) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: The verse “And kill them wherever you find them” was abrogated. Before that, of ransom, or of manna."
"33935","(33935) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; In his saying: {Either from us after, or as a ransom} He said: neither from, nor from a ransom."
"33936","(33936) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Amr, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him during the captivity on the day of Badr. Then Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, your people and your clan are the sons of your uncle, so take from them. ransom, and Omar said: Kill them, so the following verse was revealed: {It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has established wealth in the land} He said Mujahid: and Al-Ithkhan: which means killing. (Ibn Jarir 43)"
"33937","(33937) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: Omar said: Every captive who was in the hands of the polytheist Muslims, then he was released from The treasury of Muslims."
"33938","(33938) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Bishr bin Ghalib, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr asked Al-Hasan Ibn Ali, on the authority of a man who fights on behalf of the people of the religion, and is captured? He said: So he redeemed it from the taxes of those people on whose behalf he fought."
"33939","(33939) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the people of the covenant, when the polytheists took them captive, and then the Muslims conquered them, he said: They will not be enslaved."
"33940","(33940) Ali bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: The slave shall not be ransomed, Nor the covenants."
"33941","(33941) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He hated killing prisoners."
"33942","(33942) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He used to say: The prisoner should not be killed."
"33943","(33943) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He hated killing a prisoner."
"33944","(33944) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: When a prisoner was brought to Ali on the day of Siffin, he took his animal, took his weapon, ordered him not to return, and released him on his way."
"33945","(33945) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Fakhita, who said: A neighbor of mine told me, he said: I went to Ali. As a prisoner on the day of Siffin, he said: I will not kill you out of patience, for I fear God, Lord of the worlds."
"33946","(33946) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Khalid bin Ja’far, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Al-Hajjaj brought a captive, and he said to Abdullah bin Omar: Arise and kill him. Ibn Omar said: This is not what we have been commanded. God says: {Until when you have made them weak, then tighten the bonds, then either from us after, or as a ransom}"
"33947","(33947) Waki’ told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Ibn Amir sent a captive to Ibn Omar. While he was in Persia, or he was forced to kill him, Ibn Umar said: As for him being wounded, no.\nWaki` said: It means trustworthy."
"33948","(33948) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man who did not name him; Omar bin Al-Khattab was brought captive to me and he freed them."
"33949","(33949) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Our companions narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The imam in the matter of captives has the choice, if If he wants, he can redeem himself, and if he wants, he can kill him. If he wants, he can kill him."
"33950","(33950) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali ordered a caller to call him, and he called out on the Day of Basra: No. A prisoner is killed."
"33951","(33951) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of the conquest of Mecca: No one who flees is killed, no one is attacked or executed, and whoever closes his door is safe. (Abu Ubaid 159)"
"33952","(33952) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father; Indeed, Ali ordered his herald, and he called out on the Day of Basra: “The one who flees from Basra shall not be followed, nor should the wounded be blasphemed, nor should he be killed.” A captive, and whoever closes his door is safe, and whoever lays down his weapon is safe, and nothing of their possessions will be taken."
"33953","(33953) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, he said: Maimun narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imamah, he said: I witnessed Siffin, they did not attack a wounded person, nor did they ask for a ally, nor did they rob a dead person."
"33954","(33954) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Al-Zubayr used to follow He was killed on the Day of Al-Yamamah, so if he saw a man with a bloodshot, he would look at him."
"33955","(33955) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Women used to treat the wounded on the day of Uhud."
"33956","(33956) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah said: The voluntary prayer is performed unless the two rows meet, or The two flanks, and if the two flanks or two rows meet, then the spoils."
"33957","(33957) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Al-Umays told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Masruq, he said: When he met The crawl, or the two rows, there is no voluntary offering, but rather the spoils, but the voluntary offering before and after."
"33958","(33958) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: Omar said: There is no voluntary redemption for the first part of the spoils. And there is no redemption after the spoils."
"33959","(33959) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was performing voluntary prayers before his obligatory five-fifth of spoils was given to him, so when the verse was revealed: {what Whatever you gain, then to Him belongs a fifth. God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bayhaqi 314, Ibn Zanjawi 1135)"
"33960","(33960) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Ata` bin al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdah; Verse: {They ask you about the Anfal} He said: Nothing strays from the polytheists from the enemy to the Muslims, whether a slave, or possessions, or It is an animal on which one can perform whatever he likes."
"33961","(33961) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Makhul, and Ikrimah; {They ask you about the Anfal. Say: The Anfal are for God and the Messenger.} They said: The Anfal were for God and His Messenger until I abrogated them. {And know. Whatever you take as spoils, a fifth of it belongs to Allah. (Tabari 1751, Ibn Jarir 176)"
"33962","(33962) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad; That a man asked Ibn Abbas about his saying: {They ask you about the Anfal}? He said: Robbery and horseback."
"33963","(33963) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; {They ask you about the Anfal} He said: What happened to the Sarayat?"
"33964","(33964) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Shihab, on the authority of his father, who said: I was the first to light a fire. In the chapter on covering up, he said: Al-Ash’ari was knocked down from his horse, and when we conquered it, he commanded me to lead ten of my people, and they gave us arrows. Equine arrows before the spoils."
"33965","(33965) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of my nephew Khalid bin Al-Walid; Al-Harith said to him: Give it to me, so he gave him a fifth of it before he divided it, so he thought about it and said: If you give it a fifth So give it to me."
"33966","(33966) Issa bin Yunus, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to us on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said: He is not given to anyone who Spoil is something that cannot be divided, except to a shepherd, a guard, or a driver who is not responsible for it."
"33967","(33967) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He sent something to Anas before the spoils were divided. He said: No, and I refuse until it is divided."
"33968","(33968) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ash‘ath, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: He does not perform voluntary prayer until five days."
"33969","(33969) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The voluntary prayer after the fifth prayer."
"33970","(33970) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: They would not carry out voluntary deeds except from The five"
"33971","(33971) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Anas bin Malik invaded with Ubaid. Allah bin Ziyad, he said: So he gave him thirty heads from the pre-Islamic captivity, he said: Anas asked him to make them from The fifth, but Anas refused to accept it."
"33972","(33972) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He was asked about plundering the spoils, if their prince gave them permission? He thought that"
"33973","(33973) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja`far narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi`, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He brings the spoils and divides them into five, so four are for those who witness them, and he takes The fifth, then he strikes it with his hand, and whatever he takes, he makes it for the Kaaba, and it is the arrow of God which he has named, then He divides what remains among five people, so it will be an share for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and an share for relatives. An arrow for the orphans, an arrow for the needy, an arrow for the wayfarer. (Abu Dawud 372. Tabari 10)"
"33974","(33974) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Salih bin Abi Al-Akhdar, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Hisham, on the authority of Malik bin Abd Allah Al-Khatha’ami said: We were sitting with Othman, and he said: Who is here among the people of the Levant? So I got up, and he said: Tell Muawiyah that when he takes your spoils, he must take five shares, and write on one of them: For God, then for him to knock, and wherever he comes out of it, for him to take."
"33975","(33975) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, he said: I asked Yahya bin Al-Jazzar About the shares of the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: One-fifth. (Nasa’i 4446; Abd al-Razzaq 9486)"
"33976","(33976) Jarir told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar; In a similar way (Abu Ubaid 34)"
"33977","(33977) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: He narrated to us like Hams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq al-Uqaili, saying: A man rose to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God, tell me about the spoils? He said: To God is an arrow, and to those who are four. He said: I said: Is anyone more worthy of it than anyone else? He said: He said: If I shoot an arrow in your side, I have no more right to it than your brother.\n(Tahawi 301, Bayhaqi 336)"
"33978","(33978) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; In his saying: {For to Allah belongs five}, he said: To Allah belongs all things."
"33979","(33979) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: One-fifth is for God, and one-fifth for the Messenger is one. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to place that fifth wherever he liked, and do with it whatever he wanted, and carry with it whomever I wish (Abu Ubaid 837)"
"33980","(33980) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; {And know that whatever thing you gain, that belongs to God by five.} He said: God’s arrow, and the Prophet’s arrow, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is one."
"33981","(33981) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ali, he said: I asked him about his saying: {And know that whatever thing you gain, a fifth of it belongs to Allah.} He said: This is the key to the speech. Allah has no share. Allah has no share. This world and the hereafter."
"33982","(33982) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: In the spoils; One-fifth is for God, and an arrow is for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet. Ibn Sirin said: The best head of captivity is taken for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then the fifth is taken out, then He is struck by his arrow with people whether he is absent or present.\n Ibn Sirin said: Al-Safi was Safiyya bint Huyayy on the day of Khaybar.\n Al-Shu’bi said: On the day of Khaybar, Safiyyah was the daughter of Huyya, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her.\n(Abu Dawud 2985, Saeed bin Mansour 2679)"
"33983","(33983) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: One-fifth of God, and the share of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace and blessings of God be upon him and Al-Saffi. He used to select for him from the spoils better than a head of captivity, if he was a captive, otherwise something else. After the five, then he will be struck with his arrow by Shahad, or he went away with the Muslims after Safiyyah. He said: And he chose Safiyyah’s daughter. Live on the Day of Khaybara.\n Ash'ath said: Abu Al-Zinad, Amr bin Dinar, and Al-Zuhri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, chose that sword. Poverty on the day of Badr. (Tirmidhi 1561, Hakim 128)"
"33984","(33984) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, who said: Al-Safi was on the day of Badr, Saif Al-Aas bin Munabbih bin Al-Hajjaj"
"33985","(33985) Muhammad bin Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He was asked about the arrow of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Al-Safi? He said: The arrow of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was only like the arrow of a Muslim man, and as for Al-Saffi, it had a gray mark. He chooses her from his Muslim spoils, if he wants a female slave, and if he wants a horse, that is what he wants.\n(Abu Dawud 2984, An-Nasa’i 4447)"
"33986","(33986) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, who said: I asked Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib about the saying of God: {And know that you have taken spoils of Anything, for Allah has five. And on the authority of this verse: {What has Allah given to His Messenger}? He said: I said: What is the fay? What is the spoils? He said: If the Muslims conquered the polytheists and their land, and they took them by force, then whatever wealth they conquered was taken. It is spoils, and as for the earth, it is spoils, and this black of ours is spoils."
"33987","(33987) Waki` narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan saying: The spoils that befall the Muslims by force belong to those whom he named. God, and four-fifths to the one who bears witness."
"33988","(33988) Ismail bin Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I read the book of the mention of al-Safi, and I said to Muhammad: What Al-Safi? He said: A head that was chosen for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, before everything else, and then his arrows would be multiplied for him afterward. People (Abu Dawud 2985)"
"33989","(33989) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; {And know that you have taken spoils of something.} He said: the sewn piece of something."
"33990","(33990) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The fifth is in the same place as the fai’, It is given to the imam, whether rich or poor.\n He said: Laith bin Abi Ruqayyah told me that Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: The path of the fifth is the path of the common people. The category."
"33991","(33991) Kathir bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, he said: Thabit bin Al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: I was informed that Two men from Banu Abdul Muttalib came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about charity, and he said: No, but if You saw something of the five with me and came to me."
"33992","(33992) Waki` narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: The family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: It is not lawful for them to give in charity, so he made one-fifth for them. (Nasa’i 4449. Tabari 10)"
"33993","(33993) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Omar gave the man ten thousand, ninety, eighty, and seventy thousand from the Fay."
"33994","(33994) Affan told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Arta told us, he said: Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: He was asked: How did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do with the five? He said: He used to carry some of his sperm for the sake of God. A man, then a man, then a man. (Ahmed 365)"
"33995","(33995) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, he said: Sayyar told us, he said: Yazid al-Faqir told us, he said: Jabir told us Bin Abdullah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The spoils are permissible for me, but they were not permissible for anyone before me."
"33996","(33996) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The spoils were not permissible for a black-headed people before you. Fire used to come down from the sky and consume it, so when On the day of Badr, the people hastened to seize the spoils, so God revealed: {If it had not been for a Book from God, a great punishment would have touched you while you took. So eat of what you have gained, lawful and good. (Tirmidhi 3085. Ahmad 252)"
"33997","(33997) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid and Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The spoils were made lawful for me, but they were not made lawful for anyone before me."
"33998","(33998) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The spoils were permissible for me, but they were not permissible for a prophet before me."
"33999","(33999) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid - Ghayir Waki’ added to it - on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, On the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The spoils were permissible for me, but they were not permissible for a prophet who was before him."
"34000","(34000) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, On the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: The spoils were permissible for me, but they were not permissible for a prophet before me."
"34001","(34001) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, he said: Al-Qasim and Makhul narrated to us, on the authority of Abu In front of him; On the Day of Khaybar, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade arrows to be sold until they are divided. (Tabarani 7774)"
"34002","(34002) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is nothing wrong with a man selling his share of the spoils before it is divided."
"34003","(34003) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Marzuq, Mawla Tajib, said: We invaded with Rufa’ bin Thabit Al-Ansari towards the West, so we conquered a village called Laha. He tried it, and he stood up and preached to us and said: I will not tell you anything except what I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying about us. On the Day of Khaybar: Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not sell spoils of war until he divides it with them."
"34004","(34004) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jadham bin Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid On the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade buying The spoils until they are divided. (Abu Ali 1088)"
"34005","(34005) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling the spoils until they are divided. (Abdul Razzaq 9489)"
"34006","(34006) Abd bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He used to hate buying something from the spoils, and he said: It contains gold and silver, meaning before... He swears"
"34007","(34007) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad bin Sirin; They both disliked selling the spoils until they were divided."
"34008","(34008) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He forbade the day of news on the authority of"
"34009","(34009) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who raised it to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He forbade selling spoils until they are divided. (Nasa’i 6241, Abu Ali 2410)"
"34010","(34010) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumir, on the authority of a servant of Quraysh, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah narrated to Muawiyah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling the spoils until they are divided. Shu`ba said another time: And you know what it is. (Abu Dawud 3362 and Ahmad 387)"
"34011","(34011) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Usayd bin Abdul Rahman Al Khathami, on the authority of Muqbil bin Abdullah, on the authority of Hani bin Kulthum Al-Kinani said: I was the owner of the army that conquered the Levant, so I wrote to Omar: We have conquered a land. There is an abundance of food and fodder, and I was reluctant to approach any of that unless by your command and permission, so write to me. By your command regarding that, so Omar wrote to me: Let the people eat and feed. Whoever sells anything for gold or silver... It is obligatory to pay the fifth of God and the share of the Muslims."
"34012","(34012) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Usayd bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Khaled bin Durak, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhayriz, he said: Fadalah bin Ubaid, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about selling food and fodder on land. Rum? Then His Eminence said: Some people want to make me abandon my religion, and by God, I hope that this will not happen. Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever sells food for gold or silver, one-fifth of God’s money is due on it. Muslims"
"34013","(34013) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Ad-Darik, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, on the authority of his virtue Ibn Ubaid Al-Ansari said: Some people want to make me abandon my religion, but by God, I hope to die. And I am upon him. Whatever is sold for gold or silver, one-fifth of Allah’s reward and the honor of the Muslims is for it."
"34014","(34014) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace They eat of the spoils when they get them, including the lambs and cows, and they feed their animals, but they do not sell them. Sell your return to Maqasim."
"34015","(34015) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, he said: I heard him say: A sack of fat was given to me on the Day of Khaybar. He said: So I stuck to it and said: This is for me, I will not give it to anyone. Something, then I turned around and saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiling, so I felt ashamed. (Bukhari 3153, Muslim 1393)"
"34016","(34016) Jarir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: We used to raid and receive food, fruits, honey, and fodder. So he is a share of it other than his share."
"34017","(34017) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to eat food in the land of The war, and they isolate themselves before the Khums."
"34018","(34018) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, when they conquered the city or the palace, they ate of wheat, flour, ghee, and honey."
"34019","(34019) Abd al-Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’; The people are raiders, and they are in secret, and they attack almost all of the ghee, honey, and food? He said: They will eat, and whatever remains, return it to their imam."
"34020","(34020) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to make concessions in food. And fodder, unless they need money."
"34021","(34021) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Ja`far al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, on the authority of a boy To Salman, his name is Suwayd, and he praised him kindly, saying: When the people conquered the cities and went out in pursuit of the enemy, I was injured. He asked him, and Salman said to me: Do you have any food? He said: I said: Ask him what I got. He said: Give him. If it is money, we will give it to those people, and if it is food, we will eat it."
"34022","(34022) Waki’ told us, he said: Uqba told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Buraida; He was asked about food that is obtained in enemy territory? He said: If he sold some of it for a dirham, he would return it, otherwise he was deceitful."
"34023","(34023) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhayriz , Khaled bin Al-Duraik, and others; They used to say about a man who acquires food and fodder in the land of the Romans, so they said: He eats, feeds, and fodders, so if he sells He returned any of that with gold and silver as spoils of the Muslims."
"34024","(34024) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no harm in food and fodder found in Enemy land, that they may eat from it, and feed their animals, so whatever is sold from it is among the Muslims."
"34025","(34025) Aidh bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: When the expedition went out, they captured spoils. Of cows or sheep, they may eat according to what they measure, and not be extravagant. When they are brought to the army, it will be Between them."
"34026","(34026) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We were Fruits and honey are a share in our raids, so we eat them and do not take them away. (Bukhari 3154, Bayhaqi 59)"
"34027","(34027) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, who said: There is not a fifth in food, rather the fifth is in gold and silver."
"34028","(34028) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I said to Al-Hasan: We will receive honey, ghee, and cheese in the enemy’s lands. Shall we quintuple? He said: We have been its share, so we will eat it."
"34029","(34029) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Sa’d, a sheikh from the people of Wasit. Abdullah bin Abbas did not see anything wrong with a man eating food in the land of polytheism, until its people entered."
"34030","(34030) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Abi Al-Hasan, and Abi Ishaq, that they said in The people take the spoils: they eat, but they do not carry them."
"34031","(34031) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Khalid ibn Abi Imran, he said: I asked Al-Qasim, and Salim About the man who acquires food in enemy land, collects it from it, and earns dirhams from it? They said: He puts it in food that he eats, but he does not gain any money from it."
"34032","(34032) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Raja’ ibn Hiyawah; That Abu Ubaidah wrote to Omar ibn al-Khattab about a slave who had been captured by the polytheists, and then the Muslims defeated him after That? He said: His companion has more right to it as long as he does not divide it, so if he divides his right goes away."
"34033","(34033) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Raja’ ibn Hiyaw, on the authority of Qabisah ibn Dhu’ayb, who said: Omar said: The polytheists had not gained any of the Muslims’ wealth, so they invaded them after they had defeated them, and a man was found. What he owned in his own right before the arrows were divided, then he has more right to it, and if it was divided then he has nothing to do with it."
"34034","(34034) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, he said: Ali said: It is for the Muslims in general, because it They had money."
"34035","(34035) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father; That Ali used to say regarding the enemy’s possession of the Muslims’ wealth, it is in the same position as their wealth. He said: And Al-Hasan was He decrees that."
"34036","(34036) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Zuhara bin Yazid Al-Muradi; The mother of a Muslim man stayed behind and joined the enemy, so the Muslims took her as spoils, then her family recognized her, and it was written about her. Abu Ubaidah to Omar, so Omar wrote: If the mother-in-law has not been given a fifth and has not been divided, then it will be returned to her family, even if she is It was divided and divided, so he went on his way."
"34037","(34037) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; One of his servants remained, and he went to him with a horse, and he entered the enemy’s land, and Khalid bin Al-Walid attacked him, and he returned one of them. Ali during the lifetime of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the other was returned after the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 3069)"
"34038","(34038) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salman bin Rabi’ah; As for what the enemy had achieved, he said: His companion has more right to it as long as it is not divided, so if it is divided then nothing matters."
"34039","(34039) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of his father, or on the authority of his uncle, who said: He lost a horse to me and the enemy took it. He said: So the Muslims prevailed over him. He said: I found him in Saad’s stall. He said: So I said: My horse. He said: So he said: I have shown you. I said: I I call upon him and he praises you. He said: If he answers you, then I do not want any clear proof from you."
"34040","(34040) Ismail bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; My mother was seized by the enemy, and a man bought her. Her master disputed with him to Sharih, and he said: The Muslim is more deserving of the one who responded to him. He gave her the price to his brother, and he said: She was born to her master. He said: He freed her, by the judge of the prince, if she was such and such, and if It was such and such. He said: A man says: He is more knowledgeable about the judiciary than Zaid bin Khalda."
"34041","(34041) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The enemy has not achieved anything from The wealth of Muslims is known to its owner, so he has more right to it, and if it is divided, then it goes away."
"34042","(34042) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The enemy has not befallen the Muslims before. Therefore, if its owner gets it before it is divided, then he has more right to it, and if it is divided, then he has more right to the price."
"34043","(34043) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali, who said: He did not achieve The enemy is permissible."
"34044","(34044) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The polytheists did not prevail against him. Of the Muslims’ possessions, then the Muslims prevailed upon him. If it was divided, he was more entitled to the price, and if it was not divided, he would return it. Aliyah"
"34045","(34045) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfi, who said: The Muslims killed a camel. For a man from among the Muslims, then a man from the enemy bought it, so its owner disputed with it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he established clear evidence, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that the price for which he bought it from the enemy should be paid to him, otherwise he will be abandoned. Between him and us. (Abu Dawud 339. Al-Bayhaqi 111)"
"34046","(34046) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: It is not permissible for a Muslim to attack an enemy. The Muslims are food, and there is no weapon with which to strengthen them against the Muslims, so whoever does that is a sinner."
"34047","(34047) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He hated carrying weapons against the enemy. He said: I told him: Should horses be carried against them? He said: He refused that, and said: As for what strengthens them for fighting, then no, and as for anything else, there is no problem.\n And Amr bin Dinar said it."
"34048","(34048) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Umar bin Abdulaziz forbade the horses from being taken to land. India"
"34049","(34049) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated carrying weapons or horses to the enemy's land for trade."
"34050","(34050) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Ibrahim; It was disliked to carry a weapon or property to the enemy of the Muslims."
"34051","(34051) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They both disliked selling weapons in the event of strife."
"34052","(34052) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Abu Hayyan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They both disliked selling weapons in the event of strife."
"34053","(34053) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He will not be sent to the people of war. Anything of weapons and horses, nor anything used for use on weapons and horses."
"34054","(34054) Shazan narrated to us, he said: Aban Al-Attar narrated to us, on the authority of his commanders, he said: It was disliked to sell weapons in combat."
"34055","(34055) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, who said: The companions of Abdullah were raiding at the time of Al-Hajjaj: Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, Abu Sinan, and Abu Juhaif."
"34056","(34056) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: I heard them mentioning: that Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd used to invade The Kharijites in the time of al-Hajjaj, he would fight them."
"34057","(34057) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He conquered Al-Rayy during the time of Al-Hajjaj."
"34058","(34058) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muthanna bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Jamra, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the invasion with The princes have done so? He said: You fight for your share of the Hereafter, and they fight for their share of this world."
"34059","(34059) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d Abi Uthman, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Yashkuri, on the authority of Jabir said: I said to him: Should I attack the misguided people with the Sultan? He said: Fight, for upon you is what you have been burdened with, and upon them is what they have been burdened with."
"34060","(34060) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Al-Fazari, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They were asked about fighting with bad leaders? They said: Your honor, your reward, and your grace, and their sin is upon them."
"34061","(34061) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Yazid. Al-Nakha’i said: I said to my father: O my father, in the emirate of al-Hajjaj, are you going to fight? He said: O my son, I have come across people who hate pilgrims more than you, and they do not abandon jihad under any circumstances, even if it is... People's opinion regarding jihad is the same as your opinion regarding the payment of royalties, meaning the tax."
"34062","(34062) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was mentioned to him that a people They say: There is no jihad, so he said: This is something that Satan proposed to him."
"34063","(34063) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Rabi’ bin Subaih told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I asked Ibn Umar About the invasion with the imams of injustice, which they committed? He said: Conquer."
"34064","(34064) Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Laith, who said: A mujahid was fighting with the Banu Marwan. He was a giver who saw no harm in it."
"34065","(34065) Abu Bakr narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: A mission came out against the people in the time of Al-Hajjaj, so he went out In it is Abdul Rahman bin Yazid."
"34066","(34066) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: He used to hate jihad with These, meaning the unjust ruler."
"34067","(34067) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, who said: A mission came out against the people in the time of Al-Hajjaj, so he went out there. Ibrahim Al-Taymi and Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i. Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i said: To whom are you inviting? To the pilgrims?"
"34068","(34068) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Muslim A man believed in a group of people while he was with Amr ibn al-Aas, Khalid ibn al-Walid, and Abi Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah. Amr said, And Khaled: We do not protect those who do so. Abu Ubaidah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: He will reward me. Muslims each other."
